"Because this brutal regime treated such people, our elites and patriots formed a front on December 2 in Kratie province and completely liberated the country from the Khmer Rouge regime on January 7, 1979. "
Mr. Pok Panh told the younger generation to remember these two historical days, because there is only December 2, there is January 7, there is January 7, then all Cambodians are resurrected and everything is the same. In addition, as the next generation, at all costs, we must work together to maintain and absolutely protect the peace that is the foundation for the development of the country and the peaceful living of the people.
(Siem Reap): At least 28 young and old people in two communes in Puok district, Siem Reap province, were poisoned by salted fish that they bought from the market for cooking. Affect the life expectancy. He was immediately taken to a private health center and clinic for treatment.
According to the local police, the case of the saltwater fish poisoning occurred at around 4:20 pm on December 2, 2019, when the victims were between 5 and 68 years old. The communes in Puok district are Puok commune and Khnat commune.
According to the story, the authorities confirmed that after the people bought salted fish to cook with rice and after eating salted fish, there were symptoms of poisoning, nausea and sent to the Provincial Referral Hospital. Siem Reap, Referral Hospital, Teuk Vil Health Center, Scale Health Center, at a private clinic and some patients were treated at their home.
