Chrey Thom border area will change its face and become the heart of Kandal province
(Kandal): Mr. Ney Chary, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, said that the Chrey Thom border area will change its face and become the heart of Kandal province and there will be real progress in the future.
He said this at a workshop on Dissemination of Land Use Master Plan in Chrey Thom Town, Sampov Poun Commune, Koh Thom District for Sustainable Development and Conservation on December 3, 2019 at Provincial Hall. Central.
"In the future, Chrey Thom will become a standard town by identifying suitable land use areas such as residential areas, agriculture, industry, trade, tourism, administration and infrastructure projects that make it better," he said. "Let the Chrey Thom border area change its face and become the heart of Kandal province and make real progress in the future."
The Deputy Governor added that in order for the implementation of this land use master plan to be successful, he requested the authorities at all levels, all units in the province and all stakeholders to request the construction or development of infrastructure at the local level must follow the master plan. Which has already been approved and prevented in time in case of unauthorized construction.
In this workshop, Mr. Mean Chanvanny, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, said that the master plan of Chrey Thom town, Sampov Poun commune, Koh Thom district, Kandal province has been officially implemented by Resolution 005 Pillar. Dated this 24th day of December, 2018.
He said that proper land management and urban planning have contributed to ensuring sustainable development, conservation, balance and equity, and also contributed significantly to the economic growth of Cambodia around 7% per year through the growth of Development and construction every year.
This result also reflects the efforts of the Ministry of Land Management, provinces and authorities at all levels in the implementation of the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 6th legislature of the National Assembly for the growth of employment, equity and efficiency in Cambodia to achieve. Become a high-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2050.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, in this morning's meeting, Samdech Techo described the development in the difficult situation of Phnom Penh after the liberation from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Samdech Techo stated that Phnom Penh was built during the French colonial period and also built after Cambodia gained independence during the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era of King Norodom Sihanouk. But Phnom Penh was devastated and destroyed by the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Samdech Techo reminded that after the fall of Pol Pot regime, Samdech returned to Phnom Penh, there were only 70 people in Phnom Penh and the whole capital did not have many challenges, that is, there were no people living and no car traffic. Driving. But now, after the country was liberated from the genocidal regime for almost 41 years, Phnom Penh has developed and developed greatly.
The Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, informed the French-speaking mayor that the current development and progress of Phnom Penh leads to a number of challenges that need to be addressed. Samdech Techo stated that Phnom Penh currently faces traffic problems and traffic accidents that lead to the death of many people and travel is slow.
Lack of public parking is also a challenge for Phnom Penh. Samdech Techo Hun Sen informed the delegates that he had instructed the Capital Governor to encourage investment in the construction of parking lots under parks to solve this problem.
In addition to traffic and parking problems, the problem of garbage and dirty water is also a challenge for Phnom Penh today. The Prime Minister informed the French-speaking mayor that Phnom Penh has about 3,000 tons of garbage per day, and if not collected, the garbage will pile up, causing problems for the beauty and hygiene in Phnom Penh.
Regarding the issue of garbage, Samdech Techo said that Samdech has encouraged the participation of various sectors as well as the private sector in order to convert this waste into electricity for reuse.
Regarding the issue of liquid waste, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Phnom Penh is a city with a low altitude and originally was a lake, so the discharge of liquid waste to the river to the lake has not been treated or Filter tank properly yet.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister said that these issues should be considered before solving the development of new cities. Samdech Techo said that these challenges are caused by the most advanced development, and this development comes from the peace and stability that Cambodia has.
During this morning's courtesy call, Christian Roosevelt, representing the entire delegation, said that although they have not yet visited Phnom Penh, all the mayors have observed Assessed that Phnom Penh is an old city and also durable and beautiful.
Mr. Christian Roche Ogemba said that he and the entire delegation will make efforts to take the experience from Phnom Penh to practice in their respective countries. Japan Mine Action Organization (JMAS) donates 3 bulldozers to Battambang Provincial Administration for free plowing
The second meeting was held at Battambang Provincial Hall in the presence of Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Provincial Governor, relevant district governors, specialized departments and relevant provincial hall officials.
He stated that his project was planned to be done in 5 provinces in Cambodia, but he chose Battambang as a potential province to try first, providing 3 machines for plowing and clearing farmers' land evenly to receive Get more output in the future.
The provincial governor would like to support and accept the support to help create conditions for the Japanese side to make this process successful and thank Japan for always helping Cambodia, especially in Battambang province.
