Cambodian diplomat receives visiting Secretary-General of the International Organization of Francophonie
Ms. Lewis Musiki Wabo led a delegation to pay a four-day visit to Cambodia from December 2 to 5, 2019 at the invitation of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. This is her first official visit to strengthen relations between Cambodia and the OIF since she took office on January 3, 2019. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia.
According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the official visit coincides with the General Assembly of the French-speaking Mayors (AIMF) in Phnom Penh, an important Francophone event hosted by Cambodia, which she will also attend. .
During her official visit to Phnom Penh, the Secretary-General will pay a courtesy call on His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, and pay a courtesy call on Samdech Techo Hun Sen. She will also meet with Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia.
During the visit, Ms. Lewis Musikivabo will also visit Siem Reap. The Secretary General will be welcomed by the Governor of Siem Reap, Mr. Tea Seiha and visit the towers of Angkor. She will also attend a regional workshop on research activities organized by the Francophone Asia-Pacific Regional Center (CREFAP) and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, and visit bilingual classes at Wat Bo Primary School.
