Siem Reap Provincial Hall: The final balance of the Chan school collapse incident has 16 victims / 3 dead
(Siem Reap): The rescue operation for the victims of the collapse of the construction of the Sala Chan building at Wat Prasat Kork Chak in Veal village, Sangkat Kork Chak, Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province, has already rescued the victims from the pile. The final toll was 16, with three seriously injured, 10 slightly injured and three dead, according to the school. Siem Reap Province.
A statement from Siem Reap Provincial Hall confirmed that as of 7 pm on December 2, 2019, the rescue force had found a total of 16 victims, including two monks.
Three people were seriously injured (2 builders and 1 guardian), 10 people were slightly injured (2 monks, 1 security guard and 7 construction workers). All the victims are being treated at the provincial referral hospital. Separately, three victims died.
According to the mechanics and the security forces who stood and witnessed the incident, there were no more victims under the pile. However, the rescue team, led by Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap and Chairman of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command, continued to excavate the piles at night, adding strength until the piles were completely removed.
According to the report, a total of 750 people, including the armed forces, monks, people and the people, took part in the rescue operation. Nine ambulances, including two military units, three units of the 4th Zone and 4 units of the Provincial Referral Hospital.
Rescue equipment includes 4 cranes (1 Department of Public Works and Transport, 1 unit of electricity and 2 units of APSARA Authority), 3 excavators (2 units of Provincial Administration and 1 Department of Public Works and Transport), 1 electric vehicle ( Provincial Electricity Unit) 1 unit and arrange lighting for night operation as well.
