Families of traffic accident victims insist on justice after perpetrator released while injured injured lying on mats
(Kampong Chhnang): The families of three victims in a traffic accident caused by the owner of a blue Hyundai Atos car with license plate number 2A-4881 hit from behind, leaving his son, daughter-in-law and nephew unconscious and lying on the floor. The way to escape while the patient is still lying on the mat waiting to be sent to Vietnam for treatment.
According to Sok Sophoan, a resident of Koki Village, Koki Commune, Kien Svay District, Kandal Province, her mother asked the authorities to seek justice after the Court of Appeal released the perpetrator, Yus Sophal, 29, of Trapeang Thom Village, Pong Ro Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province. .
The request comes as one of his three daughters suffered a broken cervical vertebra, paralyzed, lying on a mat until now, due to a car accident on September 1, 2019 at more than 8 pm. In the 8th village, Sangkat Khsam, Kampong Chhnang city, Kampong Chhnang province, because the perpetrator was drunk, he drove the car and hit from behind.
Sok Sophoan described that on the night of September 1, her three children and nephews were riding a motorcycle together on National Road 5. When they arrived at the scene, a blue Hyundai Autos car with license plate number 2A-4891 crashed into the back, leaving their children and nephews lying unconscious on the road.
The woman said that at that time, the car ran away on the dirt road, and the people chased after it. Both drunk. After the villagers arrested the driver, the police arrived to bring the perpetrator to the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police.
On the other hand, the thing that made him even more upset was that the traffic police of Kampong Chhnang province did not check the alcohol of the perpetrator, answering that there was no machine to check and did not measure immediately at the scene until the next day, September 2. The same year, at 12 noon, he went down to take measurements. Not only that, the traffic police made a report to the court and seemed to intend to acquit the perpetrator.
At this point, a woman named Sok Sophoan confirmed that there were up to three victims, one was a nephew and the other two were children and son-in-law.
The three victims are: Som Sophors, his daughter, who was seriously injured and broke her cervix, unable to walk until now, Phorn Chetra, her son-in-law, and Nuon Sopoeun. Both nephews suffered head injuries. However, the traffic police made a report and sent it to the court, named Nuon Sophoeun alone and changed his gender. In addition, the traffic police accused the victim of riding a motorcycle to escape (hollow) before entering his car.
