Cambodia and Thailand have agreed that in early 2020, they will begin construction of a shelter in Poipet to rescue and provide services to victims and victims of human trafficking at a cost of approximately $ 1 million. The United States, a grant from the Royal Government of Thailand for a friendly relationship between Cambodia and Thailand.
It should be noted that Mr. Nhek Vannara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs and other professional officials left Cambodia on December 1, 2019 for a five-day visit to Thailand to discuss with the Thai side on the management and construction of the center. The first stop center in Poipet.
