China is now retaliating against the United States over its incursion into Hong Kong (Video inside) (Beijing): Beijing has gradually retaliated by announcing sanctions on a number of US NGOs. The United States has also suspended permits for US warships and aircraft to visit Hong Kong. This was released by Bloomberg on Monday afternoon, December 2, 2019.
The announcement was made by the Chinese Foreign Ministry at a brief press conference on Monday, just days after warning of retaliation against US President Donald Trump's signing last week. To make Hong Kong's draft law on democracy and human rights official.
The US law aims to support protesters in Hong Kong and to review once a year whether Hong Kong is eligible for special trade preferences from the United States. It also allows for sanctions in the event of serious human rights abuses that the United States sees happening in Hong Kong.
Among the US NGOs that will be sanctioned for supporting Hong Kong protesters is Human Rights Watch, and the Chinese Foreign Ministry has called on Washington to stop. China's intrusion into internal affairs with further warnings that further action will be taken if necessary.
