Angela Khok Korin made the remarks during her farewell visit to Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen this morning, December 2, 2019 at the Peace Palace.
According to Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal aide, during this morning's meeting, outgoing Ambassador Angela Cochrane recalled that she had visited Cambodia during 1993 and 1994, when That Phnom Penh is a deserted area.
But Phnom Penh today in her eyes is a beautiful city with unexpected development. This is what Angela Cochrane said, and was quoted by Eang Sophalleth.
In addition to praising Cambodia's progress, Angela Cochrane also expressed her happiness that Australia has become a country that has contributed to the development of Cambodia as it is today.
The outgoing Ambassador to Cambodia also affirmed that Australia, as well as the Australian Government, is ready to help strengthen Cambodia's trade and economy. Australia is also ready to boost cooperation in various fields, especially between the youth of the two countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Ms. Angela Cochrane for her significant contribution to the development of Cambodia-Australia relations and cooperation. In particular, she pushed for summits in Australia, exchanges of youth visits, and boosted the import of more than 97 per cent of goods from Cambodia to Australia.
Samdech Techo said that through good relations, this is a good basis to further enhance relations between the two countries through trade and investment.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked Australia for always helping Cambodia. Such as helping to establish an agricultural research institute.
It should be noted that in this farewell meeting in Cambodia this morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also presented a medal to Ms. Angela Kok Korin to thank her for helping Cambodia.
