AIDS Health Care Foundation Organizes World AIDS Day December 1, 2019
(Phnom Penh): The AIDS Health Care Foundation (AHF), together with the Government of Cambodia and civil society organizations, organized a celebration of World AIDS Day on December 1, 2019 in the evening of December 1, 2019 at the Center. Phnom Penh's Koh Pich Expo once again calls on leaders around the world to "keep their promises" to people affected by HIV and AIDS.
According to the latest UNAIDS statistics, 37.9 million people around the world are living with HIV and AIDS, and by 2018, about 1.7 million people will be infected with the new HIV and 770,000. People have died of various diseases related to AIDS. Today, while millions are being treated with antiretroviral drugs, millions more are in urgent need of help.
Please be informed that according to the best recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that the theme for the World AIDS Day December 1, 2019 is "Join together as a national movement in "Preventing the spread of HIV and AIDS."
The AIDS Health Care Foundation (AHF) is the largest HIV / AIDS organization in the world, currently providing treatment, care and services to more than 1.3 million people in 43 countries. Worldwide, such as the United States, Africa, Latin America, the Caribbean, Asia-Pacific and Eastern Europe.
