December 2, 1978 was the day when many patriotic Cambodian dignitaries, led by Samdech Heng Samrin, Samdech Chea Sim and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, backed by Vietnamese troops gathered in Snuol district, Kratie province, to protest. Overthrow of the Democratic Kampuchea Killing Fields regime of the Pol Pot genocidal brothel.
On December 2, 1978, the "United Front for the National Salvation of Cambodia", now renamed the "United Front for the Development of the Motherland of Cambodia", a leading mass organization of the Cambodian People's Party, was established in the liberated area of Cheung Khlou commune. 2 December, Snoul district, Kratie province.
In response to the call of the People's Front everywhere, they stood united as a force of national unity, with the support of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army and the support of close friends around the world to overthrow the Democratic Kampuchea regime. Achieved a glorious victory on January 7, 1979.
