Also this November, $ 386,520 was donated to the Kantha Bopha Foundation to support the operation of Kantha Bopha Hospital to save lives and treat Cambodian children, and the total amount of 11 months is 3,994,534. Dollars for the Kantha Bopha Hospital Foundation of Cambodia. Understand the law: the mission of judicial police officers
(Phnom Penh): Police refers to the guardians of the kingdom who have important roles and responsibilities in protecting and maintaining public order, security, safety and security for the people.
When a crime occurs, citizens can file a complaint to the nearest police officer who qualifies as a judicial police officer.
To better understand the mission of Judicial Police officers in contributing to the provision of justice services to the people, the FRESH NEWS Legal Awareness Program in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation would like to raise the topic of "Mission". Judicial police officers "came to present to the people, students as follows:
The judiciary police includes judicial police officers, judicial police officers, and other civil servants and public agencies whose law specifically authorizes them to investigate certain crimes within their jurisdiction.
For this week, our program would like to highlight only the mission of judicial police officers as provided in Articles 71-75 of the Code of Criminal Procedure as follows:
Judicial police officers receive complaints and defamation complaints. Judicial police officers are responsible for investigating crimes and investigating actual crimes and conducting preliminary investigations in accordance with the law.
Once the investigation has begun, the Judicial Police Officer shall implement the Order of Investigation on behalf of the Investigating Judge within the conditions stipulated in Article 173 (Subpoena) to Article 184 (Minutes created by the Judicial Police Officer). Of this Code.
All complaints received by judicial police officers require a recorder. The minutes must accurately cite the complainant's report. If necessary, the judicial police officer may call for an interpreter who is sworn in by his or her religion or belief and will interpret the language correctly according to the report. In any case, translators may not be recruited among the joint police or military police.
The minutes of filing the complaint shall be as follows:
* Name and status of the judicial police officer * The unit of the judicial police officer * Date.
Each page must be signed by a judicial police officer and a complainant. Extras and references must be confirmed by the signatures of the judicial police officer and the complainant at the margins. Before signing or fingerprinting, the plaintiff must re-read the minutes. If necessary, the judicial police officer shall read the contents of the log aloud.
In every Judicial Police Unit, there must be a list of complaints and at all times, when a complaint is filed, the Judicial Police Officer must register in the following list:
* Identity of the plaintiff * Date of filing the complaint * Name and status of the judicial police officer who made the record on the filing of the complaint * Type of action filed * Action on the complaint, such as referral to the prosecutor or initiation of an investigation .
The list of complaints must be permanently held for the court authorities as required. The judicial police officer who receives the complaint must immediately start an investigation or send a record of the complaint to the prosecutor for further action.
Judicial police officers prior to an investigation may seek guidance from the prosecutor. Upon receipt of a defamation complaint stating a clear and reasonable reason, the judicial police officer shall inform the prosecutor and seek guidance.
In any case, the judicial police officer can not leave any criminal case unattended, even after mediation between the perpetrator and the victim or the withdrawal of the complaint.
Judicial police officers who inadvertently keep records or exhibits or conceal from the court authorities the existence of records or exhibits shall be deemed to have committed the offenses punishable under the Penal Code in relation to the chapter on the search for evidence.
In the above case, the criminal offense cannot be eliminated by mediation between the perpetrator and the victim or due to the withdrawal of the complaint, the judicial police officer can not keep the case unmanaged.
In conclusion, judicial police officers have an important mission to receive complaints and defamation complaints in order to investigate the actual crime, conduct a preliminary investigation and arrest the perpetrators, as well as collect evidence and send it to the prosecution for legal proceedings.
