Mine Authority presents results of 4th Ottawa Review Conference in Oslo, Norway
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Authority for Mine Action and Mine Action Disaster Management on November 30, 2019 issued an official press release on the results of the 4th review conference of the States Parties to the Ottawa Convention. Held in Oslo, Norway from 25 to 29 November 2019.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Mines Authority, has assigned Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mines Authority, to attend the 4th Review Conference of the States Parties on the Prohibition on the Use, Storage, Production and Production of Minerals. Anti-personnel landmine transfer and demining (Ottawa permit).
Please be informed that the Review Conference is an official meeting of the 164 States Parties to the Ottawa Convention, which is held every five years. This Convention was adopted on September 18, 1997 and entered into force on March 1, 1999.
The review conference is an opportunity for the international community to review the progress of the implementation of the treaty since the Third Review Conference in 2014, by compiling practical reports to meet the principles of the treaty and urging both parties Achieve the ambition of the mine threat by 2025.
