Message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, Outstanding National Elite of the Asia-Pacific Leadership Forum on Response to HIV / AIDS in Cambodia 2019 under the theme "Together to join a national movement to prevent the spread of HIV and AIDS."
In addition, HIV testing rates among pregnant women have risen, the rate of transmission from HIV-infected mothers to their children has decreased, and the HIV / AIDS-discriminatory index has declined. Strong should be proud.
On this occasion, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen recommended six points for the fight to prevent the spread of HIV and AIDS in Cambodia:
1: The Cambodian Red Cross Youth Volunteer Branch would like to strengthen and expand educational activities to raise awareness of HIV / AIDS in rural communities and to provide support and protection to people living with HIV / AIDS.
2: For those who suspect that they are at risk of HIV infection, please hurry to get a blood test for HIV and to receive care services from health centers regularly and absolutely avoid not transmitting to others and participate in co-education. Extensive.
3: For pregnant women to go for regular health check-ups and especially early blood tests to receive services to prevent HIV transmission to the baby and encourage partners to check and receive treatment together.
4: Please all compatriots must continue to understand the prevention of HIV and protect themselves from HIV infection, especially young men and women must be careful and remember that protection is starting from yourself.
5. Absolutely do not stigmatize and discriminate against people living with HIV and AIDS, and create a supportive environment for high-risk groups everywhere to access health services, social services and legal protections.
6: People living with HIV should not be ashamed and discriminate against themselves and must hurry to get counseling and treatment in a timely manner.
Through this message, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen strongly hopes that all compatriots really understand and continue to spread to family members, friends and community more widely.
