(Phnom Penh): On November 29, 2019, Mr. Aing Serey Piseth, Deputy Governor of Chamkar Mon District, led a professional officer to inspect the houses of people affected by a Chinese construction site. Their daily lives in Village 12, Street 93, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
The inspection and problem solving for the above people came after the construction company "China Construction" was sued by them, which acted to affect daily life and cause damage to people's property.
* First: The tile roof collapsed on the bathroom roof of the old house * Second: After discussing with the construction company to study the collapse or crack, the company representative agreed to find a team of professional engineers or company Techniques to study the collapse of carpets, roofs, tiles or cracks * Third: Chamkarmon district administration is studying to find solutions and reconciliation.
During the inspection, the people requested the Chamkar Mon District Authority 3 points:
* First: Request the company to stop cutting metal that causes odors affecting their health * Second: Stop pouring cement on their house * Third: Please stop construction at 10 pm so as not to Disturbing the hiding place of the people.
In connection with the request of the above people, Mr. Aing Serey Piseth accepted to tell the company to stop immediately. According to Mr. Eang Thearith, 37 years old, the owner of the house was hit by a stone on the roof of the bathroom. "Below, I have filed a complaint asking the authorities to find out and release the compensation according to the facts."
It should be noted that the residents of Village 12, Street 93, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh, have filed a joint complaint against a Chinese construction company that is affecting their daily lives. This is according to the complaint received by Fresh News on the night of November 26, 2019.
The complaint of the people sent to the Governor of Chamkar Mon District stated that: "Please sue China Construction Company No. 1 for causing damage to property, disturbing health and causing fear to daily life."
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sam Sereyroth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, called on Chinese investors who have not yet come to Cambodia, especially investors in Shanxi Province, to study and explore the potential and investment opportunities in Cambodia and decide to invest more in Cambodia. More.
The call was made during the opening ceremony of the Cambodia-China Business and Culture Forum (Sansi) on the morning of November 29, 2019, with the participation of Wu Fujie, Vice Chairman of the China International Trade Promotion Council, Shaanxi Province. Along with the Chinese delegation from Shanxi Province and many other stakeholders.
Mr. Sam Sereyroth said that he guarantees to all investors a favorable environment and promotes investment, especially peace, political and macroeconomic stability, effective legal framework, transparency and accountability.
It should be noted that the total trade volume between Cambodia and China in 2018 reached about 7.3 billion US dollars, of which exports from Cambodia to China amounted to more than 1,300 million US dollars and exports from China came to Cambodia worth more than 6 billion US dollars.
(Phnom Penh): The Council for the Development of Cambodia, the Cambodian-Chinese Association in Cambodia and the Economic Conference Council of the China Teochew Global Federation of Business Canadia Group this morning, November 29, 2019, opened the 2019 Economic Conference of the Global China Teocese Chamber of Commerce. And the Investment Summit in Cambodia to review the actual situation of investment in Cambodia.
Also present were Duke Pung Kheavse, President of the Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia and Co-Chair of the 2019 Economic Conference Committee of the 5th China Global Business Federation, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia. And hundreds of delegates from the China Teochew Global Business Federation.
Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Li said that China-Cambodia cooperation is the result of the leaders of the two countries who have worked hard to build and nurture the achievements of this cooperation under his wise leadership. President Xi Jinping and Samdech Te are Prime Minister Hun Sen.
He added that trade cooperation between the two countries is a replication and link between other sectors, including economy, culture, health, education and social affairs. In fact, Cambodia's economic development, which has grown by about 7% per year over the past 20 years, is inseparable from the participation of Chinese companies and enterprises.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the people of Cambodia, the Deputy Prime Minister would like to thank all the Chinese companies, enterprises and investors who have invested in various sectors in Cambodia with confidence in the leadership of the Royal Government. Peace, political stability and security, order are important factors for investment in Cambodia.
Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly hopes that the China Teochew Business Federation will continue to invest more and more in contributing to the economic development of Cambodia with the Royal Government, especially all these potentials will help investors to contribute to the development of Cambodia.
According to Duke Pung Kheav Se, China is Cambodia's main trading partner and largest source of investment. Through the implementation of the One Belt One Road strategy, more and more Chinese investors are coming to invest in Cambodia, bringing development opportunities for Cambodia.
The duke continued that the Chinese businessmen Teochew were a group of influential Chinese businessmen on the international stage. They live in all parts of the world. The efforts of the Chinese businessman Teochew not only develop their business but also contribute to the economic development of the country in which they live.
The president of the Khmer-Chinese Association in Cambodia also said that Cambodia is a country rich in Chinese Teochew, and most of the Chinese people living in Cambodia are of Chinese Teochew origin.
The duke pointed out that for a long time, the Chinese people living in Cambodia have worked hard together through the heavy rainstorm with the Cambodian people and the people to participate in building and promoting economic development. From the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Please be informed that Chinese Teochew businessmen who came to meet in Cambodia are all outstanding businessmen in real estate, finance, agriculture, industry, modern technology, etc. At the same time, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea also introduced the investment policy, investment opportunities and investment projects in Cambodia to inform Chinese business people.
