About the French Higher Education Agency (AUF) The French Higher Education Agency (AUF) is an international association that has been around for over 50 years. The association brings together more than 944 French-language universities, universities, higher education networks and scientific research centers in 116 countries around the world.
AUF is one of the most important associations for higher education and research institutions in the world. It is also the operator of the Higher Education Training and Research Summit of the Francophone Group (OIF).
The AUF has a mission to promote the use of French in higher education in solidarity in the cultural, economic and social development of member countries. It operates in 10 regions, including the Asia-Pacific region.
Since its establishment in Hanoi in 1993, the Asia-Pacific Regional Office has led a team of 79 members in 12 countries in the region: Cambodia, China, South Korea, Fiji, Indonesia, Japan, Laos, Mongolia, Thailand, Vanuatu. And Vietnam, including New Caledonia and French Polynesia. Mr. Ouch Borith: Unexploded ordnance left over from the war, causing danger to the lives of Cambodians and development
