Mr. Ouch Borith asserted: "In addition, landmines, unexploded ordnance and chemical weapons remain on Cambodian soil and pose a risk to the lives of the people and the development of the country. "Despite the clearance of these munitions by the Cambodian authorities, the results have been proud in the past."
