(Phnom Penh): The Royal Academy of Cambodia launches a workshop to promote the temple's architectural talent in order to promote the evolution of the current temple structure and achieve modernization.
On November 29, 2019, the Royal Academy of Cambodia organized a workshop on the evolution of the style and architecture of Khmer temples from the Udong period to the present, which showcases the Angkorian style, forms and features of some important Khmer ancient sculptures. The foundation is the core of the Khmer soul in modern and post-modern Khmer architecture and construction.
Dr. So Chhum Bun, Director of the Asian Studies Center of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that in the context of globalization, modern Khmer construction and architecture from the French colonial period to the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era to the present Khmer is always associated with The traditional Khmer architecture and design that has been left as a precious heritage since the time of the Angkorian Empire creates the invaluable sacred value of the Khmer nation.
He added that the workshop was also part of the gathering of Cambodian intellectual resources in the field of architectural style and construction to contribute to the promotion of national identity and social development with prosperity, prosperity and peace in Cambodian society.
According to previous research, Dr. Su Chhum Bun has shown that Khmer architecture is constantly evolving and evolving from one era to another and growing steadily. Thus, reflecting that Cambodian architects have the highest level of talent, in addition to the talent of combining synthesis of foreign art and previous generations of Cambodian art, Cambodian architects have created a new art form in the form of pure Khmer art in accordance with the purely Khmer philosophy.
According to Elder Lor San Virak, an artist from the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, he highlighted the unique talents of Khmer ancestors in the field of ancient Khmer architecture.
The elder mentioned the continuous evolution and growth of Khmer architecture from one era to another, which reflected the high talent of the ancient Khmer architects.
"Apart from the talent of combining foreign art and previous generations of Cambodian art, Cambodian architects have created a new art form in the form of pure Khmer art in line with the Khmer philosophy," he said.
Elder Lo San further emphasized, for example, that during the Phnom Da period, the Khmer Banlung Mountains were temples in the form of Indian art, but later Khmer architects invented the belief in heights such as natural mountains instead. Construction of mountain temples on the plains, in fact, the construction of temples in the Odong period.
Of course, this view of reverence for the Khmer people has existed since prehistoric times, and when India came to Cambodia, these two parallel views were even more influential and cultural. What Khmer has created is an innovation that draws on foreign civilizations that are similar, can be merged, come to process and innovate to be the soul of Khmer culture in the Khmer style.
Please note that this workshop has been published as a consultative article and is a valuable contribution for the benefit of Cambodian architects to be highly creative, talented in the synthesis of foreign art and Khmer art in the past. To create a new art in the form of Khmer art as a beacon to illuminate the path of Cambodian society for continuous development with progress, prosperity and lasting glory.
