Pre-Trial Chamber concludes three days trial in Case 003 against Meas Muth
(Phnom Penh): On November 29, 2019, the Pre-Trial Chamber of the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC) concluded a three-day trial in Case 003 against Meas Muth. This is according to the announcement of the Khmer Rouge tribunal.
International Co-Prosecutors, Deputy National Co-Prosecutors and National-International Co-Lawyers presented their arguments in this case. The Pre-Trial Chamber granted the request of Meas Muth, with Meas Muth providing the Pre-Trial Chamber with a medical certificate stating that due to old age and ill health, he was not fit to stand trial. He has a co-lawyer representing him at the hearing.
A case report showing the facts and background of the relevant proceedings in Case 003 as well as the details of the appeal before the Pre-Trial Chamber was issued on behalf of the entire Pre-Trial Chamber.
The Pre-Trial Chamber will decide whether Meas Muth meets the requirements of the court's jurisdiction and whether there are enough charges to send him to trial for a felony charge or charges against him. Exemption from charges. For now, the Pre-Trial Chamber will consider issuing a ruling. This verdict is final and there is no further appeal.
