Police crack down on illegal car pawnshops in Kirivong district, Takeo province, confiscate 2 vehicles
(Takeo): The specialized force of Takeo Provincial Police, in cooperation with the specialized force of Kampot Provincial Police, on November 28, 2019, searched and confiscated 2 vehicles in an illegal car pawn shop named Heng Srey Van, 46, and Steng Sokhorn, 53, of Phsar village, Phnom Den commune, Kirivong district, Takeo province, received a car mortgage from a Vietnamese national.
They both live in Kien Giang province, Vietnam, for a ride, but the suspects took the car as collateral for Heng Srey Van, 46, and Steng Sokhon, 53, of Phsar village, Phnom Den commune. Kirivong district, Takeo province.
Police said that after contacting Vietnamese authorities to help investigate the breach of trust, police in Takeo and Kampot provinces searched until they found the two vehicles that the suspects had taken as collateral in Kirivong district and Withdraw until the car is returned to its original owner, and the owner of the pawn shop is detained by the authorities for questioning at the Takeo Provincial Police.
Police crack down on a car robbery case from Phnom Penh to Prey Veng province, confiscate 3 guns and return the car to the victim
According to the story, on November 12, 2019, the suspect named Chut Chivant left a gambling place in NagaWorld, took a motorbike taxi to Chbar Ampov to rent a car to Prey Veng province, and when he arrived, he saw a silver Highlander taxi. Wearing license plate Svay Rieng 2B-4517, the owner of the car was an acquaintance who was driving to Prey Veng when he called the owner to drive to Prey Veng and return to Phnom Penh.
At around 8 a.m., he relied on NagaWorld security to get an unidentified man to buy a car for $ 14,000 and escape. Later, on November 15, 2019, the police confiscated a Highlander car with license plate Svay Rieng 2B-4517 from Yan Sam Ol at a car wash around Boeung Trabek in Boeung Trabek Sangkat.
On November 27, 2019, at around 8:00 PM, while he was at home in Borey Phonsui, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Sen Chey, he was arrested and interrogated at the Criminal Police Office.
At the request of the victim and with the approval of Mr. Kham Sophary, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, the police handed over the car to the victim for temporary use. At the same time, the police also handed over three AK weapons to the Prey Veng Provincial Police for use.
The suspect is currently being investigated by the police and sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action.
