Speaking at a press conference on the organization of the General Assembly, Mr. Nuon Pharath, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, this morning, November 29, 2019, said that Phnom Penh was approved by the AIMF Standing Committee at the 38th meeting of the AIMF in Phnom Penh. Lille, France, from November 5 to 7, 2018, was chosen to host the 39th meeting.
According to Mr. Nuon Pharath, this is the first time that he has hosted this event, which is a valuable opportunity for Phnom Penh to showcase its achievements and experience in developing the city, which has emerged from the genocidal field until it develops in all areas. Sectors under the leadership of the Royal Government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister.
The Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh also claimed that in Southeast Asia, only Phnom Penh, which is a member of the International Association of French-speaking Mayors (AIMF), has the benefit of presenting to 294 cities its potential. To those countries from the issue of World Heritage investment.
He expects and believes that through this hosting, Phnom Penh in particular and in general, the whole of Cambodia will gain more new experiences and opportunities to show the progress of Cambodia, other countries in the world. Taking the opportunity of the meeting, the delegates of the participating countries will also visit the Angkor area of Siem Reap to visit the temples of Cambodia.
Please be informed that the International Association of French-speaking Mayors was established in 1979 to bind French-speaking countries in the sense of exchanging experiences and good ideas with each other. Phnom Penh became a member of this association in 1990 and became a permanent member in 2003. Fake police sent to court after arrest in Por Sen Chey
