Senior National Bank Official: National Financial Environment Strategy as a policy tool to achieve a stable and efficient financial system
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Neav Chanthana, Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, stated that the National Financial Environment Strategy 2019-2025 is a policy tool aimed at achieving a stable, efficient and diversified financial system. Environmentally friendly and responsive to the needs of domestic financial services.
In addition, Ms. Neav Chanthana added that the national financial environment strategy also supports the sustainability of economic growth, achieving gender equality, empowering women, increasing people's incomes and reducing poverty.
The Deputy Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia also stated that this strategy also sets the direction for the Royal Government, development partners and the private sector to jointly implement and focus on areas that require immediate action.
She said that the National Bank of Cambodia is ready to facilitate the implementation of the action plan and ensure cooperation between all stakeholders to achieve the goal of the financial environment to increase access to quality official financial services. Reduce the rate of women without formal financial services from half from 27% to 13%.
In addition, it will expand the use of official financial services from 59% to 70% by 2025, as well as improve family well-being and support economic growth. This is the additional confirmation of Ms. Neav Chanthana.
Duke Pung Kheavse stated that achieving gender equality is part of the Royal Government in Cambodia's Rectangular Strategy for Growth, Equity and Efficiency. The Royal Government recognizes the greater participation of women in the economy and will accelerate the achievement of national goals such as sustainable economic development and justice.
Emphasize that the Women and Finance program aims to focus on discussions about the financial environment in promoting women's values in the financial sector and gender inequality through strategies, policies, technologies and financial education that can help achieve Gender equality and reduce the number of women who do not have access to formal financial services. This is part of the national strategy on the financial environment 2019-2025.
Khmer Breweries installs gas extraction system to use again to help the environment!
(Phnom Penh): In the wastewater treatment system discharged from the Khmer Breweries, methane gas is converted from wastewater and extracted for use as an auxiliary energy source in the boiler.
The company has installed this highly efficient methane extraction system to share the responsibility to participate in protecting our environment.
This recycling system is very useful in reducing the use of natural resources and polluting the environment, especially preventing the release of methane, carbon monoxide and nitrogen oxides into the atmosphere.
Methane is produced by organic digestion and converted into methane, carbon dioxide, nitrogen and sulfur. Methane is passed through a sulfur extraction system to purify the methane, which then passes through a dehumidifier before being sent to the furnace.
Methane is fired in a steam furnace and produced as hot steam to be used for heating needs in the production processes of production lines such as breweries, packaging plants and water treatment systems.
