He stressed that today's workshop has provided many benefits to participants and to Cambodian producers to highlight the difficulties in film production and increase the capacity of film production.
Both producers highlighted some of the challenges facing Cambodian filmmaking, noting that Cambodian cinema has made some progress, but the rate of national drama support is still limited as audiences are more supportive of foreign films.
In addition, the two producers also presented various strategies to promote and make the film industry grow and continue to enter the international market.
