Korea continues to support the health and safety of factory workers in Cambodia with a budget of more than 270,000 dollars
(Phnom Penh): A delegation from the Korea Occupational Health and Safety Agency (KOSHA) of the Republic of Korea visited Cambodia to gather information on occupational safety and health and pledged to continue to assist Cambodia in promoting occupational safety and health for workers. Employees in factories, enterprises to better and to show support for the project to study, research and prepare a law on occupational safety and health for Cambodia.
This strong will was expressed in a meeting between Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Ms. Heaeun CHOI, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Cooperation Development of the Ministry of Labor of the Republic of Korea on Thursday morning, March 2. S2563 is on November 28, 2019 at the Ministry of Labor.
Minister Ith Sam Heng requested the Korean side to expedite the implementation of the project to study and prepare the law on occupational safety and health in Cambodia by 2023 to reduce the occupational hazards of workers in the workplace. This law is already in use in ASEAN, except for Cambodia and Laos, which do not yet have it.
In response, Ms. Heaeun CHOI stated that the Government of the Republic of Korea is preparing a law and conducting further studies to ensure that after its implementation, it is supported by all stakeholders and benefits. Better workers.
Minister Ith Sam Heng added that the preparation of the Law on Occupational Safety and Health is set out in the first program of the Strategic Plan for Employment Development and Vocational Training, Phase 2, 2019-2023 of the Ministry of Labor and contributes to the policy of the Royal Government. In particular, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, pays attention to workers' health and safety for workers.
In addition, the drafting of the Occupational Safety Law will contribute to improving the legal framework, addressing the lack of legal documents in this area, strengthening the national occupational safety and health management system at the sub-national and enterprise levels, reducing occupational accidents and diseases. Biodiversity that contributes significantly to the socio-economic progress and diversification in Cambodia as well as regional and international competition.
It should be noted that at the request of the Cambodian side on the preparation of the Law on Occupational Safety and Health, KOSHA has agreed to support Cambodia in the study and preparation by the Department of Labor Medicine of the Ministry of Labor through the project for 3 years (2021 -2023).
This project aims to study and process the law on occupational safety and health, which is implemented by the Department of Labor of the Ministry of Labor with technical and financial support from the Ministry of Labor and Labor and KOSHA, which uses a total budget of 277 $ 863.
