Cambodia, Australia discuss trade expansion due to low level
(Phnom Penh): In a meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, and Ms. Angela Corcoran, Australian Ambassador to Cambodia, who ended her term this morning, November 28, 2019, the two sides discussed Expansion of trade and investment due to low trade volume between the two countries.
After the meeting, Koy Kuong, a spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, said that the trade volume between Cambodia and Australia was still very small compared to the trade volume between Cambodia and other countries. Despite the small size, it is noted that the trade volume between the two countries is constantly increasing year by year due to the good relations and cooperation.
"Trade is increasing, however, if we compare the trade volume between Cambodia and other countries, the trade volume between Cambodia and Australia is also low," he said. That is why Cambodia and Australia are working hard to increase trade volume.
According to Koy Kuong, in this morning's meeting, Cambodia and Australia also discussed tourism. Both sides are committed to encouraging more Australian tourists to visit Cambodia, as the average number of Australian tourists visiting Cambodia has been around 130,000.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs said that ODA development assistance from 1992 to 2018 is about 1 billion US dollars. The assistance focused on infrastructure, trade, agriculture, fisheries, water, education, health, demining, as well as providing assistance to the Khmer Rouge tribunal.
The Cambodian head of diplomacy also congratulated the Ambassador on her successful diplomatic mission in Cambodia. She considers that her diplomatic mission has improved the relationship and cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Australian Government.
Ms. Angela Corcoran expressed her pleasure that during her three years of diplomatic service in Cambodia, she was very pleased with the good cooperation from the Cambodian side, especially from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. Spokesman: The Ministry of Health is still focused on finding new cases of leprosy or leprosy
(Phnom Penh): Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, on November 28, 2019, emphasized that the Ministry of Health is still focusing on finding new cases of leprosy and effective treatment with drugs. Many faces.
This statement was made on the occasion of Dr. O Vandin's participation in the meeting on the announcement of the results after the end of the project to vaccinate people affected by leprosy or leprosy held at Tonle Bassac II Restaurant in Phnom Penh. This morning, November 28, 2019.
Dr. O Vandin said that although the Ministry of Health has reduced the disease as a public health problem, but not completely eliminated. This means that replication is low and persistent as a result of which new cases occur.
Outbreaks appear to be exacerbated during this time around the community, and health workers at all levels play an important role in finding new cases and treatments, especially as the prevalence rate decreases. The huge result is now due to the participation of all parties.
On that occasion, Dr. O Vandin also thanked all the organizations that helped fight against hepatitis. She strongly expects them to continue to help with hepatitis B in partnership with the ministry in the coming years.
She also said that in 2019, the Ministry of Health will focus more on continuing to connect and fill the gaps between community and health by strengthening the knowledge of the people for them to receive consultation and treatment.
Dr. O Vandin added that in addition, the Ministry has encouraged and encouraged the provincial level to work with village volunteers and NGOs, as well as factory and media outreach campaigns.
