(Phnom Penh): A delegation of the Asian Cultural Council led by the Honorable Dr. Khuon Sodary, President of the Asian Cultural Council, Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Honorary Founding Chairman of the Asian Cultural Council, presided over the closing ceremony. "Gyeongyu World Culture Exhibition - 2019" on November 24, 2019 in Gyeongyu, Gyeongsangbuk-do, Republic of Korea.
This cultural exhibition runs for 45 days from October 11 to November 24, 2019 under the theme "Culture is the key to our future".
Ms. Khuon Sodary added that the cooperation in this cultural exhibition is to build bridges, increase communication networks and forums between communities and governments, to promote peace and sustainable development through the promotion of cultural diversity.
During the closing ceremony, the delegation of the Asian Cultural Council also met with Mr. Lee Chul-woo, Governor of Kyungsangbokdo Province and President of the Kyungyu World Cultural Exhibition Foundation, to raise the level of Cambodia-Korea relations. Become a full-fledged strategic partner to further enhance the potential of the two countries' relations, cooperation, investment and trade.
Mr. Sous Yara, Director General of the Asian Cultural Council, also signed a Memorandum of Understanding between the Secretariat of the Asian Cultural Council and the Secretariat of the World Heritage City in the Asia-Pacific Region, represented by Mr. Young Li. Both institutions in the conservation and development of heritage cities.
During the visit, the delegation also visited several historical sites, such as the Korea National Heritage Park, as well as the World Heritage Park, which show the religion and dynasty of the Seila Kingdom of Korea 1300 years ago. During the 45-day Gyeongyu World Culture Expo 2019, there will be art performances and exhibitions from 27 countries and a total of one million visitors.
The Royal Government of Cambodia also sent an art delegation led by Ms. Phoeung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, to attend the opening ceremony and performance of this event from October 5 to 15, 2019.
He said that it is an honor for the Republic of Korea, especially the Council of the World Cultural Organization, to cooperate with the Council of the Organization of Asian Cultures by promoting special cooperation in Asia in the field of cultural participation. From 10 countries in Asia and allow Cambodia to showcase its talents in organizing this World Culture Fair.
According to the Director General of the Asian Cultural Council, we are pleased that the people, as well as the entire Asian nation,'s values of our culture have given us hope in the future to create new jobs. Of new income in a culturally innovative way.
It should be noted that from November 21, 2006 to January 9, 2007, the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Korea jointly organized the Angkor-Gyeongyu World Culture Exhibition in Siem Reap with the participation of more than 30 countries and More than a million tourists. Culture is not only the preservation of tangible and intangible heritage, culture is an important source of sustainable economic growth and national identity.
