ASEAN Banking Conference Focuses on Digital Reform in Banking and Financial Services
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia is hosting the 22nd ASEAN Banking Conference, which focuses on digital reform in the banking and financial services sector in Southeast Asia. This is the first time that Cambodia has hosted the ASEAN Banking Conference, which is held every two years by ASEAN member countries.
The event was organized with the participation of about 550 delegates from ASEAN, as well as many Cambodian delegates and participants. One ASEAN Bank ”which reflects the progress and importance of digital technology and Internet connectivity in the banking sector.
Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, said, “I am confident that all delegates will have the opportunity to explore and share experiences to promote the use of digital technology in banking operations to meet the growing needs of customers and strengthen Efficiency and transparency of banking operations.
Dr. In Channy, President of the Banking Association of Cambodia and CEO of ACLEDA Bank, also highlighted the importance of integrating digital technology into the Bank's operations. Digital. This is a big change in how banks and financial institutions understand interactions and meet customer needs.
Please be informed that since 2007, EZECOM has been a leading internet company for companies and enterprises in Cambodia and also sponsored the 22nd ASEAN Banking Conference. In 2017, EZECOM inaugurated Cambodia's first submarine cable to increase its internet distribution capacity as well as make its internet service faster, more hassle-free and more secure to meet the demand for high-quality internet service at Cambodia.
