CDX Workshop on Derivatives Trading, Investment Readiness and Investment Awareness in Koh Kong Province
(Koh Kong): CDX Company of the Senior Officials of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia on November 28, 2019 held a seminar on “Derivatives Trading, Investment Preparation and Investment Awareness in the Presence of Mr. Sou” Socheat is the Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, Mr. Phay Thun Plam Keson, Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Province, many government officials and business owners.
Mr. Sou Socheat stated that the reason why the SEC set up this training was to encourage stakeholders to better understand risk management and opportunities before deciding to invest in derivatives or securities.
Expertise through derivatives or securities trading only started in 2016. Koh Kong is the 17th province to receive training on how to trade derivatives. Currently, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has licensed five counterparties and 30 derivatives brokers.
Lawrence Kook, Governor of CDX, explains that the success of this type of business requires investors to be analytical, both technical and fundamental, such as understanding the odds of products and services on the market. The world. Therefore, the company increases the training of stakeholders to understand the key characteristics before making a successful business investment decision.
Derivatives, on the other hand, refer to contracts for price gaps on the original financial instruments arising from equity securities, bonds, precious metals, crude oil, natural gas, agricultural products, currencies, as well as commodity hedging schemes.
