On behalf of the Provincial Governor, on behalf of all the leaders of the Armed Forces, I would like to express my deepest gratitude to the Minister and the accompanying delegation for taking the time to attend the Royal Government Dissemination Ceremony today. This.
The provincial governor also reported on the progress and some challenges related to floods, water shortages for crops and water for daily use of the people in the province in recent years.
At the same time, in order for the water policy for crop production to be better and better, the provincial governor also requested the Minister to establish more irrigation reservoirs and build a large-scale pumping station to supply Water to 3 districts of the province as well.
Mr. Lim Kean Hor, on behalf of all ministry leaders, thanked the provincial governor for facilitating the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to disseminate this circular. Climate change is an important topic for the whole world that we all need to pay special attention to the issue of water security from now until the next rainy season in 2020.
After receiving the circular on behalf of the Minister as the head of the institution, assigned the leaders of the ministries in charge of the 25 provincial capitals to disseminate to the local authorities at all levels to implement, especially the people to understand and understand the importance of Water in the sense of participating in the management and maintenance of water better to avoid the same situation as in 2015-2016.
