Of which, 114,891 square meters of roads and dams are occupied, 530,776 square meters are occupied and settled by the Fisheries Administration, and 27,126 square meters are occupied. The remaining 90,567 square meters. In 1998, the former Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries handed over 27,126 m2 of land to the Office of Fisheries Management and Enjoyment to date.
