Russian cows wear VR gear to reduce stress
(Moscow): A farm in Russia allows dairy cows to wear VR equipment to reduce stress and improve milk quality. This was released by the BBC on Wednesday, November 27, 2019.
VR equipment is fitted on the cows' heads to make them feel as fresh as in a beautiful summer pasture. The Russian Ministry of Agriculture and Food confirmed that based on a study that the mood or stress of cows and dairy is related. That is, the quality and yield of milk can vary according to their mood.
