* Understand and respect the rights and obligations of civil servants as stated in the content of the Law on the General Statute of Cambodian Civil Servants, especially in accordance with the spirit of the sub-decree on the management of the presence of civil servants and contracted officials and legal documents.
* Continue to train and develop its capacity to respond to the needs of work and the evolution of society, especially on language and information technology skills.
* For the head of the office at both the national and sub-national levels to participate in the deployment and division of duties to civil servants and contract officers under their supervision properly and special skills to use the resources of those officials to the best of their ability.
* Must have a spirit of unity, internal unity and good cooperation with the management and colleagues in the unit.
As a civil servant, you must protect the interests of the nation, the public interest, the interests of the unit and the interests of the civil servants.
* Must use the knowledge gained from various training courses to target and disseminate to officials in the unit who are practicing this skill but have not yet had the opportunity to participate in this training.
* Must adhere to the position of a good official, exemplary official who is willing to work with high responsibility and innovative initiative as a necessary resource to serve the unit and the motherland of Cambodia.
