Koh Kong Provincial Administration Holds a Dissemination and Consultation Forum of the Third Mandate Provincial Council
(Koh Kong): On November 27, 2019, Koh Kong Provincial Administration organized a forum for dissemination and consultation of Koh Kong Provincial Council of the third mandate in Royal Khemarak City in the presence of Mr. Kay Samrum, Chairman of Koh Kong Provincial Council and Mr. Phay Thun Plam Keson. The Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Province and all local authorities will be joined by a large number of people from three communes.
Koh Kong Provincial Council Dissemination and Consultation Forum focuses on six main goals, including:
1: Briefing on Roles, Duties and Relations between Provincial Councils and Provincial Governors 2: Brief Report on the Overview of the Development Situation, Successes and Challenges of the Provincial Administration for the first 9 months of 2013: Brief presentation on service delivery Administration at Sub-National Administration 4: Demonstration of Roles, Duties and Powers of Koh Kong Provincial People's Office 5: Consultation Process with Citizens 6: Summarize the results of the forum.
In this third mandate consultation and consultation forum, people raised many suggestions, they want roads and drainage system to be easy to travel and avoid water flowing quickly in the rainy season. These are the requests of the people of the three Sangkats in Khemarak Phoumin City, Koh Kong Province.
Mr. Kay Samrum said that some questions and suggestions have already been clarified and resolved by the relevant authorities, but there are still a small number of questions and suggestions that have not been clarified and addressed yet.
