SCG's Director of Marketing and Sales in Cambodia added that as their skills improve and become accredited by the training and competition program, local builders or construction contractors will have job opportunities and income. Even higher.
The second annual Construction Competition is part of the SCG Construction Training Program, which aims to promote the construction sector in Cambodia in the long run. SCG, in collaboration with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training through the National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia (NPIC), has been organizing this master builder competition since 2018.
As of the end of 2019, more than 400 master builders from all over Cambodia have been trained and nearly 80 have participated in the annual skills competition organized by the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and SCG.
