Khmer Rouge tribunal hears arguments in Case 003 regarding Meas Muth
(Phnom Penh): The Pre-Trial Chamber of the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC) will begin its three-day trial in Case 003 against Meas Muth on 27 November 2019. This hearing was held to hear the oral arguments of the parties involved in Case 003, with Mr. Meas Muth as the accused. This is according to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Head of Public Affairs of the ECCC.
Mr. Pheaktra stated that the current hearing was not a hearing on the evidence but an appeal in Case 003 in which the parties had appealed against the Co-Investigating Judges' Closing Order. Ago.
To begin, the President of the Chamber announces a public hearing, followed by a public reading of the case file, which outlines the relevant facts and proceedings of Case 003, as well as the details of the appeals filed. In front of the Chamber. This report was issued on behalf of the entire Pre-Trial Chamber and included in the case file. More than 500 members of the public attended the hearing.
The Pre-Trial Chamber has decided that a hearing will be held in Case 003 to hear arguments from the parties in the case before the Pre-Trial Chamber issues a ruling on those appeals.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the Pre-Trial Chamber has predicted that it will be able to issue a ruling on the appeal against the Closing Order in Case 003 by the first quarter of 2020, whether the case will be sent to trial. The dismissal or dismissal depends on the decision of the three-judge pre-Trial Chamber and two international judges.
