Another 116 sub-national officials receive training on budget preparation and implementation procedures
(Stung Treng): Strengthen the capacity of sub-national officials as a policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia to achieve the implementation of the third phase of public financial management reform. Many sub-national civil servants are continuously trained after "procedures for preparing and implementing budgets for municipal, district and khan administrations."
Earlier this week, another 116 civil servants from Stung Treng, Kratie, Mondulkiri and Ratanakkiri provinces received training on "procedures for preparing and implementing budgets for municipal, district and khan administrations." This training aims to strengthen the capacity and raise awareness to participate in the implementation of the third phase of public financial management reform.
This workshop is co-organized by the Institute of Economics and Finance and the General Department of Finance, Sub-National Administration of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Speaking at the opening ceremony, Mr. NM, Director of the Institute of Economics and Finance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, stated that this training is an important activity to support the public financial management reform program and the decentralization and deconcentration reform program. And the Royal Government's Public Administration Reform Program, which will contribute to the development of human resources in sub-national administrations.
He said that this training is also to strengthen and expand the capacity of civil servants of the administration of municipalities, districts, Khans, enhance the ownership and professional conscience to respond to the actual needs of the sub-national administration, especially will help the transfer process and Resources to the sub-national administration to be more efficient.
The director of the institute also highlighted the Public Management Reform Program, which was officially launched in 2004, achieving significant achievements, especially the "credibility of the budget" in the first phase. And "Financial Accountability" in the second phase.
Mr. NM stated that the reform program is currently in the third phase in order to increase the "linking the budget to policy" priority of the Royal Government, which will be successfully completed by 2020 and will be implemented. 4 (2021-2025) in achieving the goal of "achievement accountability".
