For more details, please read the press release: APSARA Authority improves the beauty of Wat Reach Bo
(Phnom Penh): Wat Reachbo is one of the oldest pagodas on the banks of the Siem Reap River in Wat Bo Village, Sangkat Sala Kamroeuk, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province. Ascended during the reign of King Norodom.
On the inner walls of the church is a lively and beautiful painting, the ancient painting "Reamker", a famous story in Southeast Asia, painted between 1920-1924 by a craftsman named Pil and his nephew Dith. Both painters are carpenters for the big skin theater, so the paintings have the same skin-like gestures. On the outside, there are vibrant bas-reliefs on the doors and windows.
This old church has been renovated since French colonial times and is now in a state of disrepair, requiring renovation due to age and climate. In order to contribute to the preservation of this heritage, APSARA Authority has cooperated with Italian experts to start repairing important parts of the temple in 2014.
Doors, windows, paintings and statues in the church were all technically repaired and cleaned by conservators. All this work is always highly attentive and provides full opportunities about Maha Vimal Dhamma Pin Sem Sereysovano, Chief Preacher of Wat Reachbo.
The current conservation work for the church has recently been renovated in two additional phases:
* Phase 1: Study the project, quote the old plan and make the metal roof to cover the temple using the budget of the Buddhists under the initiative of Maha Vimal Dhamma Pin Sem Sereysovano.
* Phase 2: Renovation of the roof of the church focuses on repairing the roof components to maintain the balance of the roof, kill germs and insects, eat wood, repair and clean the bell tower with all the carvings and roof decoration is 100% complete under Provides funding and technical specifications from the APSARA Authority. Technically, we try to keep the look intact and use existing materials as much as possible and use appropriate methods for future conservation.
King: Today, under the leadership of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has improved the lives of people with disabilities (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni The King of Cambodia praised the leadership of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has improved the lives of people with disabilities.
The King's appreciation was conveyed through a congratulatory message on the occasion of the official launch of the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2019-2023 and the 21st and 37th Cambodia International Day of Persons with Disabilities, which will Held on December 3, 2019.
In his message, he said: "Today, under the wise leadership of the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Honorary President of the Disability Action Council, has improved the lives of people with disabilities. "Improved by promoting decent employment and career growth, as well as strengthening ownership by encouraging people with disabilities to have their own businesses to reduce poverty in society."
At the same time, the King encouraged and called on all compatriots to continue to support the activities of people with disabilities to eliminate obstacles to strengthen ownership in the direction of achievement. Promote and protect the rights of people with disabilities.
He also thanked the national and international community for their generous support, both in terms of spirit, material and financial support to help the disability sector in the Kingdom of Cambodia succeed.
