Cooperation between the Mekong countries and the Republic of Korea was established during 2011 and there are regular meetings. However, the meeting was held only at the level of the Foreign Minister, which showed that the talks, cooperation and relations were still limited and had not yet reached the top level.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, also initiated and proposed to increase the level of meetings between the countries along the Mekong River and the Republic of Korea from the level of ministerial meetings to the same summit level as China and Japan. .
Mr. Moon Jae-in at the opening ceremony of the summit this morning, despite the absence of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, he thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for initiating this summit.
At the meeting, President Moon said that if the Republic of Korea's development experience is combined with the potential of the Mekong region, the miracle on the Han River will lead to the miracle of the Mekong River.
"South Korea will stay with the Mekong, believing that the development of the Mekong is also South Korea's development," he said.
Moon also said that countries along the Mekong have become land full of development potential and South Korea has become a "special friend" of the Mekong because the region has established prosperous relations with ASEAN in preparation. For the Asia-Pacific era.
Trade volume between South Korea and the five Mekong countries totaled $ 84.5 billion in 2018, an increase of 2.4 times in the eight years following cooperation between South Korea. And countries along the Mekong River.
