"We must work together to increase the economy and improve the lives of the people to another level in order to effectively manage and conserve natural resources for generations to come," he added. "The Ministry of Environment has set a community economic development plan to better manage natural resources across the country, and Prey Lang is an important start."
Mr. Say Sam Al emphasized that Cambodia's protected areas are unique in that they live with natural resources, and that the sustainable protection and conservation of natural resources for future generations requires the participation of all stakeholders. In particular, make the community economically strong and prosperous.
He stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the attention of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has already presided over two national forums on "Protection and Conservation of Natural Resources" in 2016 and The year 2017 has set clear strategic objectives and visions to ensure that all stakeholders participate in the protection and conservation of natural resources.
On that occasion, the Minister announced the priority plan for community economic development, including improving community life by helping the community to build infrastructure, improving health, raising livestock, and encouraging the children of the people in the community. Higher education and vocational training shift from reliance on natural resources to new career options such as industry and services.
At the same time, the Minister of Environment encouraged the people in the community to develop eco-tourism, in which the Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Tourism will cooperate to organize and help train eco-tourism skills to improve the livelihood of the community.
On that occasion, two communities in the protected area, Kbal Dauntey Protected Area and Choam Merech Protected Community in Kampong Thom Province, signed an agreement with Mr. Nong Veasna, Member of Parliament for Kampong Thom Constituency, to develop the livelihood of the community. Community water management for three consecutive years, with each community receiving $ 5,000 per year.
The delegation also distributed anti-malarial mosquito nets to rangers and local people. At the same time, Mr. Say Sam Al and representatives of relevant ministries, institutions, provincial authorities and representatives of development partners inspected the forest in the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary.
Prey Lang is designated as "Prey Lang" Wildlife Sanctuary on an area of 431,683 hectares in Kampong Thom, Kratie, Preah Vihear and Stung Treng provinces by sub-decree No. 74 dated 9 May 2016. And 83 park rangers have been defending and conserving since the transfer of control from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to the Ministry of Environment in April 2016.
In 2019, the Ministry of Environment has organized and officially recognized 19 protected communities with tens of thousands of people living in and near the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary in order to increase resource management participation. Nature is sustainable and contributes to improving the lives of local communities in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The delegation of relevant institutions appreciated the efforts of the rangers of the Ministry of Environment who have sacrificed everything to protect and preserve the Prey Lang forest sanctuary, as well as the participation of the community in the protected area in conservation work.
