(Mondulkiri): Mr. Keo Remy, Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, affirmed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, is one of the leaders who cares deeply about the values of peace, political stability, especially respect for rights. People, contrary to some individuals, deliberately put Cambodia in insecurity.
Mr. Keo Remy made this assertion on the morning of November 26, 2019, when he presided over the opening of a lecture on "Keeping the Peace Together to Promote Human Rights". In collaboration with the Cambodian Human Rights Committee and the Mondulkiri Provincial Administration.
Mr. Keo Remy said: "When there is a war and the right to food is over, the right to education is no more, there is no shelter, not even life is guaranteed, so human rights are all related to these stories and experiences, Samdech "Techo Hun Sen, you have such experience, you are a leader who thinks about the key is to maintain peace and stability."
Through Samdech Techo's great respect for human rights, Mr. Keo Remy continued that only Cambodia has allowed the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia since the 1990s, as well as Promote cooperation with other organizations working on human rights so that they can express their views on human rights in Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen without restrictions.
The Cambodian human rights chief stated: "If a leader does not respect the supreme law of the state, and if he is to lead a country in a state of dictatorship and let the people believe, it is a dictatorship and people who do not follow the law are over. "And just in case of human rights, we have done a lot of work and the government has done a lot to help promote human rights."
Mr. Sim Sitha stated that the new water treatment plant has a capacity of up to 400,000 cubic meters per day, divided into two stages, the first step is to produce nearly 200,000 cubic meters of water per day, using a total investment of 156 million. Dollars.
The Director General of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority said, "I would like to inform you that the construction of a water treatment plant in Bak Kheng, with a total cost of 156 million US dollars, has a capacity to supply 195 thousand cubic meters of water. One day.
At the same time, the head of the Water Supply Authority also pointed out that the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority and the construction team expect that the construction site will officially open in January 2020.
Currently, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has 4 water treatment plants, one of which is under construction (Bak Kheng factory). These four factories have a capacity of only 560,000 cubic meters per day and currently supply from three factories: Prek Village, Chroy Changva and Niroth.
From year to year, the demand for water has increased steadily. In 2014, Phnom Penh was supplied with only 163 million cubic meters of water per year, in 2015 increased to 178 million cubic meters per year, in 2016 increased to 199 Million cubic meters per year.
Congratulations! Cambodia has another baby dolphin, born in Stung Treng province
(Kratie): It is a happy story for the people of Kratie province as well as the people of Cambodia as well.
According to the Cambodian Natural Resources Conservation Organization (WWF-Cambodia), the newborn dolphin was spotted on November 20, 2019 at around 8:30 am. In Tbong Khla Dolphin Canyon, in Koh Chrum village, O'Mreah commune, Siem Bok district, Stung Treng province.
A research team from WWF and Kratie and Stung Treng Fisheries Administration inspected newborn dolphins after receiving information from the Koh Chrum River Guard on November 17, 2019. After the inspection, the research team actually found the newborn dolphin and the team also observed and photographed the baby dolphin and its mother.
According to the Cambodian Natural Resources Conservation Organization, the newborn dolphins are about five days old in a herd of about six large dolphins.
The new baby dolphin is the twelfth baby dolphin recorded to be born in 2019 from January to November, with six dolphins recorded being born in In Stung Treng and six baby dolphins were recorded being born in Kratie.
Dolphins in the Mekong River at Kampi Dolphin Canyon in Kratie Province and Dolphin Canyon in Stung Treng Province are becoming a national and international tourist attraction today. The director of the Fisheries Administration considered that the presence of new dolphins will be another important contribution to tourism along the Mekong River.
Mr. Eng Chea San also called on the people as well as the fishing community to protect dolphins to increase the number of dolphins in Cambodia's Mekong River.
