(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Liam Soda, Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, called on Chinese investors to continue to invest in Cambodia, especially in Preah Sihanouk Province.
The Deputy Governor of Sihanoukville made this call on the occasion of his participation in the Chinese Business Entrepreneur Conference in Sihanoukville.
Mr. Liam Soda continued to support Chinese investors in Sihanoukville to promote economic growth and create jobs for people, especially young people. He also welcomed and called on Chinese investors to invest more in Cambodia, especially in Sihanoukville.
The Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province said that Preah Sihanouk Province is an important national development pole in the coastal area of Cambodia and a province with high economic potential to attract investors and tourists with beach entertainment and beautiful islands and ports. International, international airports and rich natural resources.
Mr. Liam Soda said that the meeting of the Chinese Business Association in Cambodia in Sihanoukville is a good opportunity to exchange information, opinions, experiences and discuss good solutions for doing business in Sihanoukville and establish Network as well as strengthen business relationships.
With the good relations between Cambodia and China, Mr. Liam Soda also mentioned the words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the Free Trade Agreement between Cambodia and China.
Mr. Liam Soda stated that on December 4, 2019, the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of China will hold a meeting to negotiate a free trade agreement. The meeting was held to open up more and better trade between Cambodia and China.
This free trade agreement will provide more market flow opportunities to Cambodia in addition to what has been achieved through the ASEAN-China Free Trade Agreement.
Liang Chiling, President of the Chinese Business Association of Cambodia in Sihanoukville, said that based on the cooperation of one road, one belt and close relations between the two countries will help Sihanoukville to develop and prosper. .
He stressed that the Chinese Business Association will strive to attract more Chinese investors to invest in Sihanoukville to develop the coastal province's economy.
Mr. Oknha Chea Soeun, Permanent Vice President of the Cambodian-Chinese Coalition in Cambodia, said that the meeting of Chinese business entrepreneurs in Sihanoukville was an opportunity to discuss and exchange ideas and business partnerships between Chinese investors.
He said that he welcomes the presence of Chinese investors in Sihanoukville and expects that this beautiful coastal city will become an international city with high development.
