At the ASEAN-ROK Summit held in Busan, South Korea on Tuesday, South Korean President Moon Jae-in and leaders of ASEAN member states decided to adopt A statement on "Vision for Peace, Prosperity and Partnership" aimed at strengthening ties between South Korea and the ASEAN community.
On the other hand, Moon and the leaders of ASEAN countries reaffirmed their respective commitments for free trade and expressed strong opposition to the principles of all forms of protectionist trade. The two sides also pledged to promote trade and investment for development and prosperity in the region, and stressed cooperation to reduce regional development differences.
On the occasion of the 30th anniversary of the establishment of bilateral dialogue between South Korea and ASEAN, the South Korean Presidential Palace stressed that the statement of common vision will help guide cooperation and cooperation. As a South Korea-ASEAN partner towards a better future.
