Director of Film Department continues to call for more film production and quality to reach foreign markets
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pok Borak, Director of the Film and Arts Department of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, continued to call on all local filmmakers to produce more and more quality films in order to enter the foreign film market.
Mr. Pok Borak made this remark during the opening ceremony of the 6th National Film Festival 2019 under the slogan "Together to promote Khmer cinema" on the night of November 25, 2019.
Pok Borak, director of the Department of Film and the Arts at the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, said: "The production of small market factors and internal administrative relations are not yet good, which is the main obstacle to the growth process in the film industry."
Mr. Pok Borak also advised filmmakers to produce quality films in order to gain the support of a large audience to contribute to the betterment of Cambodian films.
He added, "In order to improve the quality of Cambodian films to compete with foreign films, especially to capture the overseas film market, the Ministry of Culture has introduced a number of measures, such as training human resources on film skills, facilitating the private sector. "Investment in the film industry, tax facilitation, legal documentation related to film production, focusing on the provision of public services, as well as efforts to find a film market."
He said that the 6th National Film Festival is a measure of the filmmakers' ability to produce films as an indicator in determining the direction of our film development.
Mr. Hap Touch, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, said that the 6th National Film Festival 2019 is not only a forum for film competitions to win awards, but also a forum for gathering, studying, understanding, measuring and sharing. Share experience, knowledge and creativity as well.
He added that the festival is a platform to strengthen the solidarity between filmmakers and technicians in the film industry for better co-production in the future.
The Secretary of State added that the Ministry of Culture considers that the organization of this film festival will be an important annual event to contribute to the development of the film industry in Cambodia and will receive support from the public, especially young people who love Khmer films.
He added that in addition, the festival will provide more benefits for the experience for filmmakers, especially contributing to the preservation of traditional culture, national traditions to turn Cambodia into a center of Khmer culture, which is the main policy. One of the national policies on culture.
Mr. Hap Touch also encouraged filmmakers, writers, directors, technicians and artists to create innovative film products to serve the audience and contribute to the preservation of national cultural values and contributions. Directly to create jobs for the people as well.
Please be informed that the 6th National Film Festival 2019 lasts for 5 days, from November 25-29, 2019, with 9 film productions applying to participate in the competition with 18 films.
The Ministry of Culture has determined that the films to be entered into the competition must focus on a number of topics, such as: educating and disseminating knowledge about culture, traditions, national traditions, promoting a culture of peace, strengthening national unity and solidarity, creating creativity and reflecting social reality. .
All films submitted to the 6th National Film Festival 2019 must comply with the following conditions: 1. Khmer films produced by local production and obtain a screening visa from the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts. Khmer films produced between 2016 and 2019 and have never competed in the National Film Festival in the past.
