According to a recent discussion, representatives from the Ministry of Tourism requested the submission of noodles, ambok, Khmer desserts and Touk Kang to be submitted to UNESCO. However, this is just a suggestion of the representative of the Ministry of Tourism, while the decision on which heritage to choose to submit to UNESCO is not yet official, which requires further discussions.
Mr. Chuch Phoeun added that if the inter-ministerial committee has discussed and prepared enough documents to place any heritage, the documents will be submitted to the Minister of Culture and Fine Arts for review and decision.
Similarly, in the event that Cambodia decides to choose ambok, noodles, desserts, weaving, Khmer martial arts, ark, request to UNESCO to include it in the World Heritage List, so it takes a year to have the right to go out to defend.
In particular, for the intangible heritage that is being considered for submission to UNESCO, which was mentioned by Mr. Chuch Phoeun, there may be such as Phnom Kulen resort and some other forest areas protected by the government.
