General Chuon Sovann: Local authorities intervene in time for drug activities
(Phnom Penh): General Chuon Sovann, Deputy Director of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, stressed that external law enforcement forces could not solve the problem or intervene to the local level in a comprehensive and timely manner as those in the local area. "Whose itch is that person scratching only the itchy place."
This emphasis was made by General Chuon Sovann on the morning of November 26, 2019, when he chaired a meeting to review and discuss the draft national policy and guidelines on "preparation Establish drug-free villages, communes and sangkats ”at the Ministry of Interior, with the participation of many representatives of relevant ministries and institutions.
The general stressed that "this is an important point that we need to understand and think carefully, because the law enforcement forces from outside can not come to solve the problem or provide intervention to the grassroots in a comprehensive and timely manner. "Like you in the local area, whose itch is the one who scratches the itch."
