Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, Chairman of the National Mekong River Commission of Cambodia and Chairman of the MRC Council for 2019, chaired the meeting in the presence of MRC Council Ministers of the MRC member countries. Cambodia, Laos, Thailand and Vietnam, representatives of development partners, representatives of dialogue partners (China and Myanmar), representatives of regional and international organizations and a total of 100 MRC Secretariat officials.
The meeting will discuss the progress of the implementation of the MRC development strategy and strategic plan 2016-2020 and the preparation for the next phase, regional cooperation, implementation of procedures on water use management, monitoring. Rivers and some other important works. The meeting will also review and approve the MRC work plan for 2020-2021 and the drought management strategy for 2020-2025.
The Minister also mentioned the challenges in the Mekong River Basin, especially the severe drought, which caused the Mekong River to flow in 2019 at the lowest level ever. In this context, the Minister expressed the hope that the current Drought Management Strategy 2020-2025 adopted now will help solve the problem of drought in managing and reducing the risk of floods that will occur effectively.
On behalf of the Chairman of the MRC Council for 2019, the Minister thanked the development partners, dialogue partners and other stakeholders who have helped the MRC to achieve many great achievements so far in its efforts and efforts. Regional cooperation for sustainable development in the Mekong Basin.
The Minister emphasized that the MRC has been preparing the Basin Development Strategy 2021-2030 and its strategic plan 2021-2025 in order to contribute to and achieve the sustainable development goals in the Mekong Basin as set out in The Siem Reap Declaration adopted by the Heads of Government of Cambodia, Laos, Thailand and Vietnam at the 3rd MRC Summit in April 2018 in Siem Reap.
The Minister requested the partners and stakeholders to continue to support and cooperate in the process towards this goal to be successful.
