Dr. Ley Sopheap calls again for network marketers to receive training to avoid cheating
(Phnom Penh): Seeing the progress of the network marketing business is growing, Dr. Ley Sopheap, President of the Cambodian Network Marketing Business Association, also expressed concern about some opportunists who seize this opportunity. Deceive people and business people alike.
Seeing this worrying issue, Dr. Ley Sopheap once again called on network marketers as well as online product sellers to come and receive proper training to gain knowledge of business law. Like other relevant knowledge to apply for their business to avoid cheating those crooks.
As for this wicked person, he was warned by the president of the association that if he continues to commit crimes against the people, he will still be trapped in the law, and his association will cooperate with the law enforcement forces to take action. The strictest.
Mr. Ley Sopheap continued that online business people as well as network marketers can also fall into the trap of scammers without realizing it if they do not have a clear understanding of the law and can also face. The law is the same as the first scam, because "no one does not know the law."
Not only that, it also affects their own health, the health of the people who buy their products to use, making them lose confidence in themselves as sellers of products through online marketing. Apart from this, it also leads to causing problems to society.
He said that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister has made great efforts to make the country peaceful, stable and developed in all areas, such as the network marketing sector is also growing significantly. Well.
Of course, during the Industrial Revolution 4.0 in this era, the network marketing business as well as online business in Cambodia has grown a lot, especially on Facebook, but they do not understand the legal process or Problems related to their business are the cause of the opportunity for the crooks who always cheat others.
Therefore, as the private sector, an important development partner of the Royal Government, Dr. Ley Sopheap has volunteered to help train network marketers in Cambodia to gain legal knowledge and other related knowledge. The government has already announced the implementation of the e-commerce law.
The public sees this as an extraordinary opportunity for all network marketers in Cambodia, but if they do not seize the opportunity to receive training, they will reap many consequences in the future. After all, because the law has already been put into force and the measures for crimes will be strictly enforced, whether the perpetrators are conscious or unconscious, they will still be punished.
