Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi continued that in particular, to show the deeper and more effective cooperation between the two institutions in implementing the guidelines of the Royal Government as set out in the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 for employment growth, equity and efficiency to build infrastructure. Towards realizing the vision of Cambodia in 2050.
According to the Minister, the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy focuses on strengthening gender equality as a priority in the fourth corner of the first Rectangle on Human Resource Development. Empowering women in leadership at both the national and sub-national levels, both at the political and professional levels.
In addition, it continues to promote gender mainstreaming in development policies and plans in all areas, sectors and levels. This is the additional confirmation of Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi.
At the same time, the Minister of Women's Affairs also stated that the Ministry of Women's Affairs and the Ministry of Public Service are important partners and have worked closely together in the past, which has led to significant progress on gender equality in the field of public functions, including Women's participation in civil service and leadership.
Understand that the MoU aims to promote gender equality and empower women in the field of civil service in line with the Rectangular Strategy:
* National Strategic Development Plan * Neary Rattanak Strategic Plan * Public Administration Reform Program * Public Financial Reform Program * Decentralization and Deconcentration Reform Program * Gender Mainstreaming Strategic Plan in the field of public functions and the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals.
