Senior officials of the Ministry of Interior urge Kandal provincial authorities to tighten traffic laws
(Kandal): General Yun Chhunny, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, instructed the leaders at all levels to continue to strengthen the road safety working group at the municipal, district, commune and sangkat levels, especially to strengthen the implementation of the law according to the action plan and work program. Which has been set up on a regular basis with transparency, ensuring the provision of services to the people.
This statement was made on the occasion of General Yun Chhunny's participation in the meeting to review the implementation of the Land Traffic Action Plan for Kandal Province 2019 on November 25, 2019.
At the same time, Dr. Mao Phirun, Governor of Kandal Province, also mentioned that traffic accidents have become a major challenge of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which has seriously affected the national economy.
He said that while the number of vehicles is increasing steadily, traffic accidents have become a major concern of the Royal Government of Cambodia because this problem still occurs every day, causing deaths, injuries, disabilities and Extreme damage to public and private property, which has severely affected the national economy.
The provincial governor added that traffic accidents are caused by three main factors: first: human factors, second: road factors and third: vehicle factors. In response to this, the Kandal Provincial Administration has issued a call to prevent traffic accidents and has organized a campaign to raise awareness for drivers of all types of vehicles on the road.
It should be noted that according to the report of the Department of Public Works of Kandal Province, in the first nine months of 2019, there were 169 traffic accidents in Kandal Province, a decrease of 7 times compared to the same period in 2018. 119 dead, 4 fewer, 137 seriously injured, 28 fewer, 72 minor injuries, 59 fewer. Chinese state media: "Hong Kong election results are inaccurate and questionable"
