All these factors make my company interested in building dams in Cambodia. And between 2002 and 2018, 16 years, the increase in energy sources in Cambodia has increased about 15 times. "So I am very proud and happy to be involved in the construction of the dam and to bring Chinese technology to build the economic development as well as the dam."
The reason why this big company dares to invest more in building a new dam in Cambodia is because Cambodia is transparent and fair in bidding for projects that are trusted by investors.
"The bidding was really transparent and fair because before we built the dam, we studied first and other companies studied first, so we submitted that study to the Electricity of Cambodia or the government. As a judge, so overall, the process is fair and transparent. And in the process of learning, we have to write reports and research technical specifications to be compared.
"Between our company and EDC, there is a fair agreement on the purchase and supply of energy, and with other companies there is the same, so we are fair and transparent with the purchase and sale of electricity."
"It has been a long time since President Mao, who has had close ties to Cambodia, has had a long-standing friendship with the Cambodian leadership as well as the Chinese leadership. Second, I have seen Cambodia's progress during this period remarkable, while China has a one-lane, one-belt policy.
This policy has encouraged investors to have the opportunity to contribute to building Cambodia. "Third, Huaneng Group is a company that has a lot of experience in building dams, has contributed to building our country to produce up to 400 megawatts, which can supply our country more than 20 percent of total energy."
Because Cambodia complies with BOT standards, which means construction, processing and repatriation. Therefore, even if the investment is made at a cost of hundreds of millions of dollars, all companies investing in the dam must return it to the Cambodian government in accordance with the contract between the company and the Cambodian government, which does not exceed 45 years. No.
