During the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth extended a warm welcome and expressed his deep gratitude to Mr. Lyu Xinhua and his accompanying delegation for taking the time to visit Cambodia.
Subsequent visits by Chinese high-level delegations to Cambodia have marked the remarkable progress of the friendship and cooperation between our two countries, which is being strengthened and expanded day by day.
He said that at present, in terms of economic and financial relations with Cambodia, China ranks first in many areas, such as investment, bilateral trade and tourism. Meanwhile, the amount of cooperation financing from the Government of the People's Republic of China to the Royal Government of Cambodia, both concessional loans and grant financing, also ranks first.
Mr. Lyu Xinhua informed Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth that the South-South Cooperation Council of the People's Republic of China was established in 2014 and is an institution under the auspices of the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
The council is a bridge between Chinese companies and institutions with companies and institutions of developing countries, with the function of promoting cooperation between China and developing countries in many fields: politics, economy, trade, culture, education. Science, technology and so on.
While Cambodia is one of the closest friends of China and our two countries have traditionally enjoyed good relations, especially the excellent relationship between Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Xi Jinping, President of the People's Republic of China, the Chinese government supports Fully and encourage more Chinese companies to invest in Cambodia.
At the same time, Lyu Xinhua believes that investing in human resources plays an important role and a key factor in supporting and promoting sustainable economic growth. In this regard, the Council for the Promotion of South-South Cooperation of the People's Republic of China also encourages Chinese companies to invest in projects to establish international schools in Cambodia to help train children and youth in Cambodia.
In response, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth emphasized that Cambodia and China are strategic partners in all fields and partners in building a single destiny community. The level of cooperation between our two countries today has reached an unprecedented level.
For foreign direct investment, hundreds of Chinese companies have registered to invest in Cambodia each year with billions of dollars in investment capital. The Royal Government of Cambodia welcomes more new investment projects from China, as Cambodia still has many potential investment opportunities.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth expressed his deep gratitude to the Chinese government and people for their support to the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia. Chinese investment projects have made a significant contribution to Cambodia's development and contributed to Cambodia's high and sustainable economic growth, as well as job creation and income generation to support the livelihoods of the Cambodian people.
