(Pursat): Officials of CamControl Branch in Pursat Province, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce and local authorities, this morning, November 25, 2019, disseminated education and inspected food products displayed at Samaki Krakor Market in Anlong Village. Tnaot, Krakor district, Pursat province, as a result, no food, cakes or food containing banned chemicals were found.
Mr. TOCH Chao Koy, President of CamControl Branch in Pursat Province, said that during the inspection, the experts conducted preliminary tests on noodles, noodles, noodles, palm sugar, vinegar, sausages and packaged goods, and as a result, no banned chemicals were found. No food or packaging was found, but officials also confiscated 12 expired bottles of Coca-Cola, equivalent to 5.5 kilograms, and destroyed them.
Mr. Toch Chao Koy added that the team also educated and educated traders on food safety by distributing and posting posters and instructing traders on hygiene, organizing goods and selling in an orderly manner. According to the type of food and other consumer goods placed separately, avoid the display of expired goods, canned cans, corrugated iron and goods containing banned chemicals.
