Minister Say Sam Al: We work together to improve the economy and livelihood of local communities to effectively manage and conserve natural resources
(Siem Reap): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, said that we must work together to increase the economy and improve the living standards of the people to another level in order to increase the efficiency of managing and conserving natural resources for future generations. More.
Mr. Say Sam Al made this remark at the invitation of him to chair the forum on "Protection and Conservation of Nature" organized by the General Department of Local Communities of the Ministry of Environment on November 25, 2019 in the province. Siem Reap.
Mr. Say Sam Al emphasized: “Communities have an important role to play in joining local authorities at all levels at the local level to protect and conserve natural resources, and this participation is an honor for the whole nation and for the legacy of future generations. " The Minister also encouraged the authorities, development partners and communities to work together to organize eco-tourism services to attract more tourists.
He said that Cambodia has rich natural resources and biodiversity. Forests cover about 50% of the country, the highest rate in Southeast Asia. To date, the Royal Government has increased the area of protected areas under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Environment to about 41% of the country, equivalent to about 7.2 million hectares, making Cambodia the second largest in Asia after Bhutan.
"Ecotourism and payment plans for ecological services can also provide opportunities for the development of economic activities, while also supporting conservation work," said Say Sam Al.
To achieve this goal, Mr. Say Sam Al highlighted the priority activities that contribute to community development to better contribute to the protection and conservation of natural resources in Cambodia, including the improvement of community life in protected areas by creating conditions. To ensure food security, nutrition, health promotion, education of the children of the community who have completed the 12th grade and received vocational training and continue to higher education.
Mr. Say Sam Al said that the Ministry of Environment will work with relevant partners to prevent and eliminate communicable diseases from community areas, protected areas for the well-being of the people. He stressed that the Ministry of Environment supports the development of infrastructure, providing new employment options for community members to increase income, which contributes to reducing pressure on existing natural resources.
The Minister added that the Ministry will organize the development and conservation of heritage sites, which will help the community to be more active and important in the protection and conservation of temples, historical sites, beliefs, customs, religious traditions of indigenous peoples as well as the people. Cambodia is in a nature reserve.
Cambodia's nature reserves embed a rich cultural heritage that provides attractions for nature tourism and exploration. At the same time, work to strengthen and expand ecotourism services that encourage sustainable development and transform the lives of communities through the establishment of potential ecotourism services in protected areas.
It should be noted that the forum on "Protection and Conservation of Nature" was held under the theme "Commitment and local ownership to ensure the sustainable use of natural resources" with the participation of the leadership of the Ministry of Environment, representatives of ministries and institutions. Involved the governor of the North Tonle Sap Provincial Board of Governors, local authorities, the armed forces and many communities.
The organization of this forum is part of responding to the strategic goal of the Royal Government of Cambodia in mainstreaming and raising the awareness of the people in the communities, protected areas and other local communities to participate in preventing resource crime. Nature as well as strengthening the role of local communities in participating in the protection and conservation of natural resources and improving livelihoods by increasing the interests of local communities.
A group of US investors looking for investment opportunities in tourism in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): A group of investment and tourism delegates intervened from Los Angeles, California, USA to seek investment opportunities in tourism, energy and other sectors in Cambodia, while the investment environment in this peaceful country is providing favorable conditions for all business people and investors. .
After meeting with some ministries and institutions, this group of investment and tourism delegation paid a courtesy call and discussed with Mr. Tith Chantha, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Tourism and Mr. So Mara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism at the Ministry of Tourism this morning. November 25, 2019.
After the discussion, Mr. So Visothy, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, told Fresh News that in the above discussion, the leaders of the Ministry of Tourism informed about the progress in the tourism sector as well as the policy and long-term vision of the Royal Government of Cambodia and The Ministry of Tourism in developing this priority sector to grow and aim to turn Cambodia into an international tourist destination with high attractiveness.
Mr. Sovisothy said that the leadership of the Ministry of Tourism presented the environment and policies to encourage investment in tourism, such as the introduction of policies and encourage the establishment of sacred sites, Second Home and Sustainable tourism development policy in line with the concept of "clean and green".
According to Sovisothy, major US investment companies have shown great interest in Cambodia's tourism potential, rapid development, and Cambodia's long-term vision of achieving an estimated 7 million tourist arrivals by 2020 and about 15 million. People in 2030 who need to invest in infrastructure, tourism products, as well as human resources in tourism.
At this point, the leadership of the Ministry of Tourism stressed that in order to achieve this vision, Cambodia needs to invest in the development of new tourism products and connect infrastructure as well as more direct flights.
The Ministry of Tourism has highlighted the attractive potential of Cambodia's major tourist destinations, such as Phnom Penh, Siem Reap - Angkor, the coastal region - the Southwest Zone and the Northeast Zone, which are in need of investment to develop more new tourism products.
At the same time, the group of investors from the United States also expressed their intention to invest in high-end hotels, investment in the energy sector, especially energy that does not harm the environment, such as solar energy and hydrogen-powered vehicles.
They also expressed their desire to help increase the flow of tourists from the United States to Cambodia, as in 2018, Cambodia received more than 250,000 tourists from the United States, ranking sixth in the number of international tourists. Ten countries visited Cambodia, and in the first nine months of 2019, more than 170,000 tourists from the United States ranked sixth.
Mr. Sovisothy added that the leadership of the Ministry of Tourism also informed about the policy to facilitate travel and visa facilitation for tourists of Cambodian descent from the United States.
