(Kampong Speu): Police in Kampong Speu province, under the command of Major General Sam Samoun, arrested five Cambodian and Vietnamese suspects in connection with a case of using a drilling machine to drill for marble in the sanctuary. Environment without proper permits.
Nhem Sao, Deputy Police Commissioner of Kampong Speu Province, confirmed to Fresh News on November 25, 2019 that the five suspects were: three Cambodians and two Vietnamese. The suspects were arrested for illegally stealing natural resources in Kbal Damrey village, Trapeang Chor commune, Oral district, Kampong Speu province.
Mr. Nhem Sao described that on October 18, 2019, three Vietnamese and a Cambodian man used a drilling machine to drill in the Ministry of Environment's environmental sanctuary without permission to explore natural resources. Marble.
Then recently, anti-corruption organizations saw such activities and reported to the authorities. The suspects then dismantled the drilling equipment and stored it at the home of a villager named Chhorn Thul, who lived more than a kilometer from the drilling site.
Kampong Speu Deputy Police Commissioner said that after hiding the drilling equipment, three Vietnamese suspects fled to Phnom Penh, leaving one suspect named Tin Sith. The suspect, Tin Sith, was detained by the police and told to contact his accomplices.
Later, on November 25, 2019, two Cambodians and two Vietnamese people went to retrieve the drilling equipment hidden at Chhorn Thul's house in Kampong Speu province and were arrested by the authorities. .
Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources calls on people to take care of existing water sources and not waste water
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Nhen Kuon, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, through Fresh News on November 25, 2019, called on people all over the province to take care of existing resources. And use water properly, that is, do not waste water, such as pumping fish.
Mr. Nhen Kuon also pointed out that in the main reservoirs, the water was closed, that is, in 2019, after the end of the rain, the department closed the water in the main reservoirs, so we have full water in the main reservoirs to Get ready for the future.
However, while the reservoir is full of water, Mr. Nhen Kuon requested the people to follow the Royal Government's circular: dry rice can not be done a second time and be used sparingly. Do not waste it, avoid water shortages in the future because we have a long time, from November 2019 to May 2020, which is 7 months that we all need to be careful.
Mr. Nhen Kuon said that for Oddar Meanchey province, there is no concern about the shortage of water because the reservoir as well as other natural water sources are still full, so he thinks that for Oddar Meanchey province is not Not too worried. However, he said that except for a small number of areas, it could be a challenge if his people do not think long and hard, such as pumping ponds and catching fish.
Along with the issues mentioned above, Mr. Nhen Kuon also requested the people to know how to maintain the existing water source well and not waste water. German Environment Agency: "NATO military exercises kill many marine animals and affect the environment"
