(Phnom Penh): November 25, 2019 is the 14th anniversary of Cambodia's large-scale shadow theater being inscribed on UNESCO's Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity list on November 25, 2005.
Theatrical art has a long history and a long history in the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia, is universally recognized and valued as a great human treasure and is included in the World Heritage List of Intangible and Intangible Heritage. Of Humanity in 2005 by UNESCO, which is a glorious national pride invaluable.
Big skin theater is an art that has a history when Brahmanism came to Cambodia. In the past, this type of art was only seen performing in two or three ceremonies a year and was rarely performed in public. These ceremonies include the Khmer New Year, the King's birthday and the coronation, or in the worship of famous figures.
(Kyung Yu): Honorary Dr. Khuon Sodary highlighted the value of culture by promoting multiculturalism as the foundation of peace, development, interconnection and innovation to promote peace and sustainable development.
She made the remarks while she co-chaired and gave a closing speech at the "Gyeongyu World Culture Expo 2019" in Gyeongju, Republic of Korea on the evening of November 24, 2019.
She pointed out that this event took place for 45 days from October 11 to November 24, 2019 with high success and professionalism.
She added that the Gyeongju World Culture Expo aims to contribute to the promotion of multiculturalism, focusing on the role of culture as a source of peace, harmony, development, connectivity, innovation and innovation.
She praised and congratulated the location of the cultural exhibition of Kyungyu, a historical site surrounded by relics and historical cultural sites in the ancient city of Seila, which dates back to the Angkorian period, during the 1st to 10th centuries. .
In particular, the exhibition provides an opportunity for people to better understand the value of culture. "Culture not only plays a role in promoting peace, stability, but also an important economic driver for sustainable development through tourism and innovation. It is a source of innovation and innovation and a source of humanity," she said. And human identity.
Before concluding her speech, she called for joint efforts to preserve cultural and historical heritage, integrate technological advances into cultural preservation and develop cultural corridors for peace and sustainable development.
Please be informed that the 45-day Gyeongyu World Culture Expo 2019 will feature art performances and mixed exhibitions from 27 countries and a total of half a million visitors.
Cambodia and Korea co-hosted the Angkor-Gyeongyu World Culture Fair in Siem Reap from November 21, 2006 to January 9, 2007, with the participation of more than 30 countries and more than one million tourists. In the field of conservation, Korea has been actively involved in the efforts to preserve ancient temples, especially the successful completion of the project to preserve and restore the Preah Pito and Elephant Terrace in the Angkor Thom temple complex.
