Official: 9 months this year, traffic accident in Kampot province caused 46 deaths and 242 injuries
(Kampot): In the first nine months of 2019, there were 192 traffic accidents in Kampot province, in which 46 people were killed, 137 were seriously injured and 105 were slightly injured. This is according to Mr. Chin Kuong, Director of the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport and Chairman of the Secretariat of the Kampot Provincial Road Safety Commission.
This official said this on the occasion of the Kampot Provincial Road Safety Sub-Committee to celebrate the 14th International Day of Remembrance for the victims of road accidents on the morning of November 24, 2019.
Kampot Provincial Governor Chiao Tai said that traffic accidents are a challenge in the process of national development and poverty reduction, as well as affecting security, order and traffic safety on public roads. According to the data of the Secretariat of the Provincial Road Safety Commission, the situation of road traffic accidents in Kampot Province is declining from year to year.
The provincial governor considered this important day as a reflection of the activities of joining the National Committee for Road Safety in preventing and reducing traffic accidents that are constantly increasing every year. At the same time, the provincial governor also thanked the provincial sub-committee on road safety, organizations and private companies that have supported the material, budget and spirit in the past, especially in organizing the program now.
He also called on national and international organizations, donors, local and foreign private companies, as well as other partners, to support the Kampot Provincial Road Safety Sub-Committee with more budget, materials and techniques to enable Successful implementation of the National Road Safety Committee's 8-point action plan for maximum efficiency.
In particular, do not let children under 6 years old and let pets kept on the road in case of accident, parents or guardians of children or owners of those pets. Right before the law in force.
