Mr. Long Dimanche: Cambodia and South Korea are seeking to enhance their comprehensive strategic partnership (Video inside) (Busan, South Korea): Mr. Long Dimanche, Cambodian Ambassador to South Korea, affirmed that Cambodia and South Korea Tbong has been exploring the possibility of raising the level of relations to a comprehensive strategic partnership to expand the potential of cooperation, investment and trade.
Cambodia and South Korea were officially established on October 30, 1997. The establishment of relations between the two countries took place after the visit of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen to South Korea in 1996. The visit is an important one in exploring the possibility of establishing historic diplomatic ties with South Korea.
Relations between Cambodia and South Korea over the past 22 years have grown steadily and have brought significant benefits to the national economy between the two countries.
Long Dimanche affirmed that a strategic partnership between the two countries will be made in the near future to further enhance cooperation, investment and trade between the two countries.
The Cambodian Ambassador to South Korea saw that the expansion of comprehensive strategic partnership with South Korea would bring Cambodia even greater benefits from such good relations, such as investment and trade. Karma and experience on technological development.
According to Long Dimanche, Cambodia currently receives more than $ 4 billion from South Korea in the textile, agriculture, real estate and construction sectors. Of the 214 investment projects, 123 invested in factories with a capital of $ 486 million, creating about 80,000 jobs.
The trade volume between Cambodia and South Korea is nearly 1 billion US dollars. Of that, Cambodia's exports to South Korea account for about 30 percent and South Korea imports about 70 percent.
Cambodian goods exported to South Korea are mostly garments, electronics, footwear, beverages, rubber bags, medicines, cardboard and some agricultural products.
Cambodian goods imported from South Korea include textiles, cars, beverages, electronics, machinery, home decor, medicines, soaps and plastic products.
Through the excellent relations between Cambodia and South Korea, South Korea has contributed to providing employment to many Cambodians.
From 2007 to 2019, a total of 66,565 Cambodian workers were sent to work in South Korea with a salary between $ 1,500 and $ 3,000. About $ 600 million was sent from South Korea to Cambodia through the wages of these workers, a contribution to Cambodia's economic development. Legal Awareness: Provisional Detention
(Phnom Penh): In the current situation of society, when there is a crime of a serious nature, the perpetrators may be arrested immediately or can be detained to ensure order. Or there are more serious consequences from that offense.
However, not every time a crime occurs, the decision of the commune must be made, that is, the status of the crime as well as the situation of the person who committed the crime must be studied first to avoid that the decision of detention will May infringe on their individual rights and freedoms. So how can detention be done in accordance with legal procedures?
In order to better understand this procedure, Fresh News' Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, would like to raise the topic of "Provisional Detention" to the following students:
Pre-trial detention is a procedure that takes place before the trial, while the criminal case is in the hands of the investigating judge. Provisional detention may be made in criminal or misdemeanor cases where the law provides for imprisonment for a term equal to one (1) year or more.
Pursuant to Article 205 of the Code of Criminal Procedure of the Kingdom of Cambodia, pretrial detention may be ordered when such pretrial detention is necessary:
1. To end the crime or prevent the crime from happening again. To prevent oppression of witnesses or victims or to prevent reconciliation between the accused and his accomplices. To keep material evidence or clues. To ensure the retention of the accused to the court to deal with the procedure. To protect the security of the accused. To ensure public order, not to cause chaos caused by crime.
Pre-trial detention can usually be made on the initiative of the investigating judge or on the prosecutor's conclusion, based on the consideration of a direct understanding of the defendant's personality or the actual circumstances of the crime committed. .
When the investigating judge decides on the provisional detention, it shall be made through a "provisional detention order" which must be immediately notified to the prosecutor and the accused. For the duration of pre-trial detention, the Code of Criminal Procedure of the Kingdom of Cambodia is determined separately according to the situation of the accused (juvenile or juvenile) or the nature of the offense (misdemeanor or felony).
1. Defendant as a juvenile The duration of pretrial detention shall be determined as follows:
2. Defendant as a minor, the duration of pretrial detention shall be determined as follows:
The investigating judge may decide to hand over the minor to the parents or guardians, or in the absence of the guardians, to hand over to the Provisional Education Center pending a court decision (Article 212 of the Code of Criminal Procedure) and Article 39, paragraph 2 of The Juvenile Justice Act states that minors under the age of 14 are not in pretrial detention.
In the event that a juvenile in custody is found to be under the age of 14, the investigating judge shall issue a Closing Order, release the accused and order the immediate release of the minor, despite the appeal of the prosecutor, and return the juvenile to Representatives designated by law.
In summary, pretrial detention is a procedure carried out at the stage of the investigating judge, which is decided either by the initiative of the investigating judge or by the prosecutor's conclusion, with consideration of The status of the accused or the nature of the offense. The decision to remand the detainee was made to maintain order, ensure the smooth and accurate proceedings and to prevent any adverse effects from the detainee.
Cambodia hosts commendation for having the best World Patent Championship
(Phnom Penh): The first hosting of the 17th World Youth and Women's Patent Championships in Cambodia has been hailed by international delegations and athletes as the most well-organized event. The most they have ever participated in the past. This was confirmed by Mr. Sok Sabayna, Secretary General of the Cambodian Bowls and Patents Federation.
This confirmation coincides with the closing ceremony of the historical event last night after a tough five-day match from November 19-23 at the National Stadium. The closing ceremony was held in the presence of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, and Mr. Claude Azema, President of the World Bowls and Patents Federation, as well as delegates from 49 countries.
The Secretary General of the same federation stated that winning four consecutive gold medals by the heroine Ke Leng while hosting Cambodia is a great source of pride for the federation and the nation as a whole. But at the same time, the leaders of the federation are even happier after the event was organized smoothly and successfully, especially to receive the praise of the delegates and the participants - the country is the best organized.
"Apart from recognizing the Cambodian patent team as one of the world's patent powers, many delegates also praised Cambodia's organization and hosting for the first time," he said. "Personally, tell me that this is the first time that they have participated in such a well-organized world event. Accommodation, food, travel and match arrangements from our youth volunteer team are of international standard."
It should be noted that in the result of a tough five-day competition with 49 countries participating, the Thai team took the first place with 2 gold and 1 bronze medal, while the second place went to the French Republic, winning 1 gold medal and 2 bronze medals. The three hosts, Cambodia, won one gold and one bronze medal, while Laos came in fourth, three silver and Monaco won one silver and fifth. Athletes from Spain, Madagascar, Myanmar and China also won a bronze medal.
