The new era of Cambodian tourism is ecotourism and community tourism, opening investment opportunities for all investors
(Phnom Penh): Seeing the trend of tourists who visit eco-tourism and community tourism remarkably, the Royal Government of Cambodia is firmly committed to supporting the private sector and all investors who want to Invest in ecotourism and community tourism.
This seems to indicate that in addition to cultural tourism, which has a high potential to attract tourists, ecotourism and community tourism have been opening a new era in promoting tourism in Cambodia to continue to grow.
To develop sustainable, responsible and equitable ecotourism and community-based tourism, the Royal Government recently launched a national policy on ecotourism as well as community-based tourism.
In addition, the Ministry of Tourism also held the 2nd Cambodia Tourism Investment Forum under the theme "Determining the Stages for Growth" for 2 days from 21-22 November 2019 at Sofitel Phnom Penh Phuket to highlight the opportunity Many investments in tourism, especially ecotourism and community tourism, as well as sacred tourism areas to investors, business and national-international private sector.
This important forum was also attended by representatives of various ministries, institutions, national and international speakers to come and explain, as well as to present policies related to the infrastructure of electricity and energy that serve the tourism sector and needs. Other.
After the forum, Mr. Thong Ratsak, Director General of Tourism Development and International Cooperation, said that the forum presented to investors and the private sector in the tourism sector that Cambodia's major tourist destinations are Phnom Penh, Siem Reap-Angkor, coastal areas and The Northeast region still has great potential, but it is not enough to meet the needs of tourists today.
He said that Cambodia must have more ecotourism and community tourism sites scattered throughout the country, especially to develop existing tourism communities to be more attractive.
Mr. Thong Rathsak continued that the efforts to encourage active investment is to achieve the goal "Cambodia will receive about 6.6 million international tourists in 2019 and by 2020 to receive about 7 million. Earned $ 4.375 million, not including the number of tourists in the country.
Due to the increase in the number of domestic tourists, the Ministry of Tourism has forecast that in 2019, the number of domestic tourists will reach about 11 million with an additional revenue of about 2 billion US dollars.
