Siem Reap Provincial Authority Celebrates 14th International Day of Remembrance for Traffic Accident Victims
(Siem Reap): This morning, November 24, 2019, in Sotnikum District, Siem Reap Province, the 14th International Day of Commemoration of Road Traffic Victims was celebrated under the chairmanship of Mr. Pin Prak, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province and Deputy Chairman. Siem Reap Provincial Road Safety Commission, with the participation of leaders of departments, units, district authorities, government officials, students and more than 525 people.
Mr. Ky Virin, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport and Head of the Secretariat of the Siem Reap Provincial Road Safety Sub-Committee, confirmed that the road traffic accident data in Siem Reap for the first 10 months of 2019 was 74 cases, an increase of 16 cases. There were 206 accidents (81 females), resulting in 74 deaths (18 females), 42 serious injuries (21 females) and 90 minor injuries (38 females).
He added that the report shows that in the last 10 months, the number of traffic accidents has increased significantly.
He estimated that on average in Siem Reap, two people die each week in traffic accidents, which is a challenge to national development, people's well-being, affects the government's poverty reduction policy and leaves many consequences. Others in the society seem to have created tragedy, leaving orphans, widows and the disabled.
Mr. Pin Prak said that the celebration of this day is the bell ringing again of the Royal Government of Cambodia with the promulgation of the newly amended road traffic law to warn road users and pedestrians. All kinds must change the behavior that does not respect the law to adopt a attitude of neutrality and respect for traffic laws when traveling and driving.
