Takeo Armed Forces seize nearly 100 kilos of dried marijuana
(Takeo): Takeo Provincial Gendarmerie raided a marijuana plantation in the Bayongkor Valley, confiscating nearly 100 kilograms of dried marijuana and destroying some marijuana plants.
The seizure of marijuana took place on the morning of November 23, 2019 at the Kancheng waterfall on the ridge of Bayong Kor mountain, Chheuteal Phlos village, Sre Ampok commune, Kirivong district.
Brigadier General Lalay, Commander of the Takeo Provincial Gendarmerie, said that his forces had raided a cannabis plantation in the area, with the coordination of the Takeo Provincial Prosecutor, and confiscated 15 dried marijuana. A 98-kg bag was seized and a 28-year-old suspect, Them Na, and a white Highlander were destroyed with more than 4,000 marijuana plants.
Gen. Lalay said his force was currently building a case to send the suspects and exhibits to court for legal action.
It should be noted that the Bayong Kor area in Kirivong district, Takeo province, has been the site of illegal marijuana cultivation for decades, and despite the efforts of the authorities to crack down, the perpetrators continue to steal and sell it in Vietnam. A kilo of dried marijuana sells for about $ 500. Scholarship students from New Zealand will attend the 8th Scholarship Conference to highlight the key to getting a scholarship abroad
