The new school building in Hun Sen Chamnan Leu High School is 80% completed
(Kampong Thom): The principal of Hun Sen Chamnal Leu High School claimed that from now on, there will be a lack of room for students to study, even though the school has reached the high school level, because the new building has 2 floors and 12 rooms, donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. The Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit have achieved more than 80%.
This was confirmed by Mr. Thean Vuthea, Principal of Hun Sen Chamna Leu High School on the occasion of Mr. Chea Chanto, Permanent Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the National Working Group for Stong District. On November 22, 2019.
Mr. Thean Vuthea said that at the secondary school level, there was no shortage of classrooms, but at the high school level, there was a lack of classes for students who were forced to divide their study into two shifts, but now it is no longer as difficult as before. Because the school building, which is a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, has achieved more than 80%.
The Director expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, including Mr. Chea Chanto, who reported this shortcoming to Samdech Techo in a timely manner.
Mr. Chea Chanto said that all the achievements today are not accidental, but due to the efforts and efforts of the Royal Government, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has worked hard to build peace until now. Therefore, let the people work together to maintain this existing peace.
Mr. Chea Chanto called on students to study hard to become a knowledgeable resource for the development of a more prosperous nation.
For the new school year, Mr. Chea Chanto brought books, pens, pencils, sarongs and budgets, which are the precious gifts of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to distribute to a total of 659 teachers and students. . Murderer who killed a female garment worker in Svay Rieng province jumped into the water to kill himself
(Svay Rieng): The killer who strangled a factory worker on November 22, 2019, was confirmed by Svay Rieng provincial police to jump into the water and commit suicide.
The body of the killer was found by residents and authorities at a lake east of the TY factory in Doeum Po village, Kandeang Reay commune, Svay Teap district at 11:30 on November 23, 2019.
Svay Rieng provincial police said that the man who killed the woman yesterday jumped into the water and was found this morning. The killer was named Neang Krem, 25 years old, living in Prey Keav village, Kampong Chak commune, Romduol district, Svay Rieng province.
It should be noted that on the morning of November 22, 2019, at the point of Roch Kathy White, the production of amulets in Doeum Po village, Kandeang Reay commune, Svay Teap district, Svay Rieng province, there was a case of murder of a factory woman by using a knife to cut vegetables. The woman was stabbed 14 times and died at the scene.
Police said that after careful research, police have identified the suspect as the killer of the victim and the suspect is the victim's girlfriend.
The murder was caused by the suspect, Neang Krem, 25, of Romduol district, who was the girlfriend of the victim, Khem Pisal, 24, of Sangke village, Chheu Teal commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province. Authorities said that the reason why the suspect killed the victim was his girlfriend because the woman's family refused to marry.
Sources said that immediately after receiving the information, Brigadier General Koy Sopheap, Deputy Provincial Police Commissioner in charge of Criminal Affairs, Director of the Bureau of Serious Crimes, Scientific Inspector, Deputy Inspector of Svay Teap District, doctors surrounded and examined the bodies to identify the relevant targets.
The same source said that the suspect fled the scene after the action. After examining the body, with the approval of the Brigadier General, Deputy Commissioner of Criminal Planning, the body was handed over to Mr. Khem Hun, the father of the body, for a traditional ceremony.
