Mr. Neth Pheaktra: "National Environmental Sanitation Day" 2019 was held nationwide
(Phnom Penh): "National Environmental Sanitation Day" for 2019 under the theme "Clean, Healthy Village" was held in the framework of Cambodia on November 23, with places to celebrate this day in the capital. Large public participation.
This was stated by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Environment on November 23, 2019 from Ratanakkiri Province, where he and government officials of the Ministry of Environment joined in celebrating Environmental Sanitation Day with Mr. Thong Savun Rattanakiri Provincial Governor, Mr. Nab Bunheng, Chairman of Rattanakiri Provincial Council and more than 1,000 government officials, citizens, youth and students.
The Secretary of State said that in order to ensure the quality of the environment, the beauty of the city and public health, we all need to pay attention to improve the proper management of waste by being able to pack and sort waste such as organic waste. Can be recycled such as paper or plastic and hazardous waste and other waste to turn some waste into economic value and reduce the amount of waste in landfills.
The amount of urban waste generated is more than 10,000 tons per day and the amount of waste generated by Cambodia is about 4 million tons per year, of which 60% is organic waste, 20% of this waste is 9% of plastic bag waste is paper waste and the rest is solid waste and other waste.
According to Mr. Net Pheaktra, the Ministry of Environment has been working to spread the word about the environment to people all over the country, directly and through the media. As a result, people are more aware of the environment, more involved in environmental sanitation, and more committed to environmental causes and natural resources.
"To keep Cambodia clean, a clean environment requires the participation of all," he said. "People should consider the city, town and other places where people live, work and do business as our homes and need to clean regularly to maintain the beauty and promote public welfare."
This National Environmental Sanitation Day will mobilize people from all walks of life to participate in sanitation, as well as inspire the movement to participate in environmental sanitation in public places by putting them in the right bins and planting trees to be green, fresh and comfortable. . At the same time, the celebration of Environmental Sanitation Day will change the attitudes and behaviors of people in the use of plastic products is very important.
