APSARA Authority is very worried about illegal constructions that are built against the permit
(Siem Reap): After receiving permission to renovate or dismantle an old house, build a new house instead of the residents, renovate the house or dismantle the old house, build a new house instead of the permit, which makes their construction Illegal construction.
Long Kosal, a spokesman for the APSARA Authority, said that many illegal structures were being built legally after residents of the Angkor resort received legal building permits from the APSARA Authority.
He stressed that the arrangement of housing in the area of Angkor World Heritage Site must be consistent and part of the promotion of heritage value, so all construction requests need to apply for a permit in advance and it is necessary to build in accordance with the permitted content. .
Mr. Long Kosal added that in case people wish to renovate houses, build fences, cowsheds, chicken houses, toilets or other needs of light construction, people can contact the community working group in each village. Village, commune, sangkat.
In particular, in case people wish to demolish old houses and build new ones, they can apply at the service center of APSARA Authority or at the one-stop shop of Puok district, Siem Reap city and Siem Reap provincial hall. All technical inspections and licensing are free of charge.
Therefore, APSARA Authority requests the people living in the Angkor resort area to apply for construction to APSARA Authority by clearly defining the shape and size and to repair or build in accordance with the requested request to avoid Let those buildings become illegal during the repair or construction because they face the void of the permit, eviction and legal measures.
(Phnom Penh): The first Cambodian women's team, including Ke Leng, Ouk Srey Mom, Un Sreyya and Keo Vanna, competed for a place in the semi-finals (1/2) of the World Petanque Championships Youth and For the 17th time, after beating the Vietnamese women's team 13-10 in the last eight of the three-on-three team event on Friday evening at the National Stadium.
