(Phnom Penh): On November 20-21, 2019, at the Cambodiana Hotel, the United Nations Industrial Development Organization (UNIDO) in collaboration with the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts of the Kingdom of Cambodia organized a workshop on the Digitalization and Industrial Revolution of the Second Generation. 4 In order to introduce policy makers to current trends and new policies related to the challenges and opportunities of the Fourth Generation Industrial Revolution (4IR).
This confirmation was made during the meeting between Mr. Patrick Murphy and Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, held at the Ministry of Commerce on the morning of November 22, 2019.
During the meeting, Minister Pan Sosak informed that on November 21, 2019, the Royal Government of Cambodia signed a Memorandum of Understanding with the International Labor Organization (ILO) and the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia on the Better Factories Project in Cambodia to continue to promote Working conditions in the field of garments and textiles that recognize international labor standards.
He said that the implementation of better factory projects in Cambodia is recognized internationally and also attracts investment to create jobs and better income for workers.
At the same time, the Minister also praised the contribution to the strengthening of labor standards by American companies that have invested in Cambodia and also called for more investment in areas that create value and additional skills such as agricultural processing, gem processing. Diamonds, lightweight, electronic, etc.
In response, Patrick Murphy supported the implementation of Cambodia's labor policy, recognizing that maintaining and further raising employment standards in Cambodia also strengthened Cambodia's reputation for attracting more investment.
The Ambassador also agreed on the contribution of American companies in this field, as well as job creation and skills training for Cambodian workers.
The US Ambassador stated that during his brief visit to Cambodia, he saw small and medium enterprises as an important driver in the Cambodian economy.
To support the development of small and medium enterprises in Cambodia, the US Embassy will host a forum on agro-industry in February 2020 and will invite the Ministry of Commerce to participate.
He also said that the US company GE also intends to participate in the energy sector to contribute to the shortage of electricity in Cambodia.
Minister Pan Sosak encouraged American companies and the American Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia to actively participate in the Royal Government and private sector forums to raise challenges for the Royal Government to address in a timely manner. Preah Vihear CamControl Branch Finds Defective and Outdated Goods for Sale in Preah Vihear City
