The Ministry of Interior allows the Human Rights Party to postpone the submission of the list of new leaders for 6 months (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Interior on November 22, 2019 decided to allow the Human Rights Party to postpone Six months to submit a list of new members of its leadership to the Ministry of Interior.
The extension is valid from the date of this notice until June 2020. This is according to the letter from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Minister of Interior, sent to the President of the Human Rights Party, which was received by Fresh News this afternoon.
It should be noted that on October 28, 2019, the Human Rights Party sent a letter to the Ministry of Interior requesting a delay in sending the list of the leaders of the Human Rights Party to the Ministry of Interior for a while after the party's president. Son Soubert asked to resign.
The Human Rights Party was founded by former CNRP President Kem Sokha in 2007. However, in 2012, Kem Sokha decided to unite with the Sam Rainsy Party to form the CNRP, leaving the Human Rights Party as a backbone for Son Soubert as its leader.
The following is a letter from the Ministry of Interior: French, Cambodian and Vietnamese students compete in the "Clean Up in French" creative project
(Phnom Penh): The Institute of Technology of Cambodia, in collaboration with the Agency for Higher Education in French (AUF) in the Asia-Pacific region, has launched the final competition for the 2019 Innovation Project under the theme of Entrepreneurship Towards the “Innovation for Society” project. And solidarity. ”
The 3rd Regional Competition at the Institute of Technology of Cambodia on November 21, 2019 was held with the aim of establishing a relationship between education, training and local socio-economic actors and highlighting many new entrepreneurship projects for students and youth. Recently graduated in French under the age of 35. This is also an opportunity for young people to gain experience on project planning from experts in the field of entrepreneurship.
Please be informed that at the end of August and the beginning of September 2019, 42 outstanding project ideas in the region were selected to participate in the competition and received training and guidance on setting up a company to make the project Their well-organized. Candidates visit companies, attend workshops and exchange with experts who provide a wealth of ideas and experience in designing their business plans.
The last 6 teams competed in the finals on November 21, 2019 in Phnom Penh, including 4 teams from Vietnam and 2 teams in Cambodia. They defended their business plans in French in front of a panel of entrepreneurs.
Mr. Chhun Heang Thavrith, Deputy Director General of the Institute of Technology of Cambodia in charge of International Cooperation, said at the opening ceremony of the final competition on the creation of creative projects: "This competition encourages and encourages students to use the knowledge learned from The university came up with a Start Up project that will enable you to start your own business. "Moreover, they can improve their French speaking skills."
He confirmed that this is a first-ever French-language competition in Cambodia, but other sports competitions other than French have been organized several times by the Institute of Technology of Cambodia in collaboration with other companies.
Please note that as a result of the competition, the first place went to a group of Vietnamese students, the second place went to a group of Cambodian students and the third place went to a group of Vietnamese students. The first place winners were Ms. Nguyen Mi, a student at Hanoi University studying International Relations, and Ms. Nguyen Ngoc Anh Phuong from the Asia Cool project, which recycles garbage from agricultural production.
Ms. Nguyen Ngoc Anh Phuong said that the project in which she competed was a project to process oil into biodegradable and environmentally friendly and convert waste from agricultural products. The purpose of this project is to help the environment and eliminate or reduce plastic.
