(Phnom Penh): A Korean man arrested at Phnom Penh International Airport in connection with the fraud of nearly $ 3 million in victims has been charged by prosecutors with "non-compliance with a commercial instrument" under Article 231 of the Law on Tradable Instruments and Payment Transactions. This is according to a court official told Fresh News on November 22, 2019.
After being charged, on November 22, 2019, the Korean national was sent to an investigating judge for further proceedings under a request for detention from the prosecution.
Park Hye-yong, a 67-year-old Korean man of Cambodian descent, was arrested by Phnom Penh police on the evening of November 20, 2019 at Phnom Penh International Airport.
Authorities said that the Korean scammer recently issued a check to the victims, but the victim filed a complaint to the court to issue an arrest warrant.
According to the decision, water prices will be reduced for subsistence customers (home users) who use no more than 25 cubic meters per month, while consumers with more than 25 cubic meters per month will be charged.
For business customers, the price is kept the same, except for water consumption of more than 15 cubic meters per month or more will be charged. As for customers in ministries, institutions, units and embassies, the price of water will be doubled.
A senior official of the Ministry of Industry told Fresh News that the decision to adjust the water price came after a meeting and detailed discussions between the leaders of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts. .
The same official confirmed that the water sales of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has issued three types of customers, including: customers, livelihood (home users), business customers and customers from ministries, government institutions and embassies.
The new water price adjustment has reduced the price for home users who consume no more than 25 cubic meters of water per month, with the middle and lower average living standards, accounting for more than 59 percent of all home consumers. Meanwhile, customers who consume more than 25 cubic meters of water per month have an above-average standard of living and have a need to use more water than necessary, including use for gardens, swimming pools and so on.
For customers in ministries, state institutions and embassies will have to increase the cost of water supply from 1030 riels per cubic meter to 2,500 riels per cubic meter, which will help strengthen the cost savings of ministries and institutions of the Royal Government.
Please be informed that at present, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has the capacity to produce 560,000 cubic meters per day to supply clean water in Phnom Penh and Kandal Province, as the demand for water is growing every day, which requires new investment. More.
Recently, the Royal Government of Cambodia has just decided to build a new water treatment plant in Sangkat Bak Kheng, Khan Chroy Changva, with the first phase using a budget of 156 million dollars, with a capacity to produce more than 190,000 cubic meters of water per day and the first step. 2 Use more than 140 million dollars, with a capacity of more than 190,000 cubic meters per day.
