(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued a notification on the extension of the application for foreign labor permit (quota) for 2020 to the owner or director of enterprises, establishments until the end of December 2019. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, which was received by the Information Unit on November 22, 2019.
The Ministry of Labor's announcement of the extension comes after it was observed that some owners or directors of enterprises are still late in applying for foreign labor permits (quotas) for 2020. In such a situation, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training would like to inform the owner or director of the establishment that the Ministry has postponed the application for a foreign labor permit (quota) for 2020 until the end of December 2019.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training would like to remind all owners or directors of enterprises and establishments that need to use foreign labor (quota) for 2020 to hurry to apply for permission to use foreign labor before December 31, 2019. Restrictions. Failure to apply for a permit and illegally use foreign labor will be subject to penalties in accordance with Chapter 16 of the Labor Law.
