Lottery Handover Ceremony for 101 Families of Cambodian Veterans Association in Phnom Penh
With regard to the attention of Mr. Khuong Sreng and Mr. Sar Thet, the authorities at all levels have collected data for the veterans in lines 1, 2, 2 to be specific, transparent, and honest so that the members of the association can live properly.
The association is organized into three stages, including: First: to provide landless families who are homeless, he volunteered to be resettled in Oddar Meanchey province. Second, consider the family of the veteran who already has land and a house, but his house is old and dilapidated, he needs to be repaired. Third, the family who has land and he needs to build.
Now Phnom Penh has taken the first priority for a member of the Veterans Association who has no land, no home, and he has applied and volunteered to settle in the province. Construction of houses for 101 veterans and their families in Bak Vek village, Chong Kal commune, Chong Kal district, Oddar Meanchey province.
At the same time, Ms. Mom Chandani said that today is the beginning of the lottery to accept houses, because there are some houses in the corner with the first row and the second row. Therefore, in order to be transparent and honest, the team has put the ballots with numbers to draw lots, and whoever gets the numbers, especially those who get a warm feeling that they have a house to live in.
The director of the department confirmed that the house is ready to build and beautiful, with a house size of 4 meters by 6 meters in land size of 30 meters by 80 meters, with 20 mango trees and a large pond. Considering the cultivable land per family of 2 hectares. In this sense, Samdech Techo took into account the veterans that he has merit for the nation, the people, without leaving them to live alone or homeless.
The Cambodian Veterans Association was established on January 24, 2007, 13 years ago and has a total of 9,318 members. The principle of establishing this association is the direction of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which is chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and implemented by the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, which is the direct staff to help alleviate the burdens of veterans and their families.
Ms. Mom Chandani stated that the team led the families of the veterans to receive the house in Oddar Meanchey before the handover ceremony on Friday, December 6, 2019.
Please note that before achieving the above results, the team of the Department of Social Affairs has visited and prepared many times.
RPF officials: Establishment of pensions for flight attendants, ships, domestic servants to facilitate their aging
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pen Norakvuth, Deputy Director of the National Social Security Fund (NSSF), said that in 2020, the NSSF plans to launch a pension scheme for individuals under Provisions of the Labor Law, including air, sea and domestic workers in Cambodia, should be pensioned as officials in order to alleviate the burden on employees in old age who lack access to income.
Mr. Pen Norakvuth said this on the morning of November 22, 2019, when he chaired the opening of a consultative workshop on the implementation of the "Social Security pension system for individuals under Provisions of the Labor Law, including air and sea personnel as well as domestic workers, ”at the Dara Airport Hotel.
Mr. Pen Norakvuth stated that in the past, the Social Security Administration has launched a joint social security system for occupational risk and health care, and these two regimes have also greatly eased the burden on private sector employees as well as civil servants. In the face of the risks that may arise in the past, in 2020, the UN will establish another social security system for pensions to protect the financial well-being of the elderly and Lack of income.
The Deputy Director of the National Social Security Fund further stated that the establishment of the social security system for pensions is to protect the finances of the elderly by providing a decent income to the people who participate in the pension system by stopping the habit. Raising each other, which increases the burden on the family, thus making the family life of the Cambodian people more carved.
Mr. Pen Norakvuth said that through the introduction of the Rectangular Strategy, Phase 4, Legislature 6, National Social Protection Policy 2016-2025 has made good progress, including the policy of implementing the social security system in Cambodia. It also pays attention to and promotes more effective and efficient improvements aimed at promoting the protection of the well-being and livelihood of the people, especially workers.
