China leads nearly 60 companies and enterprises to understand business in Cambodia
In a press conference after meeting with Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and representatives of Cambodian enterprises at the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce this morning, November 21, 2019, Mr. Lyu Xinhua confirmed to reporters: "I lead a delegation of 24 enterprises and 35 chairmen or people in charge of the company. "This visit focuses on learning about the Cambodian market through investing in Cambodia."
He said that bringing Chinese companies and enterprises to Cambodia is also to provide opportunities, or simply to build a bridge for Chinese enterprises and companies to have the opportunity to know Cambodian enterprises and companies to be able to work together to create investment opportunities. Together.
According to Lyu Xinhua, China's "Belt and Road" initiative has brought great benefits between Cambodia and China. The benefits, he said, are that in addition to strengthening ties between the two countries, Cambodia has achieved good infrastructure development.
"China has long considered Cambodia as its closest and best neighbor," he said. After the Belt and Road Initiative has been launched, Cambodia is considered to be at the heart of this initiative, and this initiative is the most important thing to cooperate in building infrastructure.
"I find it gratifying that after the Belt and Road Initiative is already linked to the Royal Government of Cambodia's policy, there is the greatest change in infrastructure, whether it is roads or bridges," he said. "Importantly, Cambodia's infrastructure has grown tremendously."
Wang Wentian, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, introduced the key points of China-Cambodia bilateral relations, especially the current state of practical cooperation between the two countries, to welcome more Chinese enterprises to invest and create jobs in Cambodia. He also called for in-depth discussions on business investment environment, investment experience and cooperation opportunities with entrepreneurs present here.
It should be noted that the China-South China Cooperation Association was established in August 2014 with the aim of promoting practical cooperation in the fields of economy, culture, education, technology and other fields between China and many developing countries. After the establishment of this association, this is the 14th visit organized for entrepreneurs, and the destination of the location is 3 countries, including Vietnam, Cambodia and the Philippines.
Cambodia-China trade volume in 2018 reached 7.4 billion US dollars, of which Cambodia's exports to China amounted to 1.377 billion US dollars, an increase of 37% and imports amounted to $ 6 billion, an increase of 26%. The two countries have set a new goal of boosting bilateral trade to 10 billion US dollars by 2023.
