Senior Commerce Ministry official: Cambodia will benefit greatly from free trade agreement with China
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Under Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, on November 21, 2019, emphasized that Cambodia will benefit greatly from the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, which will enable Cambodia to export. Bigger than before.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Pen Sovicheat attending a press conference on "Free Trade Agreement between Cambodia and China" organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia at the Office of the Council of Ministers this morning. November 21, 2019.
Explain the question, "Are we concerned about mutual trade that is detrimental to Cambodia because Cambodia is a small country?" "In fact, a small country like Cambodia in ASEAN is a country that will benefit greatly if we do free trade with a big country like China," said Pen Sovichet.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat said that Cambodia is a small market, but a market that China is interested in. And Cambodia is also able to import a large number of agricultural products to China, which in the past could not be fully exported.
The Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of Commerce added that the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement is designed to boost trade between the two countries. He said that China has paid close attention to the Cambodian market, so we are interested in the possibility of Chinese investment in Cambodia.
In fact, this morning, November 21, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the occasion of the inauguration of the "Indra Devi Building" of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Samdech Techo also said that the Royal Government of Cambodia and all development partners must use as much as possible. From Cambodia-China free trade, while Cambodia is currently not used to its full potential.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that today, even within the framework of ASEAN itself, ASEAN has not yet used the full potential of the ASEAN Free Trade Agreement, ASEAN likes to export to other countries, but each country does not do much But Thailand, which has a trade volume with Cambodia of more than $ 6 billion, of which Thailand imports $ 5 billion.
The Cambodian Prime Minister added that about 5 billion US dollars worth of Cambodian trade with Vietnam was also imported into Cambodia, but Cambodia with other partners such as the Philippines, Indonesia, Malaysia, Singapore from Cambodian goods as well as the goods of our Cambodian friends. Do not.
In early December 2019, the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of China are scheduled to hold the first formal talks on exploring the possibility of a free trade agreement between the two countries. China considers the opening of the first formal talks on the feasibility study of a free trade agreement between the two countries to be a special arrangement of the Chinese side based on the friendly relations between China and Cambodia.
Cambodia-China trade volume in 2018 reached 7.4 billion US dollars, of which Cambodia's exports to China amounted to 1.377 billion US dollars, an increase of 37% and imports amounted to $ 6 billion, an increase of 26%. The two countries have set a new goal of boosting bilateral trade to 10 billion US dollars by 2023.
