Senior official of the Ministry of Tourism: Good community, sustainable tourism leads to poverty reduction
(Siem Reap): Ms. Hun Dany, Secretary of State representing Dr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said that a good community, sustainable tourism leads to poverty reduction.
She said this on November 21, 2019 on the occasion of presiding over the opening ceremony of the dissemination workshop on "Women, Community and Tourism" organized by the Ministry of Tourism and the Department of Tourism of Siem Reap. Private, community, tourism and students in the province, a total of more than 250 people.
Speaking at the seminar, the Secretary of State said that the workshop was organized in order to strengthen the role of women in the community to participate in the development of tourism for sustainable growth.
She said the tourism community has been playing an important role in improving the livelihoods and poverty alleviation of local communities by creating employment and income opportunities. Community tourism is considered as an important product contributing to the socio-economic development through tourism service activities that reflect the traditions, lifestyle, cultural preservation and natural resources.
According to a senior official of the Ministry of Tourism, in all these activities, women have also made a significant and potential contribution to providing quality services to support tourism as well as attract more tourists to visit Cambodia.
"While global tourism is growing at around 5% per year, tourism and community ecotourism is growing at about 20% every year," she said. In this sense, community tourism and ecotourism are considered pillars in ensuring the sustainable development of tourism. Ministry of Public Works informs ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations about raising the retirement age of civil servants to 60 years
