The Royal Academy of Cambodia has some development projects to do with the Ministry of Tourism to continue the growth of tourism
(Phnom Penh): In a meeting with Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, Mr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, presented some necessary plans to cooperate with the Ministry of Tourism and other ministries related to the promotion of human resources services, especially strategic plans. Attract tourists to continue to increase the number of tourists visiting Cambodia.
The above meeting was held at the Ministry of Tourism on the evening of November 20, 2019, in the presence of leaders of the Ministry of Tourism and the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
On that occasion, Minister Thong Khon briefed on the current situation in tourism in Cambodia, the region and the world as well as the National Ecotourism Policy, which has just been officially launched for 1-2 days. This and many important policies informed to the delegation of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
The Minister also pointed out some shortcomings and shortcomings to Mr. Sok Touch, along with a number of proposals related to additional human resource training, requests for assistance in strategic tourism development planning.
In response to the above, Mr. Sok Touch stated some objectives:
* First, the Royal Academy of Cambodia would like to increase the training of human resources in the tourism sector with the cooperation of the Ministry of Tourism, the purpose of which is in line with the proposal of the Ministry of Tourism.
* Second, the Royal Academy of Cambodia plans to establish a foreign language translation center for tourists from each country, with the close involvement of the Ministry of Tourism.
* Third: The Royal Academy of Cambodia wants to make a tourism map that shows the various tourist destinations in Cambodia, no matter where you go.
In the fourth point, Mr. Sok Touch also suggested to the Ministry of Tourism that there should be a clear and accurate explanation of each tourist site to tourists and have a direct presentation.
He also mentioned that major tourists need to have local language translations, such as Chinese visitors must have Chinese and Korean languages and scripts, Japanese and other tourists must do the same.
The above remarks of the President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia give the Ministry of Tourism some new ideas to implement better and ready to continue cooperation with the Royal Academy of Cambodia to achieve other achievements. More.
