(Phnom Penh): A delegation of the Ministry of Tourism led by Mr. Ny Phally, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, in collaboration with experts of the World Cycling Federation (UCI), on November 20, 2019, inspected the location and technical work towards Organizing a world cycling event on the coast of Cambodia.
The first world-class cycling event in Cambodia will take place from January 4 to 6, 2020. In this international standard event, the following three-circuit cycling routes will be organized:
Preparatory phase: Held at Darasakor Resort, Koh Kong Province from January 2 to 3, 2020.
Circuit 1: On January 4, 2020, depart from Darasakor resort in Koh Kong province, cross the roundabout on Say Phu Thong Street to Koh Kong provincial town.
Circuit 2: January 5, 2020, departing from Andong Tuek Bridge in Botum Sakor District, crossing the Sre Ambel junction to the Veal Rinh roundabout and continuing to Thansur Bokor Resort, Kampot Province.
Circuit 3: January 6, 2020, departing from the top of Bokor Mountain towards the Duren roundabout in Kampot town, then the White Horse roundabout and ending in front of Kep Provincial Hall.
The Undersecretary of State called on all stakeholders, the private sector and especially the business community and the people on the streets to organize this event to be ready to support, celebrate and watch this great world-class cycling event. Crowds all together.
