Mr. Ung Dipola made this call on November 19, 2019, yesterday in a forum on "Dredging sand along the Bassac River from the Phnom Penh-Kandal border."
Mr. Ing Depola said that the problem of illegal dredging without a license and proper technology has caused the river bank to collapse, which has affected the homes of people living along the river.
Ung Dipola stated that the technical dredging does not cause landslides and does not affect the river, but also helps to deepen the river so that the flow of water can be avoided. The shore.
He also pointed out that the cause of the landslide is because in the middle of the Bassac River is shallow, causing the water to hit the banks of the river, causing landslides and can also be caused by boats and ferries open. Also near the shore, especially squatter sand dredging without proper licenses from unprofessional technical institutions that have not studied the depth and flow of the river.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Kong Sophoan, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, confirmed that the pumping of the river is in the interest of the people to facilitate the flow of water and navigation to deepen the river and reduce river bank collapse. On the other hand, the sand from this restoration will be used to build school structures, provincial offices and to fill some locations in Kandal province.
He also urged the municipal authorities to instruct sand trucks to transport dry sand and cover it properly in accordance with transport standards, not to overload, drive at the speed limit, and to take care of the environment by cleaning the car body during special transport. Roads must be cleaned regularly to avoid dirt, roads, dust that affect the health of people. APSARA Authority is building a new wooden staircase at Kbal Spean resort
