US military helicopter crashes in Afghanistan, killing two officers!
KABUL: Two U.S. soldiers were killed in a helicopter crash in Afghanistan on Wednesday. This was released by Reuters on Wednesday afternoon, November 20, 2019.
The U.S. military said in a statement that "the cause of the crash is still under investigation and there are no reports of enemy fire." But at the same time, Taliban militants claimed responsibility for the shooting down of the US military helicopter in Logar province, south of the capital Kabul.
The US military helicopter crash comes just one day after the Taliban exchanged two Western hostages with three of their commanders detained by the Afghan government. Tensions are expected to ease between the Taliban and the US-led international coalition.
This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen inaugurated the "Indra Devi Building" of the Royal Academy of Cambodia worth more than 1.5 million dollars
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, inaugurates the "Indra Devi Building" of the Royal Academy of Cambodia on Thursday, November 21, 2019.
In addition to the construction of this building, the Royal Academy of Cambodia also erected a single statue of her near the building as a place of worship.
Prior to the construction of the statue, the Royal Academy of Cambodia established a research team and organized a workshop with the participation of national and international experts from various ministries and institutions, and reached an agreement to determine the statue of Indra Devi. Solo by following the statue next to the wall of Preah Khan temple.
The sculpture of Indra Devi on copper and a shrine for the preservation of her statue was sponsored by Duke Seang Chanheng.
