Five Major International Institutions Celebrate the 30th Anniversary of the Protection of the Rights of the Child in the Campaign "Give All Rights to All Children"
Cambodia ratified the Convention on the Rights of the Child on 15 October 1992, and since then Cambodia has made significant progress in improving the lives of children. More than 97% of boys and girls are enrolled in primary school, an unprecedented rate. Infant and child mortality under the age of five has dropped by more than 70 percent, and access to clean water has tripled since 1990.
But not all children have a better childhood. There are still many children who do not have the right education standards for their age, so the 30th anniversary of the Convention on the Rights of the Child is an opportunity. In particular, to promote the priority of children's rights in national and development plans. The European Aviation Safety Agency appreciates the steady progress of Cambodia's civil aviation sector.
