Tycoon Leng Navatra Signs MOU with National Institute of Business to Establish Free Korean Language Classes
(Phnom Penh): Tycoon Leng Navatra, owner of Borey Leng Navatra, has decided to sign an agreement with the National Institute of Business to establish a free Korean language class, providing opportunities for students who wish to work in Korea. And providing specific information for students to work in Korea through a collaboration between the school-Ministry of Labor and Leng Navatra.
The signing ceremony was held this morning, November 20, 2019 at the National Institute of Business in the presence of Mr. Tim Oeun, Director of the National Institute of Commerce, Mr. Leng Navatra, General Director of Borey Leng Navatra and Mr. Chea Many professors and students.
Mr. Tem Oeun, Director of the National Institute of Business, said that through this agreement, students will easily gain knowledge of the Korean language because the study does not require payment, that is, under the sponsorship of Mr. Leng Navatra. Only once. In the past, the tycoon has always cooperated and helped the institute many times, while today, the National Institute of Commerce is honored to have the tycoon collaborate on Korean language learning.
In particular, Leng Navatra, CEO of Borey Leng Navatra, stated that the purpose of setting up this free Korean language class was to facilitate students who wish to work in Korea to learn Korean. Master the exam to work as soon as possible and provide specific information before going abroad to avoid cheating scammers and some companies that do not have a clear source.
Mr. Oknha continued that this study does not affect the study of students' skills or any work of young students, that is, we study at any free time and also encourage students to practice. Work part-time and study part-time to earn money to support your studies before deciding to work in Korea.
The tycoon emphasized that the agreement was nothing more than wanting to see our students have a better life in the future, avoiding graduation for three to four years, and then suddenly losing their jobs, leading to financial losses. And its time, and going to work in Korea is also an opportunity to save a lot of money to open a business or business when you return home.
Please note that the first free Korean language course at the National Institute of Business is for 2 years and recruits 200 students for a course of 3 to 6 months, the study time can be between 12 hours. Noon to 5 pm. The next class will continue to accept more students if there is a greater need. Man arrested after defrauding Nhek Bun Chhay of more than $ 70,000, suspect to be sent to court for further proceedings
