In honor of the late Samdech Preah Ream Bopha Devi, the Ministry of Tourism recommends suspending the sale of alcohol in entertainment centers for one day tomorrow
(Phnom Penh): In order to pay tribute to the late Samdech Reachabotrey Preah Ream Norodom Bopha Devi, the Ministry of Tourism has issued a circular instructing the owners or managers of entertainment businesses that sell alcohol to suspend the sale of all kinds of alcohol for one day. On November 20, tomorrow.
The circular continued that in order to pay tribute to the late King Norodom Bopha Devi, the Ministry of Tourism would like to make the following recommendations:
1: Owners or managers of Karaoke, Distot, Bars, and Beer Gardens throughout the capital-province shall suspend their business activities for one day on November 20, 2019.
2. The owner or manager of the restaurant and canteen business must suspend the sale of alcohol.
3. The Director of the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism shall disseminate and educate the above tourism service business owners to implement the business suspension in accordance with this circular effectively and responsibly.
