Cambodia-Myanmar is working to promote the resumption of direct flights between the two countries
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Myanmar are working to promote the resumption of direct flights between the two countries. This was confirmed by Mr. Srey Thamrong, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister.
According to Srey Thamrong, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, during the meeting, Samdech Techo welcomed the Vice President, who was honored to attend the Asia-Pacific Summit, a historic event that not only demonstrates national unity among nations. Not only Asia-Pacific, but it also shows the solidarity market between Myanmar and Cambodia in bilateral relations.
The Vice President responded with great pleasure to attend the forum and appreciated the warm welcome and pleasure in attending the summit, as well as congratulated on the success of the work. This summit, too.
Next year is the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries. The two leaders discussed ways to boost trade, boost cultural and tourism cooperation. The two sides also reached a number of agreements and made special efforts to promote direct flights, although there have been direct flights in the past but not enough guests have been suspended.
In the field of education, the prince proposed to promote student exchanges through mutual scholarships. So far, during Aung San Suu Kyi's visit, the Royal Government of Cambodia has provided 10 scholarships to Myanmar and asked the Myanmar side to respond to reach an agreement on this issue.
As Myanmar will host the third Asia-Pacific Summit next year, the Vice President invited Samdech Techo to attend the summit. In this regard, Samdech said that he will attend to show the unity of the nation in the Asia-Pacific region, as well as participate in building peace for the region.
