(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of November 19, 2019, paid a courtesy call on the Vice President and Minister of Justice of Palau, Mr. Renul Ullouch, Minister of Justice of Palau. The meeting was held at the Peace Palace.
The Prime Minister's Delegation, Srey Thamrung, said that during the meeting, Renul Ullouch expressed his pleasure at attending the Asia-Pacific Summit and that it was an opportunity for him to get to know Cambodia. Considered a good country that is clean.
He said the two countries have established diplomatic ties for a long time, but seem to be less active because we are far apart. He understood that the invitation to attend the summit would open a new page between the two countries' historical cooperation.
In response, Samdech Techo Hun Sen agreed that this was an opportunity for Cambodia-Laos to start relations as well as cooperation that could be in line with what already exists. Samdech initiated the idea that there should be a memorandum of understanding on consultations between the Foreign Ministries of the two countries so that the Ministries of the two countries can explore areas for cooperation and communication.
The next step is to sign an MoU on visa waivers for official and diplomatic passports and then to sign a trade and investment protection agreement between the two countries, he said. Through this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed to invite the President and the First Lady of Laos to visit Cambodia at any convenient time.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has stated that Cambodia-Palau should start on food and investment cooperation and that Cambodia may have some products that can be brought to the Palau market. The prince also expressed his desire to visit Palau to begin boosting bilateral ties.
At the same time, the Vice President thanked and said that he was waiting for the signing of the MoU on consultations to start examining opportunities for the two countries to learn from each other, especially in the fields of defense, investment and trade. In addition, there can be cooperation in the fight against terrorism, prevention of transnational crime and drug smuggling.
Renul Ullouch also informed the Prince about the time when Palau is hosting the Ocean Summit to be held in 2020 and the first Asia-Pacific Women's Summit to be held at the beginning. This coming December, by inviting the prince to attend.
Regarding this invitation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen accepted the invitation and said that if given the opportunity, he would attend both meetings and pay a visit to Palau.
Palau is a small country in the western Pacific Ocean near the Philippine-Indonesian border with an area of more than 400 square kilometers and a population of only tens of thousands.
One dead, 11 missing in South Korea fishing boat fire
SEOUL: One person was killed and 11 others were injured after a South Korean fishing boat caught fire near Jeju Island. This is according to a quote from Yonhap News Agency on Tuesday afternoon, November 19, 2019.
The fishing boat caught fire on the sea west of Jeju Island on Tuesday morning. About three hours later, a 60-year-old crew member was spotted more than seven kilometers south of the scene and was airlifted to a hospital on Jeju Island. But then the man was pronounced dead.
Eleven other crew members of the fishing boat, including five South Koreans and six Vietnamese, are still missing. The above crew member who lost his life was a South Korean. The South Korean navy and maritime patrol moved ships, helicopters and planes to search for the victims, but the operation was hampered by strong waves and strong winds.
