It should be informed that the Chbar Ampov district administration has been preparing public order on Street 369 and some other roads in order to maintain order and build wide and beautiful roads in accordance with the policy of national development for progress. The 23rd Greater Mekong Subregion Ministerial Conference, hosted by Cambodia, approves 255 projects worth $ 92 billion!
(Phnom Penh): The 23rd Greater Mekong Subregion Ministerial Conference (GMS Ministers) updated the investment framework in the Greater Mekong Subregion 2022, with a total of 255 projects worth approximately $ 92 billion. Agreed on the progress report and the second update of the investment framework in the Greater Mekong Subregion.
Notable achievements of the conference are the Greater Mekong Subregion Health Cooperation Strategy 2019-2023, which was officially unveiled at the 23rd Ministerial Conference. The five-year strategy will provide a guiding basis for cooperation between countries in addressing health issues that threaten the subregion.
This is according to the press release of the 23rd Greater Mekong Sub-region Ministerial Conference held on the evening of November 18, 2019 at Sofitel Phnom Penh Pokitra Hotel under the chairmanship of Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia and Minister for the Greater Mekong Subregion Program and Ahmed M. Saeed, Vice President of the Asian Development Bank.
The conference is attended by Ministers of all GMS countries and is held under the theme "Better Integration, Environment and Sustainability in the Greater Mekong Subregion".
The meeting was also attended by development partners from 20 institutions, and the development partners expressed strong support for the Greater Mekong Subregion program. The Greater Mekong Subregion Business Council also attended the 23rd Conference and issued a statement explaining private sector initiatives in the Greater Mekong Subregion.
The 23rd Greater Mekong Subregion Ministerial Conference aims to ensure the organization of the 7th GMS Summit to be held in 2021 and hosted by Cambodia.
The Ministerial Conference of the Greater Mekong Subregion discussed and reviewed the new long-term strategic framework document of the Greater Mekong Subregion for the leadership to consider and approve at the 7th Summit. Also on the purpose and content of a new comprehensive research program aimed at supporting the implementation of the new GMS strategy.
As a continuation of the GMS program, member countries are considering and addressing challenges and opportunities in new regional and global development environments and developing innovative projects. Take the latest technology and focus on software connectivity to ensure readiness for the era of the fourth generation of the Industrial Revolution.
Full Speech by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Opening Ceremony of the Asia-Pacific Summit
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on November 19, 2019, presided over the opening ceremony of the 2nd Asia-Pacific Summit, which was held at the Peace Palace in Cambodia.
The second Asia-Pacific Summit was held under the theme "Responding to Current Key Challenges: Peace, National Unity, Interdependence, Mutual Prosperity and Global Values."
The following is the full text of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech:
Today, I am proud and pleased to attend the opening ceremony of the Asia-Pacific Summit 2019 in Cambodia on the topic of Responding to Current Key Challenges, Peace, National Unity, Interdependence, Mutual Prosperity. Come with the universal values that are now solemnly celebrated.
I would like to welcome and thank His Excellency Lok Chumteav, Head of State, Head of Government, President of the National Assembly, His Excellency, Lok Chumteav, distinguished national and international guests who are present at this important summit.
At the same time, Europe, once the world's most peaceful country, is facing crises caused by political tensions and declining relations between countries, and many other global challenges. All of these challenges require countries in the Asia-Pacific region as well as the world to show a strong common will and unity as a whole to bring peace and harmony to people in the region and the world.
Let me recall some of Cambodia's past experiences related to the theme of today's summit: Peace and National Unity. In the history of Cambodia, the Indochina War from 1970-1975 and the genocidal regime from 1975-1979 destroyed the roots of the national socio-economic infrastructure. Although the Khmer Rouge regime ended on January 7, 1979, the country's civil war continued.
Subsequently, although Cambodia achieved the Paris Peace Accords in 1991 and held its first elections in 1993, the chronic civil war continued, and this was the reason why I put forward a "win-win policy". »To all stakeholders to end the chronic war, seek peace and national unity in Cambodia with three main priority conditions:
First. Ensuring that everyone can continue to survive. Ensuring that everyone has a job and livelihood. Third. Ensuring the protection of all their property.
Peace and stability are indispensable foundations for development, and equitable development and the environment are essential for strengthening and ensuring social peace and stability. The peace that Cambodia has now is an experience of Cambodia that was once plagued by war, and now Cambodia has proudly achieved a new face.
Education and public health care have also improved. Cambodia is now a country that actively contributes to the maintenance of world peace through the conquest of peacekeepers and demining teams to countries around the world under the auspices of the United Nations.
At the same time, I call on the international community to join together in respecting and re-establishing an open, multilateral system that is environmentally friendly and strictly respects the rule of law in order to train a society with a new vision and concept. Efficient and innovative, a universal value for humanity.
I hope that the Asia-Pacific Summit 2019 Cambodia will actively discuss the challenges and appropriate solutions that will contribute to building a world in which all peoples of the Asia-Pacific region as well as the world as a whole live under the shadow of peace. Peace and harmony with all nations, without distinction of race or color, of the same race.
Finally, with the announcement of the official opening of the Asia-Pacific Summit 2019-Cambodia now, I wish the meeting a fruitful result and I wish Samdech, Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs, Ladies and Gentlemen, Distinguished National and International Guests Achieve good health with happiness, prosperity and achieve success in all tasks.
