(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chan Darong, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Rural Development, confirmed that Cambodia will achieve the goal of people living in rural areas with 100% clean water and toilets by 2025.
Mr. Chan Darong stated, "As a strategic plan of the Ministry of Rural Development, we aim to encourage rural people by 2025 to have access to clean water, sanitation, clean living and a sustainable environment by 2025." "
A spokesman for the Ministry of Rural Development said that if we look at the growth momentum from 2017-2018 2018-2019, we see that by the end of 2019, toilets have reached about 80 percent and clean water has reached 65 percent, with five remaining. Next year, we can achieve 100 percent.
Mr. Chan Darong claimed that the achievement of 100% clean water and toilets by 2025 due to:
First, there is the attention of leaders and professional officials at all levels to promote this sanitation and water issue. Collaborates with one development partner, representatives of other development partners, as well as national and international organizations involved in the water and sanitation sector.
The senior official pointed out that this mechanism is not only at the national level, but also at the provincial level. In every province, there is this mechanism, and there is a provincial water supply and sanitation technical team with a number of departments and organizations working as members in this field.
