(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has thanked the Indonesian government for helping prevent Sam Rainsy and his cronies from taking Indonesian territory to overthrow the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his gratitude during a meeting with former Indonesian Vice President and President of the Asian Cultural Council (ACC) Chou Soskala on the evening of November 18, 2019 at the Peace Palace.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo thanked the President of Indonesia for providing better cooperation in the spirit of ASEAN to prevent illegal rebels. In particular, Mr. Sam Rainsy and Ms. Mu Sochua used Indonesian territory to commit corrupt activities in an attempt to overthrow the Royal Government of Cambodia. This was confirmed by Mr. Srey Thamrong, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister.
It should be noted that Mr. Sam Rainsy and Ms. Mu Sochua, along with a number of other parties, tried to use the territory of Malaysia and Indonesia to prepare their plans to overthrow the legitimate government of Cambodia on November 9. But in the end, their plans were thwarted by ASEAN members, including Thailand, Malaysia and Indonesia, through Cambodia's request not to allow them to act towards their plans.
It should be noted that in the meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Chou Sos Kala also discussed some work related to the relationship and cooperation between Cambodia and Indonesia.
Mr José Kala expressed his delight at the growing relationship between the two countries. He also said that the Asia-Pacific Summit held in Cambodia is very important, having built achievements to show the world unity to solve some challenges.
Samdech Techo also expressed his appreciation for the long-standing relationship between the two countries and thanked Indonesia for helping to train human resources such as Cambodian officials and the armed forces. In addition, trade relations and direct flights have further enhanced cooperation between the two countries.
Within the framework of ASEAN, Samdech Techo considered that Indonesia is a big country because of its large population and strong voice that helps ASEAN to influence and help the Cambodian economy.
