Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers the death of Princess Ream Bopha Devi as a loss of Cambodia's important cultural human resources (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the afternoon of November 18 This year 2019 considers the death of Princess Ream Bopha Devi as the loss of human resources living in an important cultural sector in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo's statement was made on the occasion that Samdech allowed a delegation of about 400 coaches and athletes to pay a courtesy call and receive recommendations before leaving for the 30th SEA Games in the Philippines.
Samdech Techo also confirmed that Samdech will lead a delegation of the Royal Government to pay homage to the spirit of Princess Ream Bopha Devi at 4:00 pm on November 20, 2019.
Princess Ream Norodom Bopha Devi was born on January 8, 1943 in Phnom Penh, the eldest daughter of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the King Father of Independence, Territorial Integrity and National Unity. Khmer Preah Borom Ratanakoth is the most revered deity and the concubine Phat Kanoul, the dancer of the Royal Ballet.
He received the Royal Decree to promote the title of "Samdech Reachabotrey Preah Ream" on January 24, 1994 and to the title of "Tep Neat Vatey Ek" from the Royal Decree on the Inheritance of the Living Heritage of the Kingdom of Cambodia in 2013.
