(Pursat): Mr. Cheng Lay, Deputy Governor of Pursat Province, on November 18, 2019, called on national and international development partners, local authorities, professional officials and citizens to participate in eliminating the use of illegal fishing gear to increase fish habitats. Make more places to achieve the goal of 1,200 ponds by the end of 2019.
Mr. Cheng Lay said that currently Pursat province already has 33 community fish ponds.
Ms. Lov Samnan, Director of Khmer Women's Development Organization, said that the two-day workshop aims to share the results and experiences of improving the management plans of 33 community fish ponds and action plans for implementation in 2020 and increase Cooperation with other relevant institutions.
Mr. Cheng Lay said that fish is a special food and necessary for all people in Cambodia. All of these fish are found in lakes, rivers, streams, streams, ponds, especially in the Tonle Sap Lake.
Due to the demand for fish and exports combined with climate change, the flooding of the Tonle Sap Lake was less than last year and the water temperature was hot, which affected the spawning of Fish. To make matters worse, the illegal use of sophisticated equipment has led to significant losses and declines in fish stocks in the Tonle Sap Lake, as well as in the O'Preh Lake.
He said that in order to facilitate the fish consumption of the people, it is necessary to work together to re-enrich the fish in the rice fields, rivers, lakes, canals, ponds, ponds and ponds by creating a place as a fish sanctuary to eliminate consumption. Illegal equipment is considered a task, not just a fishery. 8-year-old volunteer team of Mr. Hun Many examined and treated nearly 500,000 patients for free (Video inside)
