President of Kandal Province: Youth work is a job that does not need benefits, a job dedicated to its national cause
(Kandal): Mr. Kim Rithy, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province and President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia (UYFC) in Kandal Province, stated that youth work is unpaid work and does not take personal time. And sometimes we also have to spend our own money, so this is a job that does not need benefits, a job that requires a high commitment to its cause.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Kim Rithy, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, participating in the program to share the experience of youth volunteering in Saang District, Kandal Province on November 17, 2019.
Mr. Kim Rithy added that the volunteer work in response has given us the honor at the grassroots level, giving us the opportunity to build networks and friends to strengthen solidarity and help each other in difficult times.
Mr. Rithy also stated that this year, the Central Committee is planning to hold the 41st anniversary of the founding of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia at the 2 December Palace, which is expected to have more than 20,000 participants, and for Kandal province, it is planned to have young people to participate. More than 5,000 people.
He also encouraged all members of Saang district to continue to work on the core work, which is the identity of their respective communes, such as humanitarian work, environmental work, blood donation, sports. And educational work.
The President urged the members of the meeting to exchange views and exchange good experiences with each other regarding the volunteer work done in their commune in the past to raise issues. Faced with a lack of action plans, as well as suggestions to discuss and find a solution in a timely manner.
(Phnom Penh): The Indian Embassy in Cambodia has announced that the Indian Government's Cultural Relations Council of the Government of India will provide scholarships for Cambodian students wishing to pursue a Master's or Doctoral degree at Indian universities. For the academic year 2020-2021.
For more information on application guidelines, city briefings, university listings, conditions, scholarship fees, these FAQs are available on the scholarship website.
Scholarships under the Mekong-Ganges Cooperation provide round-trip airfare to the nearest airport and take an AC train to the university if needed, in addition to the stipend. Months and some other benefits in terms of scholarship.
Students can access the names of the universities available on the Scholarship website, details of the courses and the terms and conditions that the universities have and need. Shortlisted candidates will be called for an English test at the Embassy of India in Phnom Penh and an oral interview.
Candidates who apply for subjects such as Science, Engineering, Information Technology, etc. must have high marks and knowledge in Physics, Chemistry and Mathematics in the 12th grade final exam.
Students selected by the ICCR Scholarship will now be offered university accommodation. No students are allowed to stay private.
Students can visit the website of the university they want to apply to to ensure that they meet the university's requirements and documents.
Closing date for applications is Friday, January 31, 2020 and for PhD on July 31, 2020. Applicants for undergraduate and postgraduate scholarships must be between 18-30 years old and under 45 years old from the date of enrollment.
(Phnom Penh): As of now, more than 70 people accused of "conspiracy" related to the failed coup on November 9 have been released on bail. This was confirmed by the spokesperson of the Ministry of Justice on November 18, 2019.
Chin Malin, a spokesman for the Ministry of Justice, confirmed to Fresh News that the release on bail was in principle linked to certain conditions, such as not going abroad, not breaking the law and appearing in accordance with the law. Summoning of the authorities and so on.
The campaign to release the accused in connection with the coup case follows a series of calls by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen for the Minister of Justice to work with prosecutors and the courts to bring the perpetrators to justice. All detained rebels are out on bail.
All of the accused were arrested after participating in the illegal coup plot of Sam Rainsy to overthrow the Royal Government on November 9, 2019.
However, the coup plan failed miserably after Sam Rainsy did not return to Cambodia as promised and postponed indefinitely.
