This was stated by Dr. Chou Chandary, Deputy Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, at the finals of the 9th "Jiangsu Award" Chinese Language Competition and the Confucius Institute of the Royal Academy of Cambodia held at Asia Europe University on November 18, 2019.
Dr. Chou Chandary said that all students today are full of energy compared to the past. Cambodia and China have always respected each other, China is Cambodia's best cooperation partner. The two countries' closeness has brought the people of the two countries together and developed together as one.
He added that the traditional friendship between Cambodia and China for many generations has provided Cambodian youths with a wide range of opportunities for development, and the bilingual resources of Khmer and Chinese have also helped boost our country's relations. Both, too.
Ms. Vuth Sopheakna, Director of the Cambodian side, Confucius Institute of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that in order to promote the relationship between Cambodia and China in the study, the Confucius Institute of the Royal Academy of Cambodia organized the finals of the "Jiangsu Award" Chinese Speaking Competition. The ninth "and" Confucius Institute of the Royal Academy of Cambodia "under the theme" Beautiful Jiangsu achieved my dream ".
Ms. Vuth Sopheakna stated that so far this year, the "Jiangsu Award" has been held nine times, and the "Jiangsu Award" is a platform that has attracted more and more Cambodian students to learn about Jiangsu and its culture. China. There is a saying that "the upper heaven, the lower heaven, Suzhou and Hangzhou, the beautiful land of Jiangnan" has become a tourist destination for Cambodians.
Lor Yimin, chairman of the Jiangsu International Cultural Exchange Center, said the "Jiangsu" award reflects the kindness of the people of Jiangsu to the people of the world. He hopes that going through this final competition will encourage Chinese language learners in Cambodia to achieve their dreams and strengthen the relationship and cooperation between the Cambodian and Chinese people.
After the competition, all 18 contestants have 2 first place winners, 4 second place winners and 12 third place winners. The first and second place candidates will be invited to participate in an eight-day study tour to Jamsu Province, which will travel during August 2020.
Jiangsu is one of the most developed provinces in China, rich in beautiful scenery, rich in food resources and fish, with a thousand-year history of intercultural culture. Jiangsu Province also has many famous universities. Jiangsu is a province that is wide open in terms of cooperation and foreign relations.
