The body of Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Las Lay is being kept at Wat Sansom Kosal, Buddhists can pay their respects every day, the body will be cremated on February 3, 2020
(Phnom Penh): The body of Samdech Preah Thommalikhet, Honorary Doctor Las Lay, Samdech Preah Sang, First Deputy President, President of the Buddhist Parliament of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Chief Prelate of Wat Sansom Kosal is being kept at Wat Sansom Kosal, and Buddhists near and far can attend Incense honors the soul every day.
Until February 3, 2020, at 6:00 AM, the body of Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Kittibandit Las Lay will be marched from Wat Sansom Kosal to the crematorium in front of Wat Botum Vatey Reachvararam to celebrate the cremation. This is according to the schedule of the funeral committee, which was received by Fresh News on November 17, 2019.
Please be informed that Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Las Lay, Preah Chao Athikar Wat Sansom Kosal, received his immortality (death) on the afternoon of October 29, 2019 at the age of 106. Immediately after receiving this sad news, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, arrived at Wat Sansom Kosal to attend the funeral of Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Las Lay.
Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Las Lay was born on Wednesday, the 7th day of the lunar month of Chhnang Thao in the Buddhist era 2457, corresponding to the Christian era 1914 in Thoung village, Thoung commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province. His father is Acharya Lak and his mother is Su Ouch. He has 10 siblings, 7 brothers and 3 sisters, and is the fifth son in the family.
