The Foreign Ministry considered the coverage of the European Commission report by Radio Free Asia to be inaccurate and even raised inappropriate concerns involving tens of thousands of workers. Defame the reputation of government officials.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs confirmed that in accordance with the procedures of the European Commission sent to the Royal Government of Cambodia on 12 November 2019 its preliminary report on the assessment of the preferential tariff system "on all goods except arms -EBA". The Royal Government of Cambodia will comment on this report within a month.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs said that the relevant ministries and institutions will review the report as a whole and will provide an appropriate response in a timely manner that will reflect the latest developments in the areas of concern of the European Commission. The European Commission is expected to decide in February 2020 whether to remove the preferential trade regime.
"In accordance with the European Commission's diplomatic practices and conditions, this report is considered confidential," the ministry said. The Royal Government of Cambodia regrets and condemns the intentional misrepresentation of Radio Free Asia in order to mislead the public about the European Commission report. "Based on the wording and paragraphs quoted from this report, it is not in accordance with the original content."
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs added: "Such false information has created unfortunate concerns involving tens of thousands of workers, misleading the public and tarnishing the reputation of government officials, which RFA claims. Leaked file. "On the other hand, RFA's activities make it clear that it is not a reliable source of information, but only a propaganda station serving a political group."
