Four ministries are merging into a single inspection team to alleviate difficulties for the private sector and increase efficiency
In order for this merger to be effective, this morning, November 15, 2019, the above four Ministries held a discussion on the merger of the Labor Inspection Team at the first inter-institutional level at the Ministry of Labor under the chairmanship of Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor.
According to the results of the 18th Royal Government and Private Sector Forum, the Royal Government has assigned the Ministry of Labor to integrate the labor inspection team at the inter-ministerial level, which is divided into two steps:
* First step: All Ministries and Institutions with more than one group of factory inspectors must merge into one group and visit only once a year for one goal by preparing a list of inspection activities and Clear timing, except in cases of necessity or criminal cases.
The Ministry of Labor continues to use the same labor inspection team mechanism at the same time and uses the same assessment standards that the Ministry has been implementing since 2014. The Labor Inspection Team will inspect the work of enterprises and establishments only once a year for a specific purpose.
* The next step: the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training will lead a working group with the participation of all ministries, institutions, labor inspection teams in enterprises to check the importance of each inspection to determine which inspector. Which one should be kept and which should be removed and prepared as a list of inspection teams, functions and inspection time clearly.
Heng Sour, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor, added that in inter-ministerial discussions this morning, we requested that the list of labor inspectors of each ministry be reviewed jointly. "And with different standards, we can synthesize this standard into a common standard."
