Cambodian beer packaging machine through advanced technology
(Phnom Penh): Khmer Breweries' Cambodian beer packaging production line operates using the latest technology in the industry to ensure that all beer cans are of the right quality and quantity before being shipped to market.
All the machines in the beer packaging system are imported and assembled by Krones and KHS of Germany, a world-renowned company that supplies well-known breweries.
All stages of packaging are automated, with different functions and productivity, such as canning machines, can openers, canisters, canisters, canisters, date setters (canisters) and canisters. Put it in a can and a beer can sorting machine.
The packaging technology of each machine is capable of determining the operation of the production line according to the set standards. For example, before pouring beer into a can, the machine will check the can for any stains (scratches or crooked surface) and then clean all the packaging, especially to measure the level of carbon dioxide (CO2) correctly. First.
After pouring the beer into the can, the machine will cover the can and send it to the machine to check the level of beer. The machine will check all beer cans and if any cans are found to have the wrong amount of beer, the machine will push the beer cans out.
Properly brewed beer cans will go through another stage of heating, with the beer cans being heated to a temperature no higher than 60 degrees Celsius to ensure the quality of the beer can be stored longer and more safely and hygienically. Beer cans will continue to be shipped to the container when the machine checks that the date record is correct.
In addition, the machine will grab the cans into the case and pass by the machine to control the number of cans in the beer can and then push out any beer cans that do not reach the limit without allowing it to be sent to the extension. The machine will automatically sort the beer cans to be ready for distribution to the market.
