Canned mushrooms and fish were found for sale at Tumnup Rolok Market, Preah Sihanouk Province, and CamControl officials confiscated and burned them
(Preah Sihanouk): For food safety as well as the health of the people, the CamControl Branch Officer of Preah Sihanouk Province, led by Mr. Bun Chamroeun, Acting President, on November 15, 2019, cooperated with the officials of the Provincial Department of Commerce and local authorities. Disseminate food quality and safety at Tumnup Rolok Market, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
According to the CamControl official in Preah Sihanouk province, during the inspection, some food samples were taken for preliminary testing, including: fresh shrimp, squid, dried fish, navy beans, sausage, ginger and pickles to find banned chemicals. Which can affect the health of the people.
As a result, officials did not find any banned chemicals in the seafood, Camcontrol officials said. However, experts found that the display of defective and expired goods, including: 9 cans of LYLY mushrooms, 1 can of CBT fish, a total of about 7.79 kg of confiscated goods.
After that, the professional officer made a record of confiscating the goods and storing them at the Sihanoukville branch for destruction, and instructed other traders to understand and follow the law on quality control, safety of products and services to avoid causing harm. Impact on people's health will be able to face the law further.
Since being ceded to China by the United Kingdom in 1997, Hong Kong has been under the special administrative system, which guarantees greater freedoms than any other region in China. But the city was in deep crisis when large-scale protests erupted last June and have continued to this day with no sign of easing.
Initially, the protests were peaceful, but now they have turned violent and escalating from week to week, especially recently.
Addressing the tense situation in Hong Kong, Chinese President Xi Jinping, attending a summit in the Brazilian capital, said that protesters were committing "grave threats" to the "one country" policy. Two management systems.
At the same time, Xi reiterated Beijing's unwavering support for the Hong Kong administration, including the Hong Kong police. He also stressed that ending violence and controlling chaos and restoring order is Hong Kong's most important and urgent task.
