(VOVworld) - Senior Minister and Minister of Public Works and Transport Sun Chanthol on November 15, 2019, attended the 17th ASEAN-Japan Transport Ministers' Meeting in Hanoi, Vietnam.
The ASEAN Ministers welcomed Japan's declaration of support for activities based on the Kuala Lumpur Strategic Transport Plan 2016-2025 in the areas of air, land, sea, sustainable transport and facilitation. Transport through projects and activities under the ASEAN-Japan Transport Partnership in a comprehensive and sustainable manner.
The Ministers discussed and approved the following policy / cooperation initiatives under the ASEAN-Japan Transport Partnership:
A: Proposal of ASEAN-Japan Transport Partnership Work Plan 2018-2019
B: New initiatives under the ASEAN-Japan Transport Partnership include:
1: Training plan for the implementation of the Global Satellite System (GNSS) in ASEAN. 2: Technology for monitoring overweight vehicles. 3: Joint research on the maintenance of bridges for cross-border corridors. Public transportation for the disabled and the elderly.
C: Key outcomes of existing projects under the ASEAN-Japan Transport Partnership include: The Green Ship Strategy under the project to encourage the use of environmentally friendly vessels in the ASEAN region.
D: Update on the ASEAN-Japan Air Services Agreement. After criticizing the people for their fear and stench, the Prey Veng provincial governor assigned the provincial authorities and professional officers to instruct the owners of the crocodile farm in Ba Phnom district to prepare properly.
(Prey Veng): After criticism from the villagers in the fence with a crocodile farm that is causing them great fear on the afternoon of November 14, 2019, Mr. Chea Somethy, Provincial Governor Prey Veng assigned Mr. Chan Ran, Deputy Governor and Mr. Ouk Samnang, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to lead professional officers and local authorities to inspect the actual location.
During the inspection, the authorities found 380 crocodiles, the owner of which was 48-year-old female named Ban Neang in Kdei Dong village, Rong Damrey commune, Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Chanran told the owner of the crocodile farm to make a contract with a professional officer to apply for a business license, a permit to raise crocodiles, a transport permit for crocodiles and other permits, and to set up a proper breeding ground according to the standard. Techniques to ensure the safety of the people living next to the village with the fence.
During the inspection of the crocodile farm, Mr. Chan Ran also asked the owner of the crocodile farm to comply with the following four points of contract:
The Deputy Governor also advised the owner of the crocodile farm that if the crocodile farming has a problem for the people near the village with the fence, the crocodile owner must be responsible before the law. According to the technical standards of the department, he will close this crocodile farm.
It should be noted that the action of the authorities and officials came immediately after many families in Ba Phnom district, through the news agency Fresh News, criticized the crocodile farm, which is causing them great fear. And stinked to the villagers near the fence of Wat Neak Rainsy, Kdei Dong village, Rong Damrey commune.
They added that raising crocodiles was not standardized because they had been released from the cage a few times in the past and had been returned to their owners several times by the villagers at night. Some residents complained that there was a bad smell coming from the crocodile pond, which could not be eaten and affected their health, and they could not sleep.
