(Preah Sihanouk): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, has assigned the position of Honorary President and Vice President of the Veterans Association to the leaders and officials of Preah Sihanouk Province to better serve the veterans. More. The ceremony was held on November 14, 2019 at Sihanoukville Provincial Hall.
Mr. Kouch Chamrein, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, has been appointed as the Honorary President of the Association, Mr. Nou Sam Ol has been appointed as the President of the Association. In addition to the honorary president and president of the association, two other officials were also given the role of vice president of the Cambodian Veterans Association.
At the handover ceremony, Secretary-General Kun Kim asked the leaders of the Veterans Association to be given new positions to pay attention to the construction of houses for the homeless, homeless, homeless, and homeless veterans. .
The Senior Minister also reminded the leaders of the New Veterans Association to inspect and solve the construction of houses for 67 families of veterans, which the Provincial Veterans Association has already targeted. At the same time, the joint working group must study the land of veterans in Stung Hav district to evaluate and submit comments to the standing committee of the association.
Mr. Kun Kim also reminded the Sihanoukville Veterans Association to continue to visit the veterans to check their health status and to help solve the problem when they are struggling to make ends meet. Send to the hospital or create conditions to receive various public services to suit the merits of those who have sacrificed for the cause of the motherland in the past.
