Mr. Hun Many: No matter Cambodia or any other country, the role of the youth is really important in taking responsibility for the fate of the nation.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hun Many, Member of the National Assembly, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu Constituency and President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, on November 15, 2019, stated that no matter what country or country, the role of the youth really exists. The importance of continuing to take responsibility for the fate of the nation.
This statement was made on the occasion that Mr. Hun Many received a grant of 2 million US dollars from NagaWorld to participate in the promotion of "Youth Development and Sports in Kampong Speu" held at the Naga Underground Shopping Mall. City Walk.
Mr. Hun Many hopes that the participation, support and training of football coaches for children in Kampong Speu will give children the opportunity to train in the country and abroad, and he hopes that NagaWorld will continue to cooperate. Another face.
Mr. Hun Many expressed his hope that "I still have a dream, hope that one day the national football team will have people in Kampong Speu."
"Together we provide better opportunities for them to improve their quality of life for themselves and their families," he said. We hope that the support for these programs will increase the potential of the youth in Kampong Speu for the society and that this will give back to the family, community and the whole country.
The purpose of this youth development program is to promote talent, promote youth development and provide additional opportunities for Cambodian youth to achieve their future goals and aspirations in sports and other fields.
These projects include a two-year football development program in Kampong Speu that provides professional football coaching to secondary and high school teachers, as well as ongoing sports equipment and sports infrastructure support.
