(Kampot): After criticizing the lack of accommodation for the Sea Festival, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, urged the Kampot Provincial Administration and the Provincial Department of Tourism to advertise to all hotel owners and guesthouses in the province to receive room reservations Residence of guests and please do not increase the price too much to ensure better accommodation during the Sea Festival at the end of 2019.
The direct criticism of the above accommodation was emphasized in the 8th round of the 8th Sea Festival Preparatory Meeting at Kampot Provincial Hall on the afternoon of November 14 as government officials, artists, residents and guests Some tourists are also experiencing and worrying about the lack of accommodation.
This problem is due to the fact that some hotel and guesthouse owners refuse to accept accommodation bookings from guests at all, unreasonably stating that they rent immediately when the festival arrives (in order to get a higher price). Than booking).
In this regard, Minister Thong Khon strongly urged the Director of the Kampot Provincial Department of Tourism, Mr. Soy Sinol, to continue to disseminate to all accommodation service providers in the province to receive room reservations from guests, especially not to install Not too expensive. "This issue must be resolved," he said.
At the same time, the Minister of Tourism also asked the Governor of Kampot Province, Mr. Chiao Tai, to help push for a better solution to this problem.
The minister explained that during each festival, hotel and guest house owners should be happy to accept guest bookings, not disallow them. On the other hand, hotel owners on Bokor Mountain should consider some discounts to attract more tourists.
He urged the sub-committee to cooperate with any company to provide accommodation in tents to facilitate the accommodation of tourists because the hotel rooms are not enough.
