Construction of more than $ 150 million Bak Kheng water plant to start construction later this month
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority (PPWSA) on the afternoon of November 14, 2019 signed a contract for the construction of the first phase of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant with a total amount of 156 million US dollars with the capacity to produce clean water. 195 thousand cubic meters per day.
A total of $ 156 million, of which $ 136 million will be re-loaned from the Ministry of Economy and Finance, with the support of two development partners, the French Agency for Development and the European Investment Bank, and using the PPWSA's contribution. Phnom Penh Autonomous Region $ 20 million
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Sim Nara, Chairman of the Board of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, said that the forecast shows that the demand for clean water in Phnom Penh will reach more than 900,000 cubic meters per day by 2025 and more than 1 million. Cubic meters per day in 2030 to serve the needs of clean water to about 540 thousand families.
He stated that in order to achieve the production and supply of more than 1 million cubic meters of clean water per day, the Board of Directors of the two Guardian Ministries and the Royal Government, headed by Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen, fully supported For the action plan to expand the water production capacity of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority 2018-2025.
At the same time, Mr. Sim Nara also informed the action plan as follows:
Phase 1: The Chamkar Mon Water Treatment Plant with a capacity of 55,000 m3 will be put into operation in October 2019.
2: The second phase is by 2025 to build 4 new water treatment plants and renovate 1 water treatment plant that can produce 470 thousand cubic meters per day, in addition to the current capacity of 540 thousand cubic meters. 1 day:
3: From 2025 onwards, all 7 water treatment plants of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority must produce more than 1 million cubic meters of clean water per day to serve the needs of clean water to the people until 2030.
Mr. Sim Nara added that the construction project of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant, the first step is to supply water to the "Moradok Techo National Stadium" in Peam village, Sambour Meas commune, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province and serve the water needs of the people. An additional 500,000 live west of Phnom Penh in accordance with the Royal Government of Cambodia's water supply policy.
He said that the contract for the construction of Bak Kheng water treatment plant, the first step today is the implementation of the second phase of action plan after the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has successfully implemented the first phase action plan, that is, put into operation. Chamkarmon, with a capacity of 55,000 cubic meters per day in October 2019 recently.
In addition to the current production capacity of 540 thousand cubic meters per day, the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority will be able to produce and supply an additional 594 thousand cubic meters of clean water per day to serve the water needs of the people throughout. Phnom Penh, especially people living in Chamkarmon. This is the additional confirmation of Mr. Sim Nara.
Please note that this is the fourth project to build a water treatment plant, after the launch of Niroth Water Treatment Plant, Phase 1 in 2013 and Phase 2 in 2017 and Chamkar Mon Water Treatment Plant in 2019, which Phnom Penh Water Authority strives to distribute water to the people.
