The Senior Minister stated that the three key components that are successful in the fight against HIV and AIDS in Cambodia are: 1) ownership and guidance, 2) partnership and 3) investment.
In its ownership and leadership, the National AIDS Authority leads a multi-sectoral coordination and response mechanism. At the same time, the Royal Government of Cambodia also set out six measures to ensure sustainability in the fight against HIV and AIDS in February 2019. In addition, in connection with the Global Fund program, the Ministry of Economy and Finance will be the direct recipient from April 2018.
In the generous investment of the Global Fund, Cambodia has mobilized about $ 500 million in resources. In addition, since 2015, the Ministry of Economy and Finance has provided $ 1 million to $ 1.5 million per year as a contribution to the purchase of antiretroviral drugs. An estimated $ 800,000 a year is also provided to contract staff working on Global Fund grants.
Finally, the Senior Minister stated that as part of the decentralization policy, the Ministry of Economy and Finance will simplify the rules to allow health centers to use unaffordable funds to implement HIV / AIDS programs. At the same time, the Royal Government also agreed to include AIDS programs in the policy of safe villages and communes and the responsibilities of local authorities in communes.
