He added that as of the end of 2019, Cambodia has 5 cement factories that provide jobs in the factory to a total of 2,700 people with a capacity to produce about 8 million tons of cement per year with a total investment of about 800 million. USD.
He added that in 2017 and 2018, Cambodia achieved the supply of domestically produced cement to meet the demand, but due to the growth of construction, buildings and infrastructure increased significantly in 2018 and late 2019. Later, local cement production could not meet the market demand, leading to the import of small quantities of cement products from abroad to meet demand.
He added that in addition to cement, Cambodia also has sand, stone and chlorate to meet the needs of the construction and infrastructure sectors such as roads, bridges, hydropower, dams, irrigation and construction across the country, which has contributed to the economic development and livelihood of the people. Strong citizens, too.
