The fifth cement factory in Cambodia, which was officially inaugurated this morning, is owned by Thai Bunrong Company, located in Phnom Laang, Laang Commune, Dong Tung District, Kampot Province. Thai Bunrong Cement Factory is built on an area of nearly 700 hectares, equipped with modern technology and has a production capacity of about 2,500 tons per day, equivalent to nearly 1 million tons per year.
While the country is growing rapidly in the construction sector, Cambodia has a high demand for cement for construction. Prior to 2008, Cambodia was a country that imported all kinds of cement from neighboring countries to meet construction needs.
But after 2008, the presence of cement factories in Cambodia was gradually established for the production of cement to meet the construction needs. To date, Cambodia has significantly reduced its cement imports.
