(Kratie): It is very sad that another Mekong River dolphin died at Kampi Dolphin Canyon in Sambok Village, Sambok Commune, Chit Borey District, Kratie Province due to a mosquito net at the tail. The dolphin weighs 110 kilograms and is 2.27 meters long.
According to Chuob Ratana, director of the Kratie Provincial Department of Tourism, the dolphin may have died on November 11 and floated on the river on the 12th, while the river guards at the Kampi checkpoint spotted it.
The director of the department said that it weighed about 110 kilograms and was 2.27 meters long, and when he died, his abdomen swelled.
According to Chuob Ratana, the net attached to the dolphin's tail is probably a net that floats on the river when the water rises, claiming that the people in the area also have a lot of knowledge about dolphin conservation and the benefits of dolphins. So they do not put nets in the area where the dolphins live, but the exact reason is yet to be determined.
In connection with this regret, Mr. Chuob Ratana also revealed that the total number of dolphins registered in 2017 was 92, of which Kratie was between 58-63.
According to WWF, in 2019 the Mekong River dolphin has increased by nine more, including five in Kratie. So far, five dolphins have died, including three in Kratie.
