The demonstration of bokator left by Khmer ancestors took place at a location on Keo Chenda Street, Sangkat Chroy Changva, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh. 65 bokator players and 9 pairs of bokator performers, each performance includes: teacher worship, door martial arts, martial arts and martial arts performances. Fight in the ring.
This bokator and fight performance was attended by Mr. Seng Thavrin, Chairman of Central Park Management Committee, Mr. Hul Buntha, First Vice Chairman of the Honorary Committee of the Academy of Cambodia, Mr. Tan Chuor Hong, Second Vice Chairman of the Honorary Committee of the Academy of Cambodia and Mr. Ta Krama Meas San Kim Sean, Advisor to the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and President of the Cambodian Bokator Academy.
The organization of bokator performances and fights aims to preserve and develop bokator, a national heritage, to promote Cambodian children and the world better, promote traditional Khmer martial arts, and encourage emotional support to players. Bokator all over the country continue to study and train hard to participate in performing and fighting the martial arts of Khmer ancestors to become more famous throughout the country and the world.
In the arena, there are 5 pairs of fighters, 18 of them from martial arts schools in 4 provinces: Phnom Penh, Khmer Heritage Martial Arts School in Phnom Penh, Phnom Penh Rayong Martial Arts School, Ta Dambang Dek Martial Arts School in Kampong Chhnang Province and Lok Ta Martial Arts School. Moeung warehouse, Pursat province.
Bokator is an ancient Khmer martial art and a top martial art of the Khmer ancestors, dating back to ancient times, and some have been dubbed as the martial arts of the gods. The meaning of the word bokator is a combination of the words bokator and lion, which bok means hit, push, push or punch, while the lion means king of great power or great power. So bokator is a martial art that can fight lions.
To help promote this martial art, Mr. Krama Meas San Kim Sean, with the financial support of the film, shot by Tycoon Tek Ngoy, has finished filming a film on bokator entitled "The Soul of Bokator" and plans to show it to the audience. Visit early next year, please join us to support bokator.
