Watch the video of a large crowd visiting Kep beach: Mr. Kong Vibol led a delegation of the General Department of Taxation to attend the 40th Annual Meeting of the Association of Tax Administration-CATA in Malaysia
CATA Fiscal Administration Association has active member tax administrations from 46 countries established since 1978 with the aim of assisting member states in attending major conferences, trainings, major programs, outreach and Share knowledge to develop effective fiscal administration leading to sustainable development and good governance.
The Commonwealth Fiscal Association Conference is held annually to share experiences and identify necessary regional and global tax-related measures that can respond to new trends and challenges in the Commonwealth. The era of progress towards the digital economy in particular can ensure sustainable economic development and ensure stable tax revenue growth.
During the four-day conference, six technical working groups will discuss various aspects, including the first group, the challenges and obstacles of digitalization, the second group, strategies for digitalization, the third group of fiscal administration. Tax collection management in the digital economy, the fourth group is Taxes and Shadow Economy, the fifth group is the strategy to respond to the shadow economy and the sixth group is the shadow economy and digitalization.
