As for the Ok Ambok ceremony to worship the moon god, it is described as a ceremony held to dedicate to the fulfillment of the bodhisattva's merits while being born as a rabbit. The bodhisattva rabbit sacrificed his body by jumping into a huge fire to cook meat for the hungry Indra Brahmin to eat. This caused Indra to draw a rock as a rabbit at the moon.
