Khmer civilization expert Rath Sandab gave an interview to Fresh News about the history of the Royal Festival. According to Khmer civilization experts, the history of the Royal Water Festival, Ok Ambok, floating lanterns, Ok Ambok and worshiping the moon god is divided into three as follows:
* History of the Lantern Floating Ceremony: To be grateful to the Ganges and the earth for giving life and well-being to the land that we are defrosting. On the other hand, the floating of the lanterns is associated with the belief of Buddhism, that is, to worship the glass jaws of the dragon world, which the Buddha went to Stung Nomtea and elsewhere, believing that it was a great merit. For the prosperity of oneself, the people and the nation.
* History of the creation of the Ok Ambok ceremony and the worship of the moon god: It was made by the Cambodian people to commemorate the bodhisattva who referred to the birth as a rabbit, at which time he sacrificed his life to Indra to fulfill his merit. At the same time, the Ok Ambok ceremony and the worship of the moon god were held to create a happy atmosphere for the Cambodian people, because this is the free season from the rainy season rice harvest.
