Senior Minister Osman Hassan returns to Cambodia after successful mission in Indonesia
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of November 7, 2019, Mr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions, returned home to Cambodia after successfully completing a four-day mission in the Republic of Indonesia from November 4 to 7, 2019 ago.
During the four-day mission, Senior Minister Osman Hassan addressed the 8th World Zakat Forum in Bandung, Indonesia, which was attended by nearly 400 people, including senior researchers. Leading various Zakat institutions from 35 countries under the chairmanship of Dr. Ma'ruf Amin, Vice President of Indonesia.
After the 8th World Economic Forum, Senior Minister Osman Hassan also paid a courtesy call and discussed work with the Vice President of Indonesia.
After paying a courtesy call on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, with deep affection and sentiments to Ma'ruf Amin, Senior Minister Osman Hassan said that peace and prosperity in Cambodia can be achieved through strong leadership. The right of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the contribution of the Indonesian friends.
He said that after many years of long war, a nation with only empty hands under the leadership of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen has turned this country into the seventh ranked country in In the world's fastest growing economy with over 7% economic growth over the last 20 years.
In addition, under the right leadership policy of the Royal Government, it has created national harmony, which is a good example for the world. These are the efforts of leaders at all levels, in which the Islamic community is also a part of the commitment to unite as a whole in accordance with the policies of the Royal Government.
He added that Indonesia has also played an important role in contributing to the peace process in Cambodia, both in the negotiation phase and in the Paris Agreement phase, expanding cooperation with Cambodia, helping to train troops and develop human resources. In Cambodia, it has contributed to sending peacekeepers (UNTAC) to Cambodia to provide scholarships to Cambodian students, including Cambodian Muslim students.
In addition, the Republic of Indonesia has co-sponsored the establishment of the Cambodian Muslim Scholars Union to become a member of the ASEAN Muslim Scholars Alliance. In particular, the Cambodian Khmer Muslim community knew Indonesia well through its cultural, traditional and religious ties, and considered the Republic of Indonesia a good friend.
Before concluding, the senior minister informed the Indonesian side of the evil attempts of the illegal opposition to overthrow the government and dissolve the monarchy in Cambodia. On behalf of the Royal Government, Mr. Osman Hassan requested the Indonesian side to help prevent all activities of this group.
