He added that many of the fruitful achievements that Cambodia has achieved have actively contributed and supported both financial resources and technical assistance from Japan and the Japanese people.
Mr. SUZUKI Hideo also expressed his pleasure to work in Cambodia and expressed his appreciation for the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which has brought a lot of development in the socio-economic sector and progress in all areas, especially growth. High economy at an average rate of 7% per year, which has transformed Cambodia from a low-income country to a low-middle-income country.
He added that Japan will continue to support and promote all activities and cooperation in the region, such as Mekong-Japan and ASEAN-Japan cooperation.
