According to the history of the Royal Water Festival, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon were held to commemorate the heroic example of the Khmer Navy, which liberated the land from the oppression of the enemy. This event is popular with people from all over and is celebrated every year with boat races and rowing for men and women, floating lanterns, chanting and worshiping the moon, reflecting the strong religious beliefs of the Cambodian people. .
