Ministry of Water Resources: Cambodia will be affected by the 24th typhoon named Nakri, causing light to moderate rain from today to November 13!
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has announced that Cambodia will be affected by the 24th typhoon Nakri, which will cause rain from today to November 13, 2019.
According to the Ministry of Water Resources, the typhoon will bring low rainfall to the lower provinces and coastal areas from November 7 to 13.
From the 7th to the 9th, the provinces in the north-central and northeastern highlands will receive less rain. Then from November 10 to 11, there will be light to moderate rain.
