(Kandal): Mr. Kim Rithy, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province and President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Kandal Province, praised Westland International School, a private educational institution that has actively contributed to the reform of the in-depth education system. And social and national development.
Such a statement of appreciation was made on the occasion of Mr. Kim Rithy, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, presiding over the distribution program for lower and upper secondary school certificates, which was completed in the 2018-2019 academic year of Westland International School. The ceremony was held at Westland International School, located in Takhmao City, Kandal Province on November 6, 2019.
Mr. Kim Rithy said that Westland International School has a high responsibility and responsibility to train young people, students, which is an important human resource for the future development of the country, as the saying goes. "Youth is the bamboo shoots and pillars of the nation," he said.
The Deputy Governor of Kandal also commended the leaders of Westland International School for their contribution to many social causes, including:
* Clean Environment Day in Takhmao every year to promote and inspire all people to participate in cleaning Takhmao clean * Blood donation program to the National Blood Transfusion Center. * Psychological education program for students to study hard, do good deeds, love the rich and avoid taking drugs in the way of Buddhism.
At the same time, Mr. Kim Rithy also encouraged all students to participate and follow the instructions and orientation of the school because the school program is good for young people to continue their education in higher education and social work. The future.
According to the report, Mr. Thorn Soklim, Director of Westland International School, said that Westland International School is a private educational institution officially recognized by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports in Prakas 2172, dated 22 July. 2011. In fact, Westland International School has three major curricula currently underway.
To contribute to the in-depth reform of the education system to improve the quality of secondary education, Westland International School has strengthened its rigorous student testing based on the slogan of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports: And designed curricula that link theory to practice, including science experiments, biology, physics, and chemistry in the classroom.
In addition, the school also organizes short internship programs at government institutions as well as some private institutions to study and understand. And Khmer civilization and the organization of a science fair showcasing students' work every year to provide opportunities for students to express their abilities, talents and achievements.
Westland International School not only contributes to in-depth education reform, but also in a number of social activities, including: Westland International School Clean Environment Day Program, Blood Donation to the National Blood Transfusion Center to Save Lives Blood is needed and involved in other humanitarian programs.
