Speaking to Fresh News tonight, a senior official of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs confirmed that according to the information received by the Cambodian Ambassador, Mu Sochua traveled to Jakarta, Indonesia, using only a tourist visa, not a visa. Do not do politics. After leaving Indonesia, she traveled to Malaysia.
The source also revealed that the main reason for the rebel leader to travel to Indonesia was from an NGO there called for a visit and a lunch was arranged for her to use a tourist visa, but suddenly She was about to hold a political press conference when she was banned by the authorities. The ban also comes at the request of the Cambodian ambassador.
On November 6, 2019, the Cambodian Ambassador to Indonesia requested that the Indonesian authorities arrest Mu Sochua, one of the leaders of the rebels who plotted a coup to overthrow the Royal Government of Cambodia.
"The Republic of Indonesia and Cambodia have been close friends for 60 years," the Cambodian Embassy in Indonesia said in a statement. "Therefore, the Cambodian Embassy in Jakarta would like to request the Indonesian authorities to arrest Mu Sochua and send her to Cambodia immediately in the spirit of ASEAN."
The Cambodian Embassy has confirmed that Mu Sochua is the Vice President of the Cambodian National Rescue Party (CNRP), which was dissolved by the Supreme Court of Cambodia on November 16, 2017. Her party today is an illegal party in Cambodia. She is a fugitive who was arrested by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on October 2, 2019 in connection with an attempt to overthrow a legitimate elected government.
Instead of facing legal action, Mu Sochua fled Cambodia and is seeking asylum in the United States, the embassy said. The Royal Government of Cambodia has requested all ASEAN member states to arrest and extradite Mu Sochua to Cambodia if she trespasses on their territory.
