(Phnom Penh): In the workshop to summarize the competition for the third model resort and after finding the winners of the 26 model resorts for 2019, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, announced some necessary recommendations to call Let all stakeholders continue to work together to achieve further tourism growth.
The recommendations of Minister Thong Khon include:
* First. Investment: Continue to promote the development and investment of all types of tourist resorts and tourism communities that consider the environment, cleanliness and society. In this context, all investment and development projects as tourist resorts must incorporate green and clean thinking.
Through the "Third Model Resort" competition, businesses will be able to capture the concept of "green and clean" by considering green architecture, energy saving, waste management, social and humanitarian work, and so on.
In this regard, the Ministry of Tourism must prepare guidelines and criteria for tourism development projects that need to take into account the environment, culture and social protection as a basis for evaluation of those projects.
* Second. Management: The Capital-Provincial Departments of Tourism must strive to encourage all tourism resorts to have clear managers and to have a clear management structure and to encourage all resorts to have a clear development plan.
At the same time, all tourism departments must continue to make efforts to manage and develop various tourist resorts in their localities well. In addition, the specialized department of the Ministry of Tourism must prepare standards for various types of resorts, such as agro-tourism resorts, adventure tourism destinations, eco-tourism resorts, especially green resort standards to support this model tourism competition movement next year.
At the same time, the Ministry of Tourism, the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism must cooperate to promote public awareness to staff and tourists who visit the resorts about the proper disposal of garbage and to prepare a code of conduct. Do's and don'ts to promote to tourist destinations across the country.
* Fourth. Security: All tourist resorts must have adequate signs, including information signs and location signs, especially signs showing prohibited locations and hazardous areas, in accordance with the minimum standards of tourist resorts of the Ministry of Tourism.
* Fifth. Dissemination: The Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism must continue to encourage all tourist resorts to participate in various competitions, especially this model resort competition.
At the same time, he encouraged the recording of short videos of new tourist resorts, as well as efforts to promote new destinations to share on social media and other media, and the specialized department of the Ministry of Tourism should be prepared. Photo, video and mass tourism competitions to inspire patriotism in the light of peace.
* Sixth. Private Sector: He encouraged the private sector, especially all travel agencies, to organize tours and bring more tourists to all resorts across the country, especially the winning resorts in this model racing movement.
At the same time, it is necessary to prepare a lot of local tour packages for people, students, private employees, workers, civil servants with reasonable prices to all tourist destinations across the country.
