Promoting Effective Education Sector A Private School Adds Stem Robusting to Its Students
(Phnom Penh): In order to contribute to the promotion of education in Cambodia to be more effective in line with international education and to help its students develop their brains faster, Asia-Australia School during the opening ceremony The new school year 2019 2020 This morning, November 6, 2019, announced the addition of a new subject of Stem Robosing to its students in addition to other subjects.
The opening ceremony of the new school year of the Asia-Australia School and the addition of Stem Robosing courses was presided over by Mr. Hem Bonarin, Director of Asia Australia School, Mr. Ros Savithy, Executive Director of Robotsing Cambodia, Mr. Kuy Panchhay, Director of RIELLIONAIRE With the participation of many teachers, guardians and students.
Mr. Hem Bonarin said that for the Asia-Australia School, there are training courses in both Khmer and English with a total of 306 students of all levels, all specialties, both primary schools in Khmer and English at all levels. Recently, the school has added a new program, the Stem Robosing curriculum, to further strengthen students' ability with international education.
He added that this Storm Robot education will help students get new creative ideas to help students improve their ability to a greater extent.
Mr. Ros Savithy added that the robotics program has been expanding its branches around the world, and there are countries in Asia are running the program, such as South Korea, Malaysia and China. Coding software will also effectively develop the brain and child skills of children and youth through hands-on learning as well as fun entertainment.
