Two Best Chinese Movies to Be Free in Pailin
(Pailin): Two outstanding Chinese-Cambodian mobile films will be screened for the first time for free for the people of Pailin so that the people of Tbong Pich have the opportunity to watch and enjoy The traditional culture between China and Cambodia goes deeper.
The screening team of the 4th China-Cambodia Mobile Film Tour on November 6, 2019 has traveled to Pailin Province to screen Chinese and Khmer films for the people here to watch freely from This afternoon at 6 in the park in front of Pailin Provincial Hall. This is according to the broadcast of the Cambodia-China Friendship Radio.
Mr. Yin Vutha, Special Officer of the Film Department of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, who is the Chairman of the Working Group for the 4th China-Cambodia Mobile Screening, said that the team has distributed leaflets and broadcasted on the market. Village, school from this event.
He said that the film screened in Bailin has two films, the Chinese film entitled "The Last Kilometer" and the Khmer film "Krasang", which has an educational value that reflects the lives of the people of Cambodia and China. In each period, the people of the two countries get to know each other more through art and through this film.
Ratana Rayuth, Program Manager of Cambodia-China Friendship Radio, said that this is the first time that the leadership of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts and the Chinese Embassy in Phnom Penh have chosen Bailin as the first destination for the screening event. The 4th Cambodia-China Mobile Expo 2019 aims to further promote the cultures of the two countries.
Since 2016, the best Cambodian-Chinese mobile film screenings have been held in 20 provinces and cities in Cambodia, with nearly 100,000 viewers. This outstanding China-Cambodia mobile film event is warmly welcomed by the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as people living in a large number of provinces and cities.
