SEOUL: South Korea plans to reduce its troop numbers to half a million by 2022, the Ministry of Economy and Finance announced on Wednesday. This is according to a quote from the Xinhua news agency on Wednesday evening, November 6, 2019.
South Korea is currently facing demographic changes caused by the aging population and the low birth rate that Japan is experiencing. South Korea's total population is expected to drop to 39 million by 2067, from 51 million today.
At the same time, the South Korean Ministry of Economy and Finance said it would evaluate measures aimed at requiring individuals with Korean citizenship to serve in the military. Currently, Korean citizens can enter the military if they choose to do so, but there is no requirement.
