Ms. Eva Nguyen Binh praised the development of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, which is well organized and has contributed to economic diversification. In fact, she visited three factories: a water tank factory, a panel factory and a equestrian center.
At the same time, the French Ambassador to Cambodia promised to encourage French investors to invest in Cambodia, especially in special economic zones.
It should be noted that Cambodia currently has 23 operating special economic zones, 482 investment projects that employ more than 130,000 workers and contribute about 14% of total exports. The Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has 181 investment projects that employ more than 25,000 workers.
US Congress's efforts to pass bill on Hong Kong issue hindered
WASHINGTON: Efforts in the US Congress to pass a bill aimed at putting pressure on China over the protests in Hong Kong are hampered. This is according to a quote from CNA on Wednesday afternoon, November 6, 2019.
In mid-October, the US House of Representatives unanimously approved a draft law on Hong Kong. The move prompted Beijing to react by saying that the United States was "shamelessly willing to intervene" in Hong Kong. While a U.S. Senate committee voted in favor of a similar move in September, a full-time Senate general election has yet to be determined.
Demonstrations in Hong Kong, which erupted in June 2019, continue to escalate every weekend. The Chinese government has criticized the United States for making such "blindfolded support" the rise of Hong Kong protesters.
