This recommendation was made at the opening ceremony of the 12th ASEAN-China Attorney General Conference held in Siem Reap this morning, November 6, 2019 under the theme "The role of prosecutors in the fight against trafficking. "People in the area."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Recommendations for the 12th ASEAN-China Attorney General's Conference are as follows:
1. The ASEAN-China Attorney General shall work closely with institutional and country-related issues related to "human trafficking", especially in transit and target countries, in order to respond and resolve them in a timely manner. Efficiency and transparency.
2. The ASEAN-China Attorney General shall jointly examine and evaluate the issue of "human trafficking" through a high sense of responsibility, quality and efficiency with the country and of the previously signed agreements.
3. The ASEAN-China Attorney General and relevant institutions shall continue to work together to increase and expand cooperation, facilitate and provide resources for systematic operations in order to respond in a timely manner on "human trafficking" with high efficiency. .
4. The ASEAN-China Attorney General shall jointly record and compile a report with concrete evidence to demonstrate joint efforts with relevant institutions to participate in the fight against human trafficking, which is a crime endangering society and affecting To the process of socio-economic development in the region and the world.
The ASEAN-China Attorney General's Conference is a forum for regional prosecutors to share experiences and best practices in combating, preventing, cracking down and punishing transnational crime, including "human trafficking". It is also a mechanism for strengthening cooperation between ASEAN countries and China.
The 12th ASEAN-China Attorney General's Conference is now to find a solution as well as joint cooperation, and finally the ASEAN-China Attorney General will issue a joint declaration as a basis for implementation in accordance with the UN Convention. Nations on the fight against transnational crime. New branch of Honda Ing Popi motorcycle officially opened in Phnom Penh
