Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the Occasion of the Opening Ceremony of the 12th ASEAN-China Attorney General Conference in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on Wednesday morning, November 6, 2019, presided over the opening ceremony of the 12th ASEAN-China Attorney General Conference held in Siem Reap.
The 12th ASEAN-China Attorney General Conference will be held under the theme "The Role of Prosecutors in Combating Human Trafficking in the Region".
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that today Cambodia is honored to host this important conference at a time when ASEAN member countries as well as countries in the region are working together to combat human trafficking. Transnational crime is dangerous and is rampant in our region.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the prevention, suppression and punishment of "human trafficking" is an important policy that the Royal Government has focused on and implemented in the past through the dissemination of all forms of "human trafficking." Human Trafficking ”from the national to the grassroots level.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the fight against "human trafficking" is difficult and complicated and is a transnational crime and a crime that extends to both the ASEAN region and the world.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order to fight this "human trafficking" in a timely manner, ASEAN-China member countries must have a common principle, unite, cooperate closely, effectively and transparently.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in 2024, ASEAN will host the World Cup. ASEAN can form a team to the World Cup, an identity of ASEAN.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that ASEAN is a single community but has separate laws that make it difficult to combat human trafficking. Possible.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also gave four recommendations to join the fight against "human trafficking" more effectively. The four recommendations include:
1. The ASEAN-China Attorney General shall work closely with institutional and country-related issues related to "human trafficking", especially in transit and target countries, in order to respond and resolve them in a timely, effective and timely manner. Transparency.
2. The ASEAN-China Attorney General must jointly examine and evaluate the issue of "human trafficking" through a high sense of responsibility, quality and efficiency with the country and the previously signed agreements.
3. The ASEAN-China Attorney General and relevant institutions should continue to work together to expand and expand cooperation, facilitate and contribute resources for systematic operations to be able to respond in a timely manner on "human trafficking" with high efficiency.
4 The ASEAN-China Attorney General shall jointly record and compile a report with concrete evidence to demonstrate joint efforts with relevant institutions to participate in the fight against human trafficking, which is a crime endangering society and affecting Regional and global socio-economic development processes.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Vietnam has more than 200,000 workers in South Korea.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that Cambodian workers go to work in South Korea, despite the proper organization of the exam, there are still some scammers.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government is clearly carrying out a criminal political reform. Samdech Techo continued that although the judiciary is an independent system, but if the Royal Government does not have a clear criminal policy, it will endanger the functioning of the state.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia has chosen a system in which there is a consistent cooperation between the judiciary and the executive branch to govern a consistent state.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen hopes that the Conference will continue to use the ASEAN-China Attorney General's Mechanism, a forum to strengthen co-operation and defense cooperation in the fight against "human trafficking" and all forms of transnational crime to ensure Cross-border security and safety to population issues in ASEAN-China and in the region.
