(Dongdong, Indonesia): On the morning of November 5, 2019, Mr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions, attended the opening ceremony of the World Zakat Forum (Donation) in Bandung, Republic of Indonesia.
The eighth forum will run for three days from November 5 to 7 in Bandung, Republic of Indonesia, chaired by Prof. Dr. MA’RUF AMIN, Vice President of the Republic of Indonesia.
Key topics will be discussed, such as strengthening the role of the World Zakat Forum through the digital age, the role of the Islamic Development Bank in supporting the development of digital Zakat, the management of digital Zakat, the role of digital Zakat in the project. National for Economic Development of Islam and Kazakhstan in strengthening multilateral humanitarian cooperation.
The forum was attended by about 350 participants, including speakers, researchers, leaders of various Zakat institutions from 35 countries. Senior Minister Osman Hassan will also be a guest speaker at the forum.
Please be informed that this forum was officially established in 2010 in order to facilitate the Zakat institution in managing Zakat effectively, transparently, accurately and fairly, especially for the accuracy in managing and providing Zakat through digital technology.
Zakat is the fourth obligation of Islam for Muslims around the world, that is, those who have all the assets to be removed Zakat within a year must withdraw 2.5% of their assets according to the rules. Islam is given to the poor, widows, orphans, the elderly and those who are entitled to Zakat.
