(Battambang): On the afternoon of November 5, 2019, Ms. Soeum Yeap, Chief of Tapon Commune, Sangke District, representatives of all the people thanked Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology for always helping them solve their water problems. Timely through Mr. Long Phalkun, Director of the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology and Deputy Chairman of the National Task Force to help Tapon commune.
At the same time, Mr. Long Phalkun said that as the Director of the Department of Skills and received recommendations from the Minister to serve the people in the irrigation sector at the target of reservoirs and main canals in the province. The whole of Battambang.
He added that according to the recommendation of the Minister also regularly recommended to save water by implementing when there is no water, a professional team to pump water into the main canal, secondary drainage for people to use daily, but if there is Flooding is to pump back the reservoir to store water when the dry season lacks water.
He added that today he and his team visited the pumping site at the irrigation system, Badak Reservoir is an ancient reservoir built a long time ago, located in the village. Basset, Tapon commune, Sangke district, Battambang province, about 13 km east of Battambang city.
The Badak Reservoir covers an area of more than 19 hectares and is surrounded by a 1,800-meter-long, 3-meter-high pool. The Badak Reservoir holds water for growing during the dry season and it receives water during the flood season. It was rehabilitated by the Royal Government in 2012 and received the Royal Government's budget for operation and maintenance work From 2015.
