Nearly 20,000 Armed Forces to Be Deployed to Maintain Security and Order During Water Festival
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia will deploy a total of nearly 20,000 armed forces to maintain security and order during the Royal Water Festival, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon in Phnom Penh, which will be held from The 10th to the 13th of November 2019. This is according to the spokesperson of the General Commission of the National Police.
He said that in addition to the nearly 20,000 armed forces, the Royal Government has prepared other special forces to protect and intervene at Phnom Penh International Airport to arrest people with court orders.
In response to the suggestion that the Royal Government uses more force than in previous years, Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun claimed that there was not much, just that in previous years, the National Independence Day was not in line with the Royal Ceremony. No Water Festival, but this year the Independence Day is in line with the Water Festival, so the authorities use total force.
The Deputy National Police Commissioner stressed that the number of security forces at the Royal Water Festival did not include other special forces to carry out arrest warrants for traitors at Phnom Penh International Airport.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun emphasized that the reinforcements also coincided with the announcement of the traitors that they would return to Cambodia. He stressed that the number of nearly 20,000 armed forces is enough to maintain security during the National Independence Day and Royal Water Festival. China: Because only one woman made a pilot lose his job for life!
