"Sea levels will continue to rise despite our efforts to curb greenhouse gases," scientists warn.
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - Experts warn that sea levels will continue to rise even as the world manages to reduce greenhouse gas emissions to zero by 2030 due to the Earth's ozone layer. The lost can not be repaired in hundreds of years. This was released by CNA on Tuesday morning, November 5, 2019.
According to researchers from Germany, sea level could rise by 8 cm by 2100 and may increase to 20 cm by 2300. In addition, although the world could reduce greenhouse gas emissions to zero by 2030, sea levels are still projected to rise by at least "one meter" by 2300. .
