(Kampong Speu): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie, on the morning of November 5, 2019, gave a lecture on the structure and assignment of the duties of the Gendarmerie at the Military Academy. Active. The ceremony was also attended by several leaders of the Royal Gendarmerie.
Please be informed that the Gendarmerie was established during 1957 during the Sangkum Reastr Niyum regime, which was renamed the Khmer Gendarmerie and was renamed the National Gendarmerie during 1971 during the Khmer Lon Nol regime, then abolished. Abolished like other institutions during the genocidal regime of Pol Pot from 1975 to 1979.
The Royal Cambodian Armed Forces was reborn by a decree issued on July 14, 1993, with the unification of the National Army. At that time, the Gendarmerie was only responsible for the military sheriff and was actively involved in cracking down on many major crimes. Since 1994, the Royal Government has issued Sub-Decree No. 77 on the General Structural Duties of the Royal Gendarmerie.
The Royal Gendarmerie has been asked to carry out a series of organizational reforms under the leadership of General Sao Sokha, Commander of the National Gendarmerie, in order to clearly define the working system, roles, duties, hierarchy, and efficiency.
In the past as well as now, the Royal Gendarmerie continues to work hard to overcome all circumstances and obstacles to fulfill its mission day by day to participate in maintaining security, social order, safety for the people, crime research, cooperation and strengthening implementation. The law will rescue people in the event of a catastrophe in line with the slogan "The army is the people, the people serve the people."
