National AIDS Authority Holds Second Plenary Meeting in 2019
(Phnom Penh): The National AIDS Authority held its second plenary session in 2019, chaired by Mr. Ieng Moly, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and Chairman of the National AIDS Authority, on Tuesday morning. Ek Sak BE 2563 is on November 5, 2019 at the meeting hall of the Friendship Monument of the Office of the Council of Ministers.
The Plenary Meeting of the National AIDS Authority is a semi-annual meeting attended by the Secretary of State, the Deputy Governor of the Capital and Provinces, the Chairperson of the AIDS Committee, the Ministries, Institutions and the Capital-Provincial Administration and the members of the Policy Council. Multidisciplinary fight against AIDS.
The purpose of the meeting is to review the current status of the HIV epidemic in the second half of 2019 and to review the results of the fight against HIV / AIDS achieved in the second half of 2019. The Plenary also discussed and decided to set a multi-sectoral policy direction for the fight against HIV / AIDS for the first half of 2020.
The Senior Minister reminded the Plenary Meeting that the Royal Government of Cambodia has achieved the highly committed principle of eradicating HIV / AIDS by clearly setting three zero goals: "No new HIV infections, no discrimination." For people living with HIV "and" no deaths from AIDS "by 2025.
"We have been traveling together with a clear vision in the real hope of eradicating AIDS," he said. This is because Cambodia already has a high level of efficiency, which is the political commitment of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
After listening to the report, the presentation and after discussing and exchanging opinions, our Plenary Meeting:
The Senior Minister expressed his appreciation and encouragement to the Ministry of Economy and Finance to continue to increase and facilitate the use of the national budget in the fight against HIV / AIDS and to assist the Capital-Provincial AIDS Fighting Committee to continue to promote and cooperate with Sub-national administrations, especially commune / sangkat authorities in implementing "Notification No. 213 NSC" for implementation in sub-national administrations.
