The agreement was reached at the 3rd Comprehensive Economic Partnership Summit on the afternoon of November 4, 2019 in Thailand.
RCEP is an economic cooperation partner formed to address difficult issues such as digital commerce, regulatory reform, open trade and mobility of skilled workers.
At the summit, RCEP leaders praised the efforts of RCEP ministers and their working groups to achieve a modern, comprehensive, high-quality and special RCEP agreement. Special and distinct karma for less developed countries.
Leaders also hailed the current achievement of the RCEP as a historic milestone for the entire Asia-Pacific region after the RCEP leadership announced the formal opening of talks in the city. Phnom Penh in 2012, although there are still some technical issues that need to be resolved before going through the internal procedures for signing in Vietnam in 2020.
Like the ASEAN leaders, the Prime Minister said that although Cambodia is a less developed country, there may be a need for a number of laws, economic and administrative structures after the agreement comes into force, but he still makes decisions. It is with great pleasure that the Cambodian Minister is given the mandate to sign the RCEP Agreement in 2020.
At the summit, the leaders of the RCEP countries issued a statement from the chair of the meeting on the RCEP Comprehensive Regional Economic Partnership Negotiations.
