Baghdad: Iraqi security forces on Monday opened fire with live ammunition on a crowd of protesters in the capital, Baghdad, killing five people. This was released by Reuters on Monday, November 4, 2019.
Protests in Iraq have erupted since early October, with protesters demanding that the Baghdad government address corruption and their daily lives. But during the protests, violence also erupted between authorities and protesters, leaving more than 250 people dead.
