Samdech Techo Hun Sen Attends the 14th East Asia Summit
(Bangkok, Thailand): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the afternoon of November 4, 2019, attended the 14th East Asia Summit to discuss various issues. The East Asia Summit is an important meeting of the 10 ASEAN members and eight other major countries of the world: China, Russia, Japan, the United States, Canada, South Korea, Australia and India.
At the meeting, the Heads of State and Government of the East Asian countries acknowledged that the East Asia Summit has indeed played an increasingly active role in shaping the region due to its relevance and effectiveness in responding to rapid changes in the region. International.
The leaders also considered that the 14th meeting was very important for all leaders to think and stand together, adhering to the theories of regionalism and multilateralism, which are the principles and framework. It is important for the common interest and cooperation to address the challenges that are emerging in all aspects.
The leaders also urged all parties concerned to resume peaceful dialogue and continue to work together, which will lead to the realization of lasting peace and stability on the Korean Peninsula through the full and speedy implementation of The Panmunjom Declaration, the Pyongyang Joint Declaration and the Joint Statement between the United States and the Democratic People's Republic of Korea are complete and expeditious.
The leaders also welcomed the progress made in negotiating a comprehensive regional economic partnership agreement and encouraged all parties to step up efforts to resolve outstanding issues and conclude negotiations on the agreement. That is fast as we reaffirm ASEAN's highest priority and commitment to conclude negotiations on the agreement by 2019.
