The meeting and discussion between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Robert O'Brien, Special Representative of President Donald Trump, showed the good relations, friendship and closeness between the leaders of Cambodia and the United States.
ASEAN member states include only the prime ministers of Thailand, Laos and Vietnam, while the other seven members, including Cambodia, send only foreign ministers and senior officials.
Despite the absence of the US President and some ASEAN Heads of State and Government, the meeting proceeded as planned.
At the 7th ASEAN-US Annual Summit, the ASEAN Heads of State and Government and the Special Envoy of the President of the United States of America carefully discussed the planned agenda. In particular, carefully examined and discussed on promoting the strengthening of ASEAN-US cooperation.
At the summit, ASEAN and US leaders praised the progress of ASEAN-US relations. The ASEAN and US leaders also stressed the importance of promoting partnerships with dialogue partners, sectoral dialogue partners, development partners and other external parties through each framework and implementation of joint action plans. Transactions.
ASEAN leaders encouraged the United States to continue to support the implementation of the ASEAN Connectivity Master Plan 2025 and the ASEAN Integration Initiative Phase III, which focuses on connectivity to help bridge the development gap between ASEAN member states and promote Connect the regions to achieve the ASEAN Community Vision 2025.
ASEAN leaders also praised the new technical assistance program between ASEAN and the United States Agency for International Development on the ASEAN Economic Community (AEC) through the Trade and e-Commerce Innovation for 2019-2023, which will continue to enhance Building the ASEAN Community.
At the summit, ASEAN and US leaders issued a statement by the chair of the 7th ASEAN-US Summit and adopted the ASEAN-US Leaders' Declaration on Energy Security.
