The international conference was attended by about 350 specialists, including 50 international urologists from about 20 different countries and about 300 local Chinese specialists.
The meeting was held to share experiences with each other on the application of modern techniques in urinary tract surgery, which allowed all the participating doctors to have a good new experience from the countries that have been. Participate, especially the experience of the host country China.
Dr. Sot Phearum added, "In modern surgical techniques, China can do everything, but these experiences are rarely shared with countries in the region and the world because they use Chinese and English." "Used for communication is not very widespread."
Dr. Khmer, a specialist in urinary tract surgery, added that China warmly welcomed doctors from Cambodia, with Prof. Dr. Li Chongming very pleased to see the presence of Cambodian doctors at the meeting. This is the first time and next year he will invite three Cambodian doctors to establish a good traditional relationship.
In addition, he promised to provide short training courses on kidney surgery to Cambodian students and doctors who wish to study and gain experience in kidney surgery in Kunming.
On the occasion of attending the meeting in China, Dr. Sot Phearum conveyed the memories of the Professor, Director and Deputy Director of the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital and invited Professor Dr. Li Chongming and his team to visit in person. Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital. In response, the professor promised to come soon.
Taking this opportunity, Dr. Sot Phearum advised the medical students and the next generation of doctors not to value study only in European countries such as the United States and Australia, should turn to countries in Asia, especially China, which has medical development, is not inferior to other famous countries.
He also thanked the leadership of the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital for its efforts in developing both human and material resources, and in particular the Ministry of Health's efforts to rapidly develop Cambodia's health sector over time. Last year.
