(Bangkok, Thailand): Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak has submitted two separate proposals to the United States and China to help boost Cambodia's economy. Minister Panzer Sak's proposal to the United States is to increase investment in Cambodia by encouraging US investors to study more investment feasibility. The proposal to China is to help import more Cambodian agricultural products to the Chinese market.
According to the Ministry of Commerce, a working meeting between the Minister of Commerce and the Deputy Minister of Commerce of China was held on Sunday, November 3, 2019. The meeting discussed a number of tasks aimed at strengthening and expanding economic and trade cooperation between the two countries.
The Minister asked the Chinese side to examine the possibility of importing more Cambodian agricultural products such as rice, mango, banana, cassava and some other important agricultural products. In response, the Chinese side highly valued the close cooperation between Cambodia and China and pledged to further promote bilateral trade.
The meeting between the Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, and the US Ambassador, Patrick Mofi, was held this morning, November 4, 2019. During the meeting, the Minister requested the US Ambassador to encourage more US businesses to invest in Cambodia, as well as to participate in trade fairs and business matching to boost trade.
The Ambassador praised the cooperation between the two sides and pledged to further enhance economic and trade ties.
