CDX cooperates with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and the Svay Rieng Provincial Administration to share knowledge in seizing investment opportunities to the public
(Svay Rieng): The Cambodian Derivatives Exchange (CDX) in collaboration with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and the Svay Rieng Provincial Administration organized a workshop in Svay Rieng on the topic of “Derivatives Trading: Investment Preparation and Awareness. Relevant? » By contributing to share knowledge about derivatives trading to the public as well.
This workshop is the ninth goal of the provincial seminar in 2019 and was organized with the participation of Mr. Sok Dara, Deputy Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and Mr. Sok Ros, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Provincial Board of Governors.
These provincial workshops aim to share knowledge, skills, experience, regulations and investment opportunities to the public in Cambodia.
Mr. Sok Ros highlighted the potential of Svay Rieng and the attention of the Royal Government in the development of all sectors, especially the economic sector, which is reflected in the economic reforms that help Cambodia to be growing. The economy is around 7% per year.
Mr. Sok Ros also expects the participants to gain more financial knowledge, especially in the derivatives market.
Mr. Sok Dara also presented the current situation of the derivatives market in Cambodia, as well as the position of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia in further developing the derivatives market. He encouraged investors to increase their knowledge and be ready to invest in derivatives to contribute to national economic development.
It should be noted that Cambodian Derivatives Exchange and the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia have already cooperated with the provincial administration in organizing workshops in 14 provinces, including: Sihanoukville, Kampong Cham, Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang and Takeo. Kampot, Kep, Kampong Chhnang, Pursat, Pailin, Kandal, Prey Veng and Svay Rieng provinces.
