Mr. Dmitry Medvedev's statement was made during a working meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the afternoon of November 3, 2019 in Thailand, where the two Prime Ministers attended the ASEAN Summit and Relevant meetings.
According to Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, during the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Prime Minister of Russia expressed their pleasure to meet again, especially in the framework of international forums.
The Russian Prime Minister stated that Cambodia is a close friend of Russia. The Prime Minister expressed the expectation that the relations between the two countries will be closer by continuing to further expand cooperation and bilateral relations, especially between the government and the government and other frameworks.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Russia for its continued cooperation in a number of areas, including culture. Samdech Techo also thanked Russia for supporting Cambodia to become an observer country of the Shanghai Cooperation Organization and for providing training to Cambodian military officers and providing technical assistance in the field of demining.
The Prime Minister also expressed his pleasure at the increase in trade between the two countries. In this regard, in order to further strengthen the trade volume, Samdech Techo asked the Russian Prime Minister to encourage Russian investors to invest more in Cambodia in areas such as food processing, agro-industry, electronics industry, packaging industry and machinery industry. And so on.
He also asked the Russian side to consider the possibility of launching a project to modernize the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital in the near future, as this hospital is a symbol of long-term friendship between our two countries.
Regarding the negotiation of a free trade agreement between Cambodia and the Eurasian Economic Union, Samdech Techo thanked Russia for its principled support for the efforts to negotiate a free trade agreement between Cambodia and the Eurasian Economic Union. As Cambodia hosts the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting in 2020, Samdech Techo also invited the Prime Minister of Russia to attend the meeting.
The Russian Prime Minister also replied that Russia wants to cooperate with Cambodia in many fields, including industry, and would like to continue to support Cambodia in energy cooperation, such as oil, telecommunications, fisheries and the establishment of cooperation. Other operations in Cambodia.
Regarding free trade between Cambodia and the Eurasian Economic Union, he stressed that this is a very important task and a good initiative to sign an agreement in the near future after negotiations. The Minister also stated that Cambodia and Russia can have good cooperation in the fields of industry, science and other fields. Especially in demining in the field of defense, which Russia wants to continue in the training of Cambodian military officers.
Regarding the hospital, the Russian Prime Minister stressed that this is an important project and Russia will work hard to do this work, the sooner the better. On this occasion, the Prime Minister also thanked Samdech Techo Prime Minister for helping to promote cooperation in many fields between Cambodia and Russia. Especially in the ASEAN framework, where Cambodia has been heavily involved in the ASEAN framework and Russia for further cooperation.
Regarding the Asia-Europe Summit in 2020, the Russian Prime Minister thanked Samdech Techo Prime Minister for inviting him to attend the meeting in Phnom Penh next year and he will attend.
Regarding the training sector, the Russian Prime Minister stated that Russia will continue to support the education and training sector to Cambodia. The Prime Minister stated that next year, 2020, Russia will increase the number of scholarships for Cambodian students.
At the end of the meeting, Samdech Techo stated that he was pleased that the cooperation between the two countries was going well and would continue to deepen bilateral relations.
Regarding human resource training, Samdech Techo highlighted it as a priority area of the government and he also thanked the Prime Minister for pushing for more scholarships as well as human resource training in Cambodia.
The Russian Prime Minister stressed that all this work, especially this training, is the basis of friendship between our two countries, and we respect each other and have mutual understanding.
