Preah Sihanouk Provincial Authority, Traffic Police and Partner Organizations Organize Traffic Law Dissemination Campaign to Reduce Accidents During Water Festival
(Preah Sihanouk): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration, Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police and its partners have organized a traffic safety education campaign and enforcement of road traffic law, focusing on the impact of driving under the influence. Local alcohol in Preah Sihanouk province on November 2, 2019.
This campaign aims to raise public awareness through road safety education, focusing on the risks of driving under the influence of alcohol, to join the Royal Government of Cambodia in reducing the number of deaths and injuries caused by traffic accidents during During the Royal Water Festival 2019.
After the opening of the traffic safety education campaign, the youth group of the Cambodian Red Cross and all relevant partners who participated in the program continued to promote traffic safety by distributing posters and vehicle stickers to the people in the market for parking taxis and motorcycles. Tricycles, restaurants on the main streets, as well as the setting of traffic police targets to disseminate this educational content.
The campaign also features banners with the slogan "Do not drink alcohol, do not drive," a number of educational messages on social media, highlighting the consequences of driving after drinking alcohol, as well as distributing educational leaflets to your people. Travelers are aware of the wrong behavior that can lead to accidents while traveling and avoid making those mistakes.
Sihanoukville Provincial Hall, APIWSA and all participating partners expect that the results of this traffic safety education will be able to prevent the number of deaths and serious injuries due to traffic accidents during major festivals. Decreased than previous years.
