Legal Awareness: Peace
(Phnom Penh): In general, every person at the time of survival is, of course, striving for wealth, gold, silver, land, houses, etc., and at the same time there are some passive assets such as debts.
And when that person dies, those assets and liabilities go to his relatives, and the relatives take care of them and divide them, which is called "peacekeeping". . Therefore, in order to know exactly what kind of mediation is legal and effective?
This week, Fresh News' Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, brings the topic of "peace" to the public as follows:
According to the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the peace process begins with the death of the heir (deceased person). The place of settlement shall begin at the place of death of the heir at the time of death.
The initiation of a settlement gives effect to the inheritance of property rights as well as other rights and obligations from the heirs. Inheritance is the property, inheritance that an individual (heir) leaves behind after death.
A person who is to inherit is called a successor, a person who is to inherit the rights and obligations of the heirs through inheritance. The successor shall inherit all rights and obligations under the property of the heir from the beginning of the settlement, except for the rights and exclusive rights of the heir.
In that case, the descendants also have the right to abandon the inheritance according to the conditions and time determined by law. By law, in the absence of relatives and people of a special nature, all inheritance must become the property of the state.
Not all individuals can be intimidated by law, according to the law, in order to qualify as immigrants, they must be alive at the beginning of the civil war, in addition to the unfortunate individual and the person who has been deprived of inheritance or a baby in Fetal if the baby is alive at birth later.
A successor is a person who inherits a person who is a relative but dies before the beginning of the war or is unfortunate or a person who has been deprived of his inheritance, for example, and the descendants of the successor must become the descendants. Instead. And in the absence of a kinsman, a person with a special nature is a person who is not a kinsman but lives with the heirs or a person who has tried to treat the heirs.
2: Types of Peace
In the event that the heir dies without a heir (no word) or in the case where the heir is annulled or annulled, the division of the inheritance shall be done by legal means. Cambodian law prescribes the methods of information distribution, such as determining the share of inheritance, the method of facilitating the share of inheritance, determining the heirs, determining the share of inheritance to be received by each successor, and how The division of inheritance, for example.
B. Inheritance or Word
Because Cambodian law respects the principle of autonomy of private individuals, the law recognizes the will of the heirs as long as they live in the free management of their property. This means that while living, the heir intends to manage his property in such a way that after his death, that will is respected and obeyed.
In summary, a deed is a system of division of property that is guaranteed by law in order to protect the rights and interests of the person involved in the deceased person, especially on that person's property, including assets and passive assets. .
