Senior Ministry of Health official warns state doctors not to take patients to private clinics because it is illegal and dangerous for victims
(Koh Kong): The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Health, Prof. Thea Kruy, has issued an oral warning to all medical teams in Cambodia to ban patients from public hospitals in their private clinics, stating that such conduct is It is unethical for professionals to cause high casualties, especially in the face of the law.
The warning was issued by the 4th Medical Career Development Day in Koh Kong province on November 1, 2019.
He stressed that if they continue to commit crimes and endanger the safety of patients and face the law, they will not be able to escape the case of causing the patient to die in any way. Doctors who are working to save people do not claim to be strong or selfish, endangering patients' safety by transporting patients to their own clinics, which is illegal and unethical. As a doctor.
The Secretary of State for Health notes that although a large number of physicians today adhere to professional roles and professional ethics, a small number are still lazy by referring patients who are being treated in public hospitals to clinics. Other factors that greatly affect the safety and well-being of patients, while the private sector does not have enough medical equipment to provide medical treatment.
In response to the warnings of the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, Dr. Ho So Huon, Director of Sre Ambel District Referral Hospital and Dr. Pin Serey Vattanak, Deputy Director of Koh Kong Provincial Referral Department, jointly claimed that the phenomenon of sending patients to the home or clinic of doctors is not. This is because the hospital management has introduced new measures in line with the guidelines of many ministries and health departments to the current medical team.
All state health service managers point out that their referral hospitals have been taking care of patients and providing them with medical, diagnostic, ethical, and state-of-the-art medical equipment to increase their confidence. Come for service if the patient's condition is too serious and will be sent to the emergency room in Phnom Penh.
In mid-September, Dr. Toa Moeng requested that all people in Koh Kong province need to be examined and treated at health centers, provincial referral hospitals or private clinics licensed by The Department of Health avoids any health hazards and post declarations. For any private health service unit that has expired its license, the license must be issued immediately to renew its validity.
According to the report of the Koh Kong Provincial Health Department for August 2019, there are currently a total of 110 pharmacies, outpatient services, dental and eye care facilities. In the past, they cracked down and temporarily closed two dental clinics in Cam Phoumin City.
Each year, the Ministry of Health of Cambodia conducts training to increase the professional capacity of senior doctors in the capitals and provinces in order to strengthen the methods of diagnosing and treating patients who have experienced and do not have the skills. Important specialties for doctors to keep up with the situation.
