Mr. Steng Sokhom calls on young people to seize new opportunities, which are the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia for the people
(Prey Veng): Dr. Steng Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Task Force for Kamchay Mear District, encouraged young people at Hun Sen Kamchay Mear High School in Prey Veng to seize new opportunities. The Royal Government's efforts, especially the new approaches and approaches of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, while Cambodia is actively participating in integration at both the regional and global levels.
Dr. Steng Sokhom encouraged this on the occasion of the opening ceremony of the new school year 2019-2020 at Hun Sen Kamchay Mear High School, Kamchay Mear District, Prey Veng Province this morning, November 1, 2019, with the participation of Mr. and Mrs. Vice President. National Team Visited Kamchay Mear District, District Governor, Chairman, Deputy Chief of District Office, Commune Chief, Commune Council, Teachers, Students and Parents of approximately 2,133 students.
Dr. Steng Sokhom highlighted the important content in the opening message of the new school year 2019-2020 by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, which completely covered the development of education in Cambodia. "In that message, the key people who encourage young people and children to go to school are parents, guardians, the community and teachers," he said.
He added that the Royal Government has considered human resource training as the first of the four priorities set out in the Rectangular Strategy for implementation at all stages. The Royal Government also urged the Ministry of Education to deepen reforms and support new approaches and approaches of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
He said that the new approaches and approaches of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports show the goal of increasing the competitiveness of Cambodian youth in seizing new opportunities while Cambodia actively participates in integration at both the regional and global levels. At this point, he called on all students to seize this opportunity to increase their capacity to become a dynamic resource.
He also suggested the establishment of study clubs, professional groups to help high school students, especially those who lack the ability to learn more. Dr. Steng Sokhom also gave advice to all students and young people to work hard to learn and support all activities related to education. Instead, all students must stay away from drug use and other vicious acts.
Dr. continued that the Royal Government led by the People's Party has worked hard to build a lot of achievements, especially in the last two decades after the country is completely peaceful. In fact, in the field of education, the Royal Government has pushed schools closer to people's homes and deployed them all over the country for the sole purpose of encouraging people's children to attend school.
The Chairman of the Working Group also confirmed that since the country has achieved full peace since 1998 under the victorious policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Cambodian people have benefited greatly from this peace. Everyone can travel anywhere and anytime without worries and fears like before.
Citizens have all the freedom to do business, eat and work according to their preferences and choose the place they want. Young people choose to study according to the skills and places they want. The growth of the national economy and the macroeconomic stability of the country have gradually improved the lives of the people. All this is due to the peace factor, which is the sacred objective of every Cambodian citizen.
He claimed that Sam Rainsy's actions were an attempt to destroy peace, political stability, incitement to violence and internal separatist movements. Thus, the plan to return to Cambodia by Sam Rainsy and his cronies is a purely rebel movement that will lead to the destruction of peace and the disintegration of the nation, which can cause unpredictable catastrophe to the nation and its people. Cambodians.
The Chairman of the National Working Group explained to the people, teachers and students that Sam Rainsy's plan to return to Cambodia now is very different from the activities of Sam Rainsy's return to Cambodia in 2013, which At that time, Sam Rainsy, the president of a legitimate political party, came to the polls to receive a royal pardon, but this time, Sam Rainsy was a prisoner and a rebel leader.
