(Preah Vihear): Various materials used for forest patrol work to protect natural resources were handed over by Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to 4 community forests this morning, November 1, 2019 in the presence of Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and other relevant officials.
Mr. Peng Trida said that today, four more community forests have received materials to support forest patrols after six communities received materials last month, including two communities in Kulen district and four communities in the district. Cleft.
Mr. Peng Trida confirmed that the equipment supporting the forest patrol came from the Royal Government's 2019 program budget. These items include: hammocks, parachute shoes, raincoats, backpacks, parachutes, Korean tents, GPS scarves, desks, chairs and a total of 14 office supplies.
