A-level students in Oddar Meanchey province receive a house from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit
(Oddar Meanchey): A poor A-level student in Trapeang Prasat district, Oddar Meanchey province, received a house from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
Keo Ponleu is the only student from Oddar Meanchey province who received an A grade during the exam period in August 2019. Ponleu lives in Toul Krasaing village, Trapeang Prasat commune, Trapeang Prasat district, Oddar Meanchey province. Light living in a poor family, even housing is not suitable.
After receiving information about the poverty in Ponleu's life, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit provided a house for Ponleu and her family to be a warm home.
On October 1, 2019, Mr. Nget Chanthol, Deputy Chief of Trapeang Prasat District Assistance Team, after receiving guidance from Senior Minister Kun Kim, Chairman of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Assistance Team, has started to lead the construction team.
Seeing the difficulty in entering and leaving the house, Mr. Nget Chanthon decided to help pour soil and build a 1,000-meter-long entrance to the house at a cost of $ 2,000. The house will be completed in 15 days.
