Minister of Environment reveals the value of earthworms
Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, on November 1, 2019, highlighted the value of earthworms in the ecosystem that most people do not know.
The Minister of Environment explained that earthworms have acted as consumers, waste movers and modifiers in the ecosystem. Earthworms have a number of beneficial and beneficial effects on soil ecosystems, including: First, the processing of organic matter in which earthworms, along with bacteria and fungi, decompose organic matter; It causes tiny holes known as pores in the soil.
Mr. Say Samal added that these activities of earthworms have helped to create different types of soil in those holes or the soil around them, and through this it has changed the biological, chemical and physical processes of the system. Ecology.
Please note that the food that worms like to eat the most is the leaves and plants. In addition, it feeds on the carcasses of all kinds of rotting creatures, including small insects such as earthworms, mosquitoes, flies and mosquitoes. Researchers found that of the 1,200 worms, it was possible to dissolve one kilogram of waste in just four days.
According to some sources, in China, earthworms are used as a medicine, can be used as a tonic, aphrodisiac, or in New Zealand, earthworms are used as a valuable and tasty food. One of a kind. In some countries, earthworms are raised as food for animals such as frogs, fish and pigs because of their high protein content.
Some countries, such as the European Union and China, import large quantities of earthworms, while the United States is the largest exporter of earthworms.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong and Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An initiate a fundraiser to build achievements at Wat Tuol Sangke
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong and Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection and Ms. Annie Sok An, Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross, on November 1, 2019, initiated a charity event. To collect suffixes to build achievements in Tuol Sangke pagoda.
On the evening of November 1, 2019, the two Deputy Prime Ministers and the Buddhist leaders at the foot of the pagoda as the initiators of the ceremony were invited to participate in the blessing ceremony according to Buddhist advice, and on November 2, 2019, tomorrow, the procession Kathina Samaki goes to give to monks who remember the rainy season for three quarters in Buddha Seima to collect suffixes to build achievements as pedagogy in Wat Tuol Sangke, located in Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
The organization of this Kathina Initiative also dedicated all the merits that come from the generosity of this solidarity Kathina to the ancestors of the seven relatives who have passed away to the next world, as well as the merits to His Excellency Lok Chumteav, Lok Oknha, Ladies and Gentlemen and Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda are the initiators of the festival. May you prosper forever.
In the Cambodian market, SCG's sales revenue for the third quarter of 2019 reached 455 billion riels (US $ 111 million), an increase of 14%, most of which was From the cement-construction materials business.
Cambodia's economy continued to grow strongly during the third quarter of this year. Foreign direct investment inflows, especially from China, are driving the growth of the construction sector as a whole. In Phnom Penh and in some of Cambodia's major cities, such as Sihanoukville, Poipet and Bavet, demand remains high for cement products and construction materials.
For recent activities in Cambodia, SCG has recently developed a new formula for K-Cement products. This is an innovation that increases production capacity to meet the growing market demand in Cambodia and helps reduce CO2 emissions through the most efficient use of resources.
In particular, the operating results of SCG as a whole for the third quarter of 2019 and for the first nine months of 2019 showed a decrease in profit compared to the same period last year. This was mainly due to the decline in profits in the chemical products business due to the already low demand cycle, the slowdown in the global economy caused by trade wars and the appreciation of the Thai baht.
Meanwhile, the cement-construction materials business reported a profit growth driven by sales growth in the distribution and retail business. Moreover, the packaging business has also shown strong growth potential, especially in the ASEAN market.
