The United States has decided to "impose more sanctions on Iran" to prevent the development of its nuclear program (Video inside) (Washington): The United States confirmed on Thursday that new sanctions have been dropped on Iran, which the United States aims to impose The burden is on construction and commercial companies that produce four types of equipment for use in nuclear applications. This was released by CNA on Friday afternoon, November 1, 2019.
The announcement was made by the State Department in response to its previous commitment to exacerbate economic pressure against the Tehran regime while the door to diplomatic talks continued. It would make it more difficult for Iran's nuclear facilities to achieve nuclear weapons if the Islamic State were to follow US accusations.
Donald Trump's administration in 2018 decided to pull the United States out of the Iran nuclear deal, which was reached by six powers (the United States, China, Russia, Britain, France and Germany) in Paris in 2015. The withdrawal comes after the United States accused Iran of never abiding by the agreement, and the nuclear deal undermined the US economy and influence.
