This image has disappeared from Cambodian territory for many years after Cambodian society ended the war for about 20 years. Similar images were seen during the 2008 armed clashes with Thais at the Preah Vihear temple.
These gestures show the strong support of the people, the so-called post-battle, to support and strengthen the army that went out to defend the country from the enemy. This morning's image has attracted a lot of attention from the public and is also a reflection of the spirit of the people who love and need peace and stability in Cambodian society for the past 20 years.
