Be careful! A woman was electrocuted while charging her mobile phone.
(Central): A woman was electrocuted and lost her life because she was charging her mobile phone, playing with her phone and wearing headphones, which caused an electric shock at the scene.
This incident happened on November 1, 2019 at 8:10 AM at rented house No. 32, Sitbo village, Sitbo commune, Takhmao city, Kandal province. Victim name: An Sokna, 33 years old, Occupation: Factory worker, Place of birth: Prasat commune, Saang district, Kandal province.
According to Sok Phanny, a 34-year-old female who worked with the victim, at 7 am this morning, the victim did not come to work as usual and called a motorbike named Lao Kosal nearby. And to help look at the victim's room, when he arrived at the victim's room, he saw that the door was closed, the window was locked, and the door was not open.
The suspect called the factory workers to help him. When they arrived, they pulled out the window and opened the window key, reached for the door key, and found the victim asleep. The victim had earphones and a cell phone, a charger and a power outlet, so they turned off the power supply, but the victim died and then reported to the authorities for inspection.
In this case, the competent experts examined the scene in Takhmao City, the administrative post, the doctors, and the authorities found that the body was normal, the teeth were bitten, the tongue was hard and there were no noticeable marks. According to the conclusion, according to the conclusion of the examination of the competent experts and doctors, the victim died due to electric shock, causing death.
The body was handed over to the victim's younger brother for a traditional ceremony in his hometown.
