The Phnom Penh Sewerage Development Project aims to filter wastewater before it enters the river through the construction of a wastewater treatment plant at Choeung Ek Lake in Sangkat Choeung Ek, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh. 2,000 meters long, 500 mm in diameter, connected to Boeung Trabek pumping station.
The plant has a capacity of 5,000 cubic meters per day. Construction will begin at the end of 2020, lasting about 32 months. In addition to construction, the project will also provide technical assistance to strengthen the capacity of officials to manage factories, processes and finances.
The Phnom Penh Sewerage Development Project is a complement to the Flood Prevention and Drainage Improvement Project in Phnom Penh, Phase 1, 2, 3 and 4, which was also built with a grant from Japan. .
This project will contribute to the efforts of Phnom Penh Capital Hall as well as the Royal Government of Cambodia, which has clearly responded to the priority needs in the development of wastewater treatment systems that bring protection and improve water quality and sanitation. The environment is in line with the first angle of the fourth rectangle, as stated in the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy document of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
