Kampong Thom Province Disseminates Weed Control on New Rice Effectively to Farmers
(Kampong Thom): Officials and stakeholders in Kampong Thom province are now paying close attention to the agricultural sector in the province, especially rice, in order to promote the growth of farmers' agricultural products.
In order to promote the growth of agricultural products in this province, on the morning of October 31, 2019, the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Thom Province cooperated with a private company to promote a new agricultural product called Zevelo, which is a herbicide on rice. An effective one in the world.
Deputy Director of Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Kan Salon, said in the workshop that Kampong Thom is now a province rich in agriculture, especially rice. There are more than 220,000 hectares of rice in Kampong Thom province, with an average yield of only 3,150 kg per hectare, and this yield is not enough to meet the demand for rice exports.
Ku Rana Sarath, Trade Manager for Thailand and the Asian Peninsula, which distributes Zevelo agricultural products, said that Zevelo agricultural products were imported into Cambodia through Katera, Dow and Dupon, a new and well-known company. The world. The company offers solutions based on agricultural science, improving the lives of people around the world.
"Xavier operates in more than 70 countries around the world, providing a wide range of innovative services for the solution of agricultural problems," he said. "Our company has imported new, environmentally friendly pesticides to help get rid of weeds in the fields, increase yields for farmers, provide quality rice to compete with other countries in the world."
Kurana Sarath added that Cambodia is one of the top 10 countries in the world for rice exports. This is the first time that Zevelo has been inaugurated and launched in Kampong Thom province, because he observed that this is a province with agricultural potential and some people are experiencing weeds that harass agricultural crops. Especially rice.
"So reduce consumer fees, save time to do more work," he said. "On the other hand, even weeds that are resistant to pesticides can still get rid of the farmer. Once he uses them, he will reap the benefits without feeling it."
After Katera selected Kampong Thom as its first target province to promote the quality of veggies, he encouraged farmers to use this pesticide on their rice crops. He hopes that farmers' rice yields will be higher if they use this agricultural product.
