Ministry of Tourism leaders tell Korea that Cambodia wants Korean tourists to have more entertainment and stay longer
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pak Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, informed Mr. Lee Hyuk, Secretary General of the ASEAN-Korea Center that the Kingdom of Cambodia will not forget its friendly relations with Korea, always miss its Korean friends and want Korean tourists to come. Visit Cambodia often and stay longer.
This statement was made by the leaders of the Ministry of Tourism at the opening ceremony of a training workshop on tourism capacity building on digital tourism skills and technology marketing for about 47 tourism professionals and tour operators. From October 30-31, 2019 at Sofitel Angkor Phuket Golf Hotel and Spa Resort, Siem Reap.
Mr. Pak Sokhom said that this training workshop was organized on time in accordance with the recent development of tourism business in the context of the Industrial Revolution 4.0, especially in accordance with the request of tourism experts and tour operators. Develop the ability to use technology to promote and attract tourists, especially Korean tourists to have more entertainment to Cambodia.
In addition to sharing new knowledge and experiences from national and international speakers and professors focusing on the use of digital and technology marketing in the ASEAN-Korea framework, the workshop also shared knowledge on Capacity development on better strategic planning and tourism services to attract tourists, especially Korean tourists, to visit Cambodia more often and for a longer period of time.
In order to build human resources in the tourism sector in response to both quantity and quality, the Secretary of State urged all stakeholders to continue to cooperate and support the development of human resources in the tourism sector, in particular, requested the ASEAN-Korea Center to continue to provide additional training to you. Additional Cambodian tourism skills to be able to provide better services on all tourism services in Cambodia.
In response to the Secretary-General's request, Secretary of State Lee Hyuk expressed his commitment to continue to cooperate and support the training and development of human resources in the tourism sector, especially to strengthen the capacity of tourism professionals, tour guides and tour operators to develop their skills. The provision of services to Korean tourists to Cambodia has been steadily increasing.
It should be noted that for the first eight months of 2019, Cambodia received more than 4.4 million international tourists, an increase of 10.4% compared to the same period in 2018.
It is estimated that by 2020, Cambodia will be able to receive about 7 million international tourists and create nearly 1 million direct jobs.
